/* 科学 (Sains) 内置笔记数据：由 index.html 加载。按SPM给分格式 (F + H、Scheme 得分点、Sample Paper)。改了这个文件，记得把 index.html 里 sci.js?v= 的版本号也改一下，浏览器才会重新下载。 */
const PPTS_SCI={"sains|T4-1":[["SPM Science (1511): Paper Format and Answering Technique","SPM科学(1511)：试卷格式与答题技巧",[["Paper 1 (1511/1): 40 objective questions = 40 marks, 1 hour 15 minutes; answer all. Scientific calculator allowed.","试卷1：40道选择题＝40分，1小时15分钟，全答；可用科学计算器"],["Paper 2 (1511/2) = 80 marks, 2 hours 30 minutes. Section A: 4 structured questions, 20 marks, answer all. Section B: 38 marks, answer all (the number of items differs between sources; check the official specimen paper). Section C: one 10-mark item plus a choice of 12-mark items, 22 marks in total.","试卷2共80分：A部分4题20分（全答）；B部分38分（全答，题数各来源写法不同，以官方样卷为准）；C部分共22分（10分题＋12分题选做）"],["Difficulty ratio Low : Medium : High = 5 : 3 : 2. Content: KSSM Form 4 and Form 5. Constructs: remembering, understanding, applying, analysing; Paper 2 also evaluating and creating.","难度比例 5:3:2；范围：KSSM中四、中五；试卷2也考评价与创造"],["Marking pattern (F + H): 1 mark for each correct point (Fakta) and 1 mark for its explanation (Huraian). For a 6-mark answer, write 3 points + 3 explanations.","给分方式：每个正确要点1分，每个解释1分；6分题写3点＋3个解释"],["Always: underline command words (state, explain, compare, suggest, justify); show calculation steps with units; name the variable type (manipulated / responding / fixed); label diagrams clearly.","答题：圈出指令词；计算写步骤和单位；写清变量类型；图要标示"]],"","Tip: the format is from the official 2021-onwards SPM assessment format; confirm with your teacher for the current year."],["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Hazard: anything that can cause harm or injury (e.g. a corrosive acid, a hot flame).","危害：可能造成伤害的东西"],["Hazard symbol: a warning sign on a container that shows the type of danger of the substance.","危险标志：容器上显示物质危险类型的警告标志"],["Personal protective equipment (PPE): items worn to protect the body from chemicals, heat and injury.","个人防护装备"],["Scientific investigation: a systematic way of finding the answer to a question by carrying out an experiment and collecting data.","科学探究：通过实验收集数据来寻找答案"],["Manipulated variable: the variable that is changed. Responding variable: the variable that is measured. Fixed variable: the variable kept the same.","操纵变量（改变）；响应变量（测量）；固定变量（保持不变）"],["Hypothesis: a statement that predicts the relationship between the manipulated and responding variables.","假设：预测两个变量之间关系的陈述"]],"华文：定义要用关键词，变量三兄弟必背。","Tip: write the definition in one sentence using the keywords above."],["Laboratory Rules","实验室规则",[["Do not enter the laboratory without the teacher's permission; do not run or play.","未经老师允许不得进入实验室；不可奔跑嬉戏"],["Never eat, drink or taste any chemical in the laboratory.","不可在实验室吃喝或尝化学品"],["Read the instructions and labels before starting; follow the teacher's instructions.","开始前阅读说明和标签，听从老师指示"],["Report any accident, spillage or broken apparatus to the teacher at once.","任何意外、溢出或打破仪器须立即告知老师"],["Wash your hands with soap after the experiment and keep the work area clean and tidy.","实验后用肥皂洗手，保持桌面整洁"]],"华文：规则题常问「为什么」，要写出原因。","Tip: rule + reason, e.g. 'do not taste chemicals because they may be toxic'."],["Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)","个人防护装备",[["Safety goggles: to protect the eyes from chemical splashes and flying fragments.","护目镜：保护眼睛免受化学品溅入和碎片"],["Gloves: to protect the hands from corrosive, toxic or hot substances.","手套：保护双手免受腐蚀性、有毒或高温物质"],["Lab coat / apron: to protect the skin and clothes from chemicals.","实验服/围裙：保护皮肤和衣服"],["Mask: to prevent inhaling toxic fumes, gas or dust.","口罩：防止吸入有毒烟雾、气体或粉尘"],["Covered shoes and tied-up hair: to prevent injury from spills, broken glass and fire.","包脚鞋、绑好头发：防止被溢出物、玻璃碎片和火伤害"]],"华文：每件装备都要写「保护哪里 + 防什么」。","Tip: answer as 'to protect X from Y' to get both marks."],["Hazard Symbols","危险标志",[["Toxic: can cause death or serious illness if swallowed, inhaled or absorbed through the skin.","有毒：吞入、吸入或经皮肤吸收可致死或重病"],["Corrosive: destroys living tissue and metals (e.g. concentrated acids and alkalis).","腐蚀性：破坏生物组织和金属"],["Flammable: catches fire easily; keep away from flames and heat.","易燃：容易着火，远离火源"],["Explosive: may explode when heated, shocked or ignited.","爆炸性：受热、撞击或点燃可爆炸"],["Oxidising: helps other substances to burn. Radioactive: gives out harmful radiation.","氧化性：助燃；放射性：释放有害辐射"],["Irritant / harmful: causes skin and eye irritation. Hazardous to the environment: damages living things in water and soil.","刺激/有害；危害环境"]],"华文：看到标志要联想到对应的处理方式。","Tip: state the hazard AND the precaution, e.g. 'flammable: keep away from fire'."],["Safe Use of Apparatus and Chemicals","仪器和化学品的安全使用",[["Heating a test tube: tilt about 45 degrees, point the mouth away from people, move the tube gently in the flame.","加热试管：倾斜约45度，管口远离他人，在火焰中轻轻移动"],["Use a test tube holder or tongs for hot apparatus; allow it to cool before touching.","用试管夹/钳子拿热仪器，冷却后再触碰"],["Do not smell gases or vapours directly; waft the vapour towards the nose with the hand.","不可直接闻气体，用手轻轻扇向鼻子"],["Experiments that release toxic gases or fumes must be done in a fume chamber.","会产生有毒气体的实验要在通风橱内进行"],["Keep flammable substances away from the flame; switch off the Bunsen burner and gas tap after use.","易燃物远离火焰；用后关掉本生灯和气阀"],["Keep electrical equipment dry; do not touch plugs and switches with wet hands.","电器保持干燥，不可湿手碰插头开关"]],"华文：这些做法每一条背后都有原因。","Tip: give the action, then the reason with 'to prevent ...'."],["Handling Accidents","意外处理",[["Chemical on the skin: wash with a lot of running water for several minutes, then inform the teacher.","化学品沾皮肤：用大量流水冲洗，并告知老师"],["Chemical in the eye: rinse immediately with running water (eyewash) for at least 10 minutes and seek medical help.","化学品入眼：立即用流水冲洗至少10分钟并就医"],["Broken glass: do not pick it up with bare hands; use a brush and dustpan and put it in a special container.","玻璃碎：不可徒手捡，用扫帚簸箕并放入专用容器"],["Mercury spill (broken thermometer): do not touch; inform the teacher and let a trained person clean it up.","汞溢出：不可碰，通知老师，由受训人员处理"],["Burn from heat: place the burnt part under running water, then report to the teacher.","烫伤：用流水冲，并通知老师"]],"华文：先处理，再报告老师。","Tip: remember 'plenty of water' and 'inform the teacher' as keywords."],["Disposal of Wastes","废物处理",[["Can go down the sink: small amounts of harmless, water-soluble, diluted substances, flushed with plenty of water.","可倒入水槽：少量无害、可溶、已稀释的物质，并用大量水冲洗"],["Cannot go down the sink: toxic or flammable liquids, organic solvents, heavy-metal solutions, mercury and insoluble solids.","不可倒入水槽：有毒或易燃液体、有机溶剂、重金属溶液、汞、不溶固体"],["Hazardous waste is put in a labelled waste container for proper disposal by a licensed collector.","危险废料放入有标签的容器，交给有执照的机构处理"],["Solid waste such as filter paper and matchsticks goes into the dustbin; broken glass goes into a separate container.","固体废物（滤纸、火柴）丢垃圾桶；碎玻璃另放"],["Reason: wrong disposal pollutes water and soil and harms living things.","原因：错误处理会污染水和土壤，伤害生物"]],"华文：这是重点之一，要会分类。","Tip: give a substance, say whether it can go down the sink, and give the reason."],["Fire Extinguishers","灭火器",[["Water extinguisher: paper, wood and cloth fires. Never use on electrical or oil fires.","水：纸、木、布火灾；不可用于电器和油火"],["Carbon dioxide extinguisher: electrical and flammable-liquid fires; leaves no residue.","二氧化碳：电器和易燃液体火灾，不留残渣"],["Foam extinguisher: flammable liquids such as oil and petrol. Dry powder extinguisher: general, liquid and electrical fires.","泡沫：油类火灾；干粉：一般、液体和电器火灾"],["Fire blanket: smothers a small fire by cutting off the oxygen supply; fire sand is used on metal and oil fires.","灭火毯：隔绝氧气闷熄小火；沙用于金属和油火"],["PASS: Pull the pin, Aim at the base of the fire, Squeeze the handle, Sweep from side to side.","PASS口诀：拔销、瞄准火焰底部、压把手、左右扫射"]],"华文：选对灭火器比操作更重要。","Tip: fire needs fuel, heat and oxygen; extinguishing removes at least one of them."],["Fire Safety Procedure (F + H)","火灾安全程序（F + H）",[["F1 Switch off the gas tap and electrical supply. H: to remove the fuel or the source of the fire so that it does not spread.","F1 关掉气阀和电源。H：切断燃料/火源，防止蔓延"],["F2 Use the correct extinguisher at the base of the flame. H: so that the fuel is covered and the fire is put out.","F2 用正确灭火器对准火焰底部。H：覆盖燃料灭火"],["F3 Do not use water on an oil or electrical fire. H: oil floats and spreads the fire; water conducts electricity and causes electric shock.","F3 油火和电器火不能用水。H：油浮于水面使火蔓延；水导电会触电"],["F4 Evacuate through the nearest exit calmly to the assembly point and inform the teacher. H: to avoid injury and to account for everyone.","F4 冷静从最近出口撤离到集合点。H：避免受伤并清点人数"]],"华文：答案格式：F（做什么）+ H（为什么）。","Tip: every action needs a reason to earn the second mark."],["Steps of a Scientific Investigation","科学探究的步骤",[["1 Identify the problem and make a hypothesis.","1 确定问题并提出假设"],["2 Identify the variables: manipulated, responding and fixed.","2 确定变量"],["3 Plan the experiment: list the apparatus and materials and the procedure.","3 设计实验：仪器、材料和步骤"],["4 Carry out the experiment, collect data and record in a table.","4 进行实验，收集并记录数据"],["5 Analyse and interpret the data (graph, calculation) and make a conclusion.","5 分析数据（图表、计算）并得出结论"],["6 Write a report; repeat the experiment to get reliable results.","6 撰写报告；重复实验以确保可靠"]],"华文：顺序要记牢。","Tip: the conclusion must state whether the hypothesis is accepted or rejected."],["Variables and Hypothesis (F + H)","变量与假设（F + H）",[["F1 Manipulated variable: the one the investigator changes. H: it is the cause that is being tested.","F1 操纵变量：实验者改变的量。H：它是被测试的原因"],["F2 Responding variable: the one that is measured or observed. H: it changes because of the manipulated variable.","F2 响应变量：被测量的量。H：它随操纵变量而变"],["F3 Fixed variable: kept the same in all set-ups. H: to make sure the test is fair, so only the manipulated variable affects the result.","F3 固定变量：保持不变。H：确保公平测试"],["F4 Hypothesis format: the higher/more the (manipulated variable), the higher/lower the (responding variable). H: it predicts the relationship that will be tested.","F4 假设格式：操纵变量越…，响应变量越…"]],"华文：常考：写出变量并说明如何测量。","Tip: name the variable and state how to measure it, e.g. 'time taken, using a stopwatch'."],["Investigation: Effect of Temperature on the Rate of Dissolving of Sugar","探究：温度对糖溶解速率的影响",[["Aim: to study the effect of water temperature on the time taken for sugar to dissolve. (1m)","目的：研究水温对糖溶解所需时间的影响"],["Problem statement: does the temperature of water affect the time taken for sugar to dissolve? (1m) Hypothesis: the higher the temperature of water, the shorter the time taken for sugar to dissolve. (1m)","问题陈述与假设：水温越高，糖溶解时间越短"],["Variables: manipulated = temperature of water; responding = time taken for sugar to dissolve; fixed = mass of sugar, volume of water, stirring. (3m)","变量：操纵=水温；响应=溶解时间；固定=糖的质量、水的体积、搅拌"],["Apparatus and materials: beakers, thermometer, stopwatch, glass rod, measuring cylinder, sugar, hot and cold water. (1m)","仪器和材料"],["Procedure: 1 Pour 100 ml of water at 30 degrees C into a beaker. 2 Add 5 g of sugar and stir; start the stopwatch. 3 Record the time until all the sugar dissolves. 4 Repeat with water at 40, 50, 60 and 70 degrees C. (2m)","步骤：分别在30、40、50、60、70摄氏度的水中溶解糖并计时"],["Observation: the time taken decreases as the temperature increases (tabulate temperature and time). (1m) Conclusion: the higher the temperature, the shorter the time taken; the hypothesis is accepted. (1m)","观察：温度升高，时间缩短；结论：假设被接受"]],"华文：这是示例，格式适用于所有探究题。","Tip: the order is Aim, Problem statement, Hypothesis, Variables, Apparatus, Procedure, Observation, Conclusion."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Laboratory Safety","示例题：试卷2 A部分（实验室安全）",[["(a) [1] State the hazard symbol for a substance that can destroy skin and metals. Scheme: corrosive (1m).","(a)腐蚀性"],["(b) [2] A student spilt concentrated acid on his hand. State two actions that should be taken. Scheme: wash with plenty of running water (1m); inform the teacher (1m).","(b)酸溅手：用大量水冲洗；告知老师"],["(c) [2] Why must a test tube be heated with its mouth pointing away from people? Scheme: the hot liquid may spurt out (1m); and cause injury (1m).","(c)管口不对人：液体会喷出并伤人"],["(d) [2] State the extinguisher for an electrical fire and give a reason. Scheme: carbon dioxide (1m); does not conduct electricity (1m).","(d)电器火灾：二氧化碳灭火器；不导电"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Safety and Investigation (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（安全与探究）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain two safety measures when doing an experiment that produces toxic gas. Scheme: do it in a fume chamber (1m) to prevent inhalation of the gas (1m); wear a mask / goggles (1m) to protect from the gas (1m).","(a)有毒气体实验的两项安全措施"],["(b) [6] A student wants to find out whether the type of liquid affects the time taken for a metal ball to fall to the bottom. Plan an investigation. Scheme: aim / hypothesis (1m); manipulated: type of liquid (1m); responding: time taken to fall (1m); fixed: size of ball, volume of liquid (1m); procedure with stopwatch (1m); tabulate results / conclusion (1m).","(b)设计探究：液体种类对钢球下落时间的影响"],["(c) [KBAT] Suggest how the waste liquid from this experiment should be disposed of if it contains a heavy-metal solution. Scheme: put in a labelled waste container (1m); because it pollutes water if poured down the sink (1m).","(c)含重金属的废液处理：放入有标签容器，不可倒入水槽"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: writing 'to protect the eyes' only for goggles without the hazard. Correct: 'to protect the eyes from chemical splashes'.","错误：只写保护眼睛。正确：要写防什么"],["Mistake: using water to put out an oil or electrical fire. Correct: use carbon dioxide, foam or dry powder.","错误：用水灭油火/电火。正确：二氧化碳/泡沫/干粉"],["Mistake: mixing up manipulated and responding variables. Correct: manipulated = changed; responding = measured.","错误：混淆操纵与响应变量"],["Mistake: pouring all waste down the sink. Correct: toxic, flammable and heavy-metal waste goes into a labelled container.","错误：所有废物都倒水槽"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is the function of safety goggles? J: To protect the eyes from chemical splashes.","问：护目镜的作用？答：保护眼睛免受化学品溅入"],["S: Which hazard symbol shows a substance that destroys skin? J: Corrosive.","问：破坏皮肤的标志？答：腐蚀性"],["S: Which extinguisher is suitable for an electrical fire? J: Carbon dioxide (or dry powder) extinguisher.","问：电器火灾用哪种灭火器？答：二氧化碳（或干粉）灭火器"],["S: Name a waste that must not be poured down the sink. J: Organic solvent (or toxic, flammable or heavy-metal waste).","问：哪种废物不能倒入水槽？答：有机溶剂等"],["S: What is a fixed variable? J: A variable kept the same in all set-ups to make a fair test.","问：什么是固定变量？答：在所有装置中保持不变，确保公平测试"],["S: What do the letters in PASS stand for? J: Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep.","问：PASS代表？答：拔销、瞄准、压把手、扫射"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-2":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["First aid: the immediate help given to a casualty before professional medical help arrives.","急救：专业医护人员到达前，对伤病者给予的即时救助"],["First aider: a person trained to give first aid.","急救员：受过急救训练的人"],["Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR): a combination of chest compressions and rescue breaths to keep blood and oxygen flowing when the heart and breathing have stopped.","心肺复苏（CPR）：胸外按压加人工呼吸，在心跳呼吸停止时维持血液和氧气循环"],["Heimlich manoeuvre: abdominal thrusts used to remove an object that blocks the airway of a choking person.","海姆立克急救法：用腹部冲击排出阻塞气道的异物"],["Casualty: a person who is injured or suddenly ill. Fracture: a broken or cracked bone.","伤病者；骨折：骨头折断或裂开"],["Automated external defibrillator (AED): a device that gives an electric shock to restore a normal heart rhythm.","自动体外除颤器（AED）：电击使心律恢复正常的仪器"]],"","Tip: define first aid with the keywords 'immediate help' and 'before medical help arrives'."],["Aims of First Aid","急救的目的",[["Preserve life: keep the casualty alive (clear the airway, restore breathing and circulation, stop heavy bleeding).","保全生命：保持气道通畅、恢复呼吸与循环、止血"],["Prevent the condition from becoming worse: e.g. immobilise a fracture, do not move the casualty unnecessarily.","防止病情恶化：如固定骨折，不随意搬动"],["Promote recovery: reduce pain, comfort and reassure the casualty, protect the wound from infection.","促进康复：减轻痛苦、安抚伤者、保护伤口防感染"],["A first aider must keep calm, make sure the area is safe for himself first, and never give food or drink to a seriously injured person.","急救员要冷静，先确保自身安全，严重伤者不可给饮食"]],"","Tip: remember the three aims as preserve life, prevent worsening, promote recovery."],["Primary Survey: Danger, Response, Airway, Breathing, Circulation","初步检查：危险、反应、气道、呼吸、循环",[["Danger: check that the surroundings are safe for you, the casualty and bystanders (traffic, fire, electric wire).","危险：先确认现场对自己、伤者和旁人安全"],["Response: tap the shoulders and shout ‘Are you okay?’. If there is no response, shout for help and call for an ambulance.","反应：轻拍双肩并呼喊；无反应则呼救并叫救护车"],["Airway: tilt the head back and lift the chin to open the airway.","气道：仰头抬颏打开气道"],["Breathing: look at the chest rise, listen and feel for breath for not more than 10 seconds.","呼吸：看胸部起伏、听、感觉气流，不超过10秒"],["Circulation: check for a pulse and for severe bleeding. No normal breathing means start CPR.","循环：检查脉搏和严重出血；没有正常呼吸则开始CPR"]],"","Tip: write the steps in the correct order: danger, response, airway, breathing, circulation."],["Calling for Emergency Help","呼叫紧急援助",[["Call 999 (police, ambulance, fire) or 112 from a mobile phone.","拨打999或手机112"],["Give the exact location of the accident and a landmark if possible.","说明准确地点及地标"],["Tell what happened, the number of casualties and their condition (conscious? breathing?).","说明发生何事、伤者人数及情况"],["Give your name and phone number and do not hang up until told to; follow the operator's advice.","报上姓名电话，听从接线员指示，不要先挂断"],["Ask someone to bring an AED if there is one nearby.","请旁人去取附近的AED"]],"","Tip: location, what happened, number of casualties are the key points."],["CPR for an Adult: Steps","成人CPR步骤",[["CPR is done when the casualty is unresponsive and not breathing, or not breathing normally (only gasping).","无反应且无呼吸或仅喘息时进行CPR"],["Place the casualty on a firm, flat surface, on the back. Kneel beside the chest.","让伤者平躺在硬而平的表面"],["Place the heel of one hand at the centre of the chest (lower half of the breastbone); put the other hand on top and interlock the fingers; arms straight.","掌根放在胸部中央（胸骨下半部），双手交叠，手臂伸直"],["Compress at a depth of about 5–6 cm at a rate of 100–120 compressions per minute; allow the chest to rise fully after each compression.","按压深约5–6厘米，每分钟100–120次，每次让胸廓完全回弹"],["After 30 compressions, open the airway (head tilt, chin lift), pinch the nose and give 2 rescue breaths, each about 1 second until the chest rises.","30次按压后，打开气道、捏鼻，吹2口气，每口约1秒，见胸部起伏"],["Continue 30 : 2 until the casualty responds, an AED arrives or medical help takes over.","持续30:2直到伤者恢复、AED到达或医护接手"]],"","Tip: write 30 compressions : 2 breaths, 100–120 per minute, 5–6 cm deep, centre of the chest."],["CPR (F + H)","CPR要点（事实+解释）",[["F1 Place the hands at the centre of the chest. H: the compressions squeeze the heart between the breastbone and the spine to pump blood.","F1 手放胸部中央。H：按压使心脏被挤压而泵血"],["F2 Compress at 100–120 per minute and 5–6 cm deep. H: to keep enough blood flowing to the brain and other organs.","F2 速度深度要足够。H：保证脑和器官有足够血液"],["F3 Allow the chest to recoil fully after each compression. H: so that the heart can refill with blood.","F3 每次让胸廓回弹。H：让心脏重新充血"],["F4 Tilt the head back and lift the chin before giving breaths. H: to open the airway by lifting the tongue away from the back of the throat.","F4 仰头抬颏。H：使舌头离开咽后壁，打开气道"],["F5 Use an AED as soon as it arrives and follow its voice instructions. H: the shock can restore a normal heartbeat.","F5 AED一到立即使用。H：电击可恢复正常心律"]],"","Tip: each action (F) must be followed by its reason (H) to score both marks."],["CPR for Children and Infants; Recovery Position","儿童和婴儿CPR；复原姿势",[["Child (about 1 year to puberty): compress with one or two hands to about one-third of the depth of the chest, still 30 : 2 for one rescuer.","儿童：用单手或双手按压至胸厚约三分之一，单人施救仍为30:2"],["Infant (under 1 year): use two fingers on the centre of the chest, compress about one-third of the chest depth; give gentle puffs covering the mouth and nose.","婴儿：用两指按压胸部中央，深约三分之一；轻吹气，口鼻同时覆盖"],["Child and infant: the compression rate is also 100–120 per minute; use gentler force than for an adult.","儿童婴儿：频率同样100–120次，力度比成人轻"],["Unconscious casualty who is breathing normally: put in the recovery position (on the side, head tilted back, top leg bent).","无意识但有正常呼吸：置于复原姿势（侧卧、头后仰、上腿弯曲）"],["Reason: the tongue does not block the airway and vomit or fluid can drain out, preventing choking.","原因：舌头不堵气道，呕吐物可流出，防止窒息"]],"","Tip: for infants write 'two fingers'; for adults 'two hands'."],["Choking and the Heimlich Manoeuvre: Steps","窒息与海姆立克急救法：步骤",[["Choking: a foreign object blocks the airway. Signs: cannot speak, cough or breathe, hands on the throat, face turns blue.","窒息：异物阻塞气道；表现：不能说话、咳嗽、呼吸，手抓喉咙，脸发青"],["Mild blockage: encourage the person to keep coughing.","轻度阻塞：鼓励继续咳嗽"],["Severe blockage in a conscious adult: stand behind the person and wrap both arms around the waist.","严重阻塞（清醒成人）：站其身后，双臂环抱腰部"],["Make a fist with one hand and place it just above the navel and below the rib cage; hold the fist with the other hand.","一手握拳，置于肚脐上方、肋骨下方，另一手握住拳头"],["Give quick upward and inward thrusts until the object is expelled or the person becomes unconscious.","快速向内向上冲击，直到异物排出或伤者失去意识"],["If unconscious: lay the person down, call for help and start CPR.","若昏迷：平放、呼救并开始CPR"]],"","Tip: fist above the navel, below the ribs; thrusts are inward and upward."],["Heimlich Manoeuvre (F + H)","海姆立克法要点（事实+解释）",[["F1 Thrusts are given on the abdomen, above the navel. H: this pushes the diaphragm upward and forces air out of the lungs to push the object out.","F1 冲击腹部肚脐上方。H：推高膈肌，肺内气体冲出把异物排出"],["F2 Do not do it on a pregnant woman or an infant in the usual way; give chest thrusts to a pregnant woman and back blows plus chest thrusts to an infant. H: abdominal thrusts may injure the unborn baby or the infant's organs.","F2 孕妇改胸部冲击，婴儿用拍背加胸部按压。H：腹部冲击可能伤胎儿或婴儿内脏"],["F3 Stop and start CPR if the person becomes unconscious. H: the person is no longer able to cough and may stop breathing.","F3 失去意识就改做CPR。H：无法咳嗽，可能停止呼吸"],["F4 Do not try to pull the object out with fingers blindly. H: it may push the object deeper into the airway.","F4 不要盲目用手指挖。H：可能把异物推得更深"]],"","Tip: explain the effect on the diaphragm and the air pressure in the lungs."],["Bleeding","出血",[["Severe bleeding can cause shock and death because of loss of blood.","大量出血可导致休克甚至死亡"],["Step 1: wear gloves if available; press directly on the wound with a clean cloth or sterile dressing.","步骤1：戴手套，用干净布或无菌敷料直接按压伤口"],["Step 2: raise the injured limb higher than the heart (if no fracture), and lay the casualty down.","步骤2：抬高伤肢高于心脏（无骨折时），让伤者躺下"],["Step 3: bandage firmly over the dressing; if blood soaks through, add more dressing on top and do not remove the first one.","步骤3：用绷带包扎；血渗出则在上面加敷料，不要拿掉原有的"],["Seek medical help. Do not wash a deep wound or remove an embedded object; press around it.","寻求医疗协助；深伤口不要冲洗，嵌入物不可拔出"]],"","Tip: direct pressure + raise the limb + bandage; give the reason, to slow down blood flow and clot the blood."],["Burns and Scalds","烧伤与烫伤",[["Burn: damage to the skin caused by dry heat, fire, chemicals or electricity. Scald: caused by hot liquid or steam.","烧伤：干热、火、化学品或电；烫伤：热液体或蒸汽"],["Cool the burn under cool running water for at least 10 minutes. Reason: to reduce the heat, pain and damage to the skin.","用流动冷水冲至少10分钟；减热、减痛、减少损伤"],["Remove rings, watches and tight clothing near the burn before swelling starts; do not pull off cloth stuck to the skin.","肿胀前取下戒指手表和紧身衣物；粘住皮肤的衣物不要硬扯"],["Cover loosely with a clean non-stick dressing or cling film. Do not burst the blisters.","用干净不粘敷料或保鲜膜轻轻覆盖；不要弄破水泡"],["Do not apply ice, butter, oil, toothpaste or ointment. Reason: they trap heat and may cause infection. Seek medical help for large or deep burns.","不可涂冰、牛油、油、牙膏、药膏；会积热并引起感染；大面积或深度烧伤须就医"]],"","Tip: running water for at least 10 minutes is the key mark; state what NOT to apply."],["Fractures","骨折",[["Signs: pain, swelling, bruising, deformed limb, unable to move the part normally.","表现：疼痛、肿胀、瘀青、变形、无法正常活动"],["Do not move the casualty unless there is danger; keep the injured part still.","除非有危险，否则不要移动伤者；保持伤处不动"],["Immobilise the fracture with a splint (e.g. a board or rolled newspaper) and bandage above and below the fracture; arm injuries can be supported with a sling.","用夹板（木板、卷起的报纸）固定，在骨折处上下绑扎；手臂可用三角巾悬吊"],["Open fracture (bone through the skin): cover the wound with a clean dressing and control bleeding; do not push the bone back.","开放性骨折：用干净敷料覆盖止血；不可把骨头推回"],["Reason for splinting: to prevent further damage to blood vessels, nerves and muscles and to reduce pain. Seek medical help.","固定的原因：避免血管神经肌肉进一步受损并减痛；然后就医"]],"","Tip: immobilise (splint) and the reason, to prevent further injury."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: First Aid","示例题：试卷2 A部分（急救）",[["(a) [1] State the ratio of chest compressions to rescue breaths in adult CPR. Scheme: 30 : 2 (1m).","(a)成人CPR按压与吹气比"],["(b) [2] State where the hands are placed during CPR and the depth of the compression. Scheme: centre of the chest / lower half of the breastbone (1m); about 5–6 cm (1m).","(b)手位置及按压深度"],["(c) [2] Explain why the casualty's head is tilted back before giving rescue breaths. Scheme: to open the airway (1m); the tongue is lifted away from the back of the throat (1m).","(c)为何仰头"],["(d) [2] A girl suffers a scald on her arm. State the first aid. Scheme: cool under running water for at least 10 minutes (1m); cover with a clean non-stick dressing (1m).","(d)烫伤急救"],["(e) [1] State the purpose of a splint. Scheme: to immobilise the fractured bone (1m).","(e)夹板的作用"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Emergency Situations (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（紧急情况）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [6] A man collapses in a shopping mall. He is unresponsive and not breathing. Describe the actions of a first aider. Scheme: check danger (1m); check response by tapping and shouting (1m); call 999 / 112 and ask for an AED (1m); open the airway and check breathing (1m); CPR at the centre of the chest, 30 compressions : 2 breaths (1m); continue until help arrives or use the AED (1m).","(a)商场昏倒男子：急救员的行动"],["(b) [2] Explain why the compressions must be done on a firm, flat surface. Scheme: so that the force can compress the chest (1m) and pump blood from the heart (1m).","(b)为何在硬平面上按压"],["(c) [KBAT, 2] A child chokes on a sweet during lunch and cannot cough or speak. Justify the use of the Heimlich manoeuvre. Scheme: the airway is completely blocked (1m); thrusts increase air pressure in the lungs to expel the object (1m).","(c)KBAT：证明海姆立克法的必要"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: writing 15 : 2 for adult CPR. Correct: 30 compressions : 2 breaths.","错误：成人写15:2。正确：30:2"],["Mistake: using the Heimlich manoeuvre on an unconscious person. Correct: start CPR instead.","错误：对昏迷者用海姆立克法。正确：改做CPR"],["Mistake: putting butter, toothpaste or ice on a burn. Correct: cool with running water for at least 10 minutes.","错误：烧伤涂牛油牙膏或冰。正确：流水冲10分钟以上"],["Mistake: forgetting to call for emergency help or to check the danger first. Correct: check the danger, then call 999 / 112.","错误：忘记先查危险和呼救。正确：先查危险再拨999/112"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is the adult CPR ratio? J: 30 compressions : 2 rescue breaths.","问：成人CPR比例？答：30次按压:2次吹气"],["S: Where are the hands placed in CPR? J: At the centre of the chest (lower half of the breastbone).","问：CPR手放哪里？答：胸部中央（胸骨下半部）"],["S: What is the Heimlich manoeuvre used for? J: To remove an object blocking the airway of a choking person.","问：海姆立克法用途？答：排出阻塞气道的异物"],["S: How long should a burn be cooled under running water? J: At least 10 minutes.","问：烧伤要冲水多久？答：至少10分钟"],["S: Why is a fractured limb splinted? J: To immobilise it and prevent further injury.","问：为何给骨折固定？答：固定伤处，防止进一步受伤"],["S: What is the emergency number from a mobile phone? J: 999 or 112.","问：手机紧急号码？答：999或112"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-3":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Body temperature: the degree of hotness or coldness of the body; measured in degrees Celsius (°C) with a clinical thermometer.","体温：身体的冷热程度，用体温计测量，单位°C"],["Pulse rate: the number of pulses (heartbeats felt in an artery) per minute; unit: beats per minute.","脉搏率：每分钟脉搏次数（动脉感到的心跳），单位：次/分钟"],["Blood pressure: the force of the blood pushing against the walls of the arteries; measured in mmHg.","血压：血液对动脉壁的压力，单位mmHg"],["Systolic pressure: the pressure when the heart contracts. Diastolic pressure: the pressure when the heart relaxes.","收缩压：心脏收缩时的压力；舒张压：心脏舒张时的压力"],["Body mass index (BMI): a value calculated from the mass and height of a person to show whether the body mass is healthy.","身体质量指数（BMI）：由体重和身高计算，显示体重是否健康"],["Hypertension: blood pressure that stays higher than the normal level. Health parameter: a measurement that shows the state of health of the body.","高血压：血压持续高于正常；健康参数：显示身体健康状况的测量值"]],"","Tip: always include the unit when stating a health parameter."],["Measuring Body Temperature","测量体温",[["Instrument: clinical thermometer (digital or mercury-free), infrared (ear or forehead) thermometer.","仪器：体温计（电子式）、红外线耳温/额温枪"],["Places: under the tongue (mouth), armpit, ear, forehead.","部位：舌下、腋下、耳、额头"],["Normal body temperature is about 37 °C (range about 36.1–37.2 °C); a temperature above the normal range suggests a fever, below suggests low body temperature.","正常体温约37°C（约36.1–37.2°C）；高于范围表示发烧"],["Digital thermometer: place the tip under the tongue or in the armpit, wait for the beep, then read the display.","电子体温计：尖端放舌下或腋下，等待哔声后读数"],["Clean the thermometer with alcohol or soapy water before and after use.","使用前后用酒精或肥皂水清洁"]],"","Tip: state the place, the normal value with °C and what a higher value means."],["Body Temperature: Precautions (F + H)","体温测量注意事项（事实+解释）",[["F1 Do not measure right after exercise, a hot bath or a hot or cold drink. H: these change the temperature of the body surface or mouth, so the reading is not accurate.","F1 运动、热水澡或冷热饮后不要测。H：影响体表或口腔温度，读数不准"],["F2 Make sure the tip of the thermometer touches the skin or the tissue in the mouth or armpit. H: so that the thermometer reads the body temperature, not the surrounding temperature.","F2 尖端要接触皮肤或组织。H：读到体温而非环境温度"],["F3 Wait until the reading is stable (the beep). H: the thermometer needs time to reach the body temperature.","F3 等读数稳定（哔声）。H：温度计需要时间达到体温"],["F4 Clean the thermometer before sharing. H: to prevent the spread of germs.","F4 共用前清洁。H：防止病菌传播"]],"","Tip: precaution (F) + reason (H) = 2 marks."],["Measuring Pulse Rate","测量脉搏率",[["Pulse points: wrist (radial artery), neck (carotid artery) and temple.","脉搏位置：手腕（桡动脉）、颈部（颈动脉）、太阳穴"],["Place the index and middle fingers (not the thumb) lightly on the pulse point. Reason: the thumb has its own pulse that may be mistaken for the casualty's pulse.","用食指和中指（不用拇指）轻按；因为拇指自己有脉搏，会混淆"],["Count the number of pulses for 1 minute, or for 15 seconds and multiply by 4 (30 seconds × 2).","数1分钟，或数15秒再乘4（30秒乘2）"],["Normal resting pulse rate of an adult: about 60–100 beats per minute.","成人静息脉搏约60–100次/分钟"],["Pulse rate increases during exercise, fear and excitement because the body needs more oxygen and energy; it is lower during rest and sleep.","运动、恐惧、兴奋时脉搏加快（身体需要更多氧和能量）；休息睡眠时较低"]],"","Tip: write ‘two fingers’ and the unit ‘beats per minute’."],["Pulse Rate: Worked Example","脉搏率：计算示例",[["Formula: pulse rate (beats per minute) = number of pulses counted ÷ time (min), or pulses in 15 s × 4.","公式：脉搏率=次数÷时间（分钟），或15秒次数×4"],["Example 1: 18 pulses counted in 15 seconds. Pulse rate = 18 × 4 = 72 beats per minute (1m for substitution, 1m for answer with unit).","例1：15秒18次；18×4=72次/分钟"],["Example 2: 40 pulses counted in 30 seconds. Pulse rate = 40 × 2 = 80 beats per minute.","例2：30秒40次；40×2=80次/分钟"],["Interpretation: both values are within the normal resting range of 60–100 beats per minute.","判断：都在正常静息范围60–100内"]],"","Tip: show the working and write the unit beats per minute."],["Measuring Blood Pressure","测量血压",[["Instrument: sphygmomanometer (digital or manual with a stethoscope).","仪器：血压计（电子式或手动加听诊器）"],["The person sits down, rests for about 5 minutes, keeps the back supported and the feet flat on the floor.","坐下休息约5分钟，背靠椅，双脚平放"],["Wrap the cuff on the bare upper arm at the same level as the heart; do not talk or move during the measurement.","袖带绑在裸露上臂，与心脏同高；测量时不说话不动"],["Reading is written as systolic / diastolic, e.g. 120/80 mmHg.","读数写成收缩压/舒张压，如120/80 mmHg"],["Normal blood pressure for an adult is about 120/80 mmHg.","成人正常血压约120/80 mmHg"]],"","Tip: write both values with the unit mmHg."],["Interpreting Blood Pressure","血压的判读",[["Hypertension (high blood pressure): a reading of 140/90 mmHg or higher on repeated measurements.","高血压：多次测量达到140/90 mmHg或以上"],["Hypotension (low blood pressure): a reading below about 90/60 mmHg; may cause dizziness and fainting.","低血压：约低于90/60 mmHg；可能头晕昏厥"],["Causes of hypertension: too much salt and fatty food, lack of exercise, obesity, smoking, stress.","高血压原因：盐和油腻太多、缺乏运动、肥胖、吸烟、压力"],["Risks of hypertension: heart disease, stroke and kidney failure.","高血压的风险：心脏病、中风、肾衰竭"]],"","Tip: link hypertension to heart disease and stroke."],["Blood Pressure (F + H)","血压要点（事实+解释）",[["F1 Rest for about 5 minutes before the measurement. H: exercise and anxiety raise blood pressure, so the reading would be higher than the true value.","F1 先休息约5分钟。H：运动和紧张使血压升高，读数偏高"],["F2 The cuff is placed at the same level as the heart. H: the height of the arm changes the blood pressure reading.","F2 袖带与心脏同高。H：手臂高度会影响读数"],["F3 Take two or three readings and find the average. H: to get a more accurate and reliable value.","F3 测2–3次取平均。H：更准确可靠"],["F4 Reduce salt and fat in the diet and exercise regularly. H: to lower blood pressure and the risk of heart disease.","F4 少盐少油、规律运动。H：降血压，减少心脏病风险"]],"","Tip: precaution (F) + effect on the reading (H)."],["Body Mass Index (BMI): Formula and Categories","BMI：公式与分类",[["Formula: BMI = mass (kg) ÷ height² (m²), written as \\(\\text{BMI} = \\dfrac{\\text{mass (kg)}}{\\text{height (m)}^2}\\).","公式：BMI=体重(kg)÷身高²(m²)"],["Height must be changed to metres first: 160 cm = 1.60 m.","身高要先换成米：160厘米=1.60米"],["Below 18.5: underweight. 18.5–24.9: normal (healthy). 25.0–29.9: overweight. 30.0 and above: obese.","低于18.5偏瘦；18.5–24.9正常；25.0–29.9过重；30.0及以上肥胖"],["BMI has no unit in the final answer (kg m⁻² may be written).","BMI一般不写单位（可写kg m⁻²）"],["Limitation: BMI does not show the amount of fat or muscle; an athlete with much muscle may have a high BMI.","局限：BMI不显示脂肪或肌肉多少；肌肉发达的运动员BMI可能偏高"]],"","Tip: convert cm to m before squaring."],["BMI: Worked Examples","BMI：计算示例",[["Example 1: mass 70 kg, height 1.75 m. BMI = 70 ÷ (1.75)² = 70 ÷ 3.0625 = 22.9 (1m formula, 1m substitution, 1m answer). Category: normal.","例1：70÷3.0625=22.9，正常"],["Example 2: mass 52 kg, height 160 cm = 1.60 m. BMI = 52 ÷ (1.60)² = 52 ÷ 2.56 = 20.3. Category: normal.","例2：160厘米=1.60米；52÷2.56=20.3，正常"],["Example 3: mass 65 kg, height 150 cm = 1.50 m. BMI = 65 ÷ 2.25 = 28.9. Category: overweight.","例3：65÷2.25=28.9，过重"],["Example 4: the mass that gives a BMI of 24.9 for a height of 1.60 m: mass = BMI × height² = 24.9 × 2.56 = 63.7 kg (the highest normal mass).","例4：BMI为24.9、身高1.60米：质量=24.9×2.56=63.7 kg（正常的最高体重）"]],"","Tip: show formula, substitution and answer; round to one decimal place."],["Healthy Lifestyle Based on Health Parameters (F + H)","根据健康参数的健康生活方式（事实+解释）",[["F1 A person with a high BMI should reduce high-fat and high-sugar food and exercise regularly. H: to reduce body mass and the risk of diabetes, heart disease and hypertension.","F1 BMI高者要少油少糖并运动。H：降体重，减少糖尿病、心脏病、高血压风险"],["F2 An underweight person should eat a balanced diet with enough energy and protein. H: to gain mass and strengthen the body.","F2 过瘦者要均衡饮食，足够能量和蛋白质。H：增重强身"],["F3 Measure the health parameters regularly. H: abnormal values give early warning so that action can be taken.","F3 定期测量。H：异常值提供早期警告"],["F4 Do not smoke and manage stress. H: smoking and stress raise blood pressure and pulse rate.","F4 不吸烟、减压。H：吸烟和压力使血压和脉搏上升"]],"","Tip: advice + how it improves health."],["Investigation: Effect of Exercise on Pulse Rate","探究：运动对脉搏率的影响",[["Aim: to study the effect of the duration of exercise on pulse rate. Problem statement: does the duration of exercise affect the pulse rate? (1m)","目的：研究运动时间对脉搏率的影响"],["Hypothesis: the longer the duration of exercise, the higher the pulse rate. (1m)","假设：运动时间越长，脉搏率越高"],["Variables: manipulated: duration of exercise; responding: pulse rate; fixed: type of exercise, same student, time of day. (3m)","变量：操纵：运动时间；响应：脉搏率；固定：运动种类、同一学生、时间"],["Apparatus: stopwatch. Activity: running on the spot or step-ups.","仪器：秒表；活动：原地跑或踏台阶"],["Procedure: (1) sit and rest for 5 minutes, then count the resting pulse for 1 minute; (2) run on the spot for 1 minute and count the pulse immediately; (3) rest until the pulse returns to normal; (4) repeat with 2 and 3 minutes of exercise; tabulate. (3m)","步骤：静坐5分钟量静息脉搏；运动1分钟后立即量；恢复；再做2、3分钟；记录成表"],["Observation: the pulse rate rises as the duration of exercise increases. Conclusion: hypothesis is accepted; the longer the exercise, the higher the pulse rate. (2m)","观察：运动时间越长脉搏率越高；结论：假设成立"]],"","Tip: manipulated = what you change, responding = what you measure."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Health Parameters","示例题：试卷2 A部分（健康参数）",[["(a) [1] Name the instrument used to measure blood pressure. Scheme: sphygmomanometer (1m).","(a)测血压的仪器"],["(b) [2] A student has a mass of 54 kg and a height of 1.50 m. Calculate the BMI. Scheme: 54 ÷ (1.50)² (1m); 24.0 (1m).","(b)计算BMI：54÷2.25=24.0"],["(c) [1] State the category of the BMI in (b). Scheme: normal (1m).","(c)BMI类别：正常"],["(d) [2] State two precautions when measuring the pulse rate at the wrist. Scheme: use the index and middle fingers (1m); count for 1 minute / the person must be at rest (1m).","(d)测脉搏的两项注意事项"],["(e) [1] State the unit of blood pressure. Scheme: mmHg (1m).","(e)血压单位"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Health Parameters (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（健康参数）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain two precautions to get an accurate reading of blood pressure. Scheme: rest 5 minutes (1m) because exercise raises blood pressure (1m); cuff at heart level (1m) because arm height changes the reading (1m).","(a)准确测血压的两项注意事项"],["(b) [KBAT, 4] Mr Ali is 1.70 m tall with a mass of 95 kg and a blood pressure of 150/95 mmHg. BMI = 95 ÷ 2.89 = 32.9 (1m); obese (1m); he has hypertension (1m); suggest he reduce salt, fat and sugar and exercise regularly to reduce the risk of heart disease and stroke (1m).","(b)KBAT：BMI32.9肥胖，高血压；建议少盐油糖并运动"],["(c) [KBAT, 2] Justify why a rugby player with a high BMI may still be healthy. Scheme: BMI does not show the body fat (1m); the player has a large muscle mass which is heavy (1m).","(c)KBAT：为何BMI高的运动员仍可能健康"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: using height in cm in the BMI formula. Correct: change to metres, then square.","错误：用厘米算BMI。正确：先换成米再平方"],["Mistake: using the thumb to feel the pulse. Correct: use the index and middle fingers.","错误：用拇指摸脉搏。正确：用食指和中指"],["Mistake: forgetting the units (beats per minute, mmHg, °C). Correct: always write the unit.","错误：漏写单位。正确：必写单位"],["Mistake: writing diastolic over systolic. Correct: systolic / diastolic, e.g. 120/80.","错误：把舒张压写在前面。正确：收缩压/舒张压"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is the formula of BMI? J: BMI = mass (kg) ÷ height² (m²).","问：BMI公式？答：体重(kg)÷身高²(m²)"],["S: Which instrument measures blood pressure? J: Sphygmomanometer.","问：测血压的仪器？答：血压计"],["S: What does a BMI of 27 mean? J: Overweight.","问：BMI为27代表？答：过重"],["S: What is the normal resting pulse rate of an adult? J: About 60–100 beats per minute.","问：成人正常静息脉搏？答：约60–100次/分钟"],["S: Why is the pulse rate counted for 15 seconds then multiplied by 4? J: To get the number of beats in 1 minute.","问：为何数15秒再乘4？答：得到每分钟的次数"],["S: State one effect of hypertension on health. J: Increases the risk of heart disease or stroke.","问：高血压的一项影响？答：增加心脏病或中风风险"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-4":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Green technology: the use of technology that conserves natural resources, reduces pollution and does not harm the environment, so that future generations can also meet their needs.","绿色科技：节约自然资源、减少污染、不损害环境，使后代也能满足需求的科技"],["Sustainable development: development that meets the needs of the present without harming the ability of future generations to meet their needs.","可持续发展：满足当代需求而不损害后代满足其需求的能力"],["Renewable energy: energy from sources that are replaced naturally and will not run out, e.g. solar, wind, hydro, biomass.","可再生能源：自然补充、不会耗尽的能源"],["Non-renewable energy: energy from sources that cannot be replaced in a short time, e.g. coal, petroleum and natural gas (fossil fuels).","不可再生能源：短时间内无法补充，如煤、石油、天然气"],["Energy efficiency: using less energy to do the same work. Carbon footprint: the total amount of greenhouse gases released by an activity, a person or a product.","能源效率：用较少能量做同样的功；碳足迹：活动、个人或产品释放的温室气体总量"],["Biodegradable: can be broken down by microorganisms into harmless substances.","可生物降解：可被微生物分解成无害物质"]],"","Tip: define green technology with ‘conserve resources’, ‘reduce pollution’ and ‘future generations’."],["Importance of Green Technology","绿色科技的重要性",[["Reduces pollution of air, water and soil, and reduces the emission of greenhouse gases that cause global warming.","减少空气、水、土壤污染和造成全球变暖的温室气体"],["Conserves natural resources and energy so that they last longer.","节约自然资源和能源，使之更持久"],["Four pillars of the National Green Technology Policy: energy, environment, economy and society.","国家绿色科技政策四大支柱：能源、环境、经济、社会"],["Four main sectors of green technology in this chapter: energy, water and waste management, agriculture and forestry, transportation.","本章四大领域：能源、水和废物管理、农业与林业、交通"],["Everyone, including individuals, industry and government, has a role in practising green technology.","个人、企业和政府都有责任实践绿色科技"]],"","Tip: link green technology to reduced pollution and conservation of resources."],["Energy Sector: Issues","能源领域：问题",[["Burning fossil fuels in power stations and vehicles releases carbon dioxide, which increases the greenhouse effect and causes global warming.","燃烧化石燃料释放CO₂，加剧温室效应，导致全球变暖"],["It also releases sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides, which cause acid rain, and particles that cause haze.","也释放SO₂和氮氧化物（酸雨）及微粒（烟霾）"],["Fossil fuels are non-renewable; they will be used up if used too fast.","化石燃料不可再生，用得太快会耗尽"],["Demand for electricity keeps increasing with population and industrial growth.","人口与工业增长使电力需求不断增加"]],"","Tip: name the pollutant and the effect, e.g. SO₂ causes acid rain."],["Energy Sector: Solutions (F + H)","能源领域：解决方法（事实+解释）",[["F1 Use solar energy (solar panels, photovoltaic cells). H: sunlight is renewable and does not release carbon dioxide during operation.","F1 太阳能（光伏板）。H：可再生，运行时不排放CO₂"],["F2 Use hydro, wind or biomass / biogas energy. H: they are renewable and produce less pollution than fossil fuels.","F2 水力、风力、生物质/沼气。H：可再生且污染少"],["F3 Use energy-saving appliances with a high energy efficiency label, such as LED lamps. H: they use less electricity for the same work, so less fuel is burnt.","F3 用节能标签电器，如LED灯。H：同样功用耗电少，燃料少烧"],["F4 Use a smart switch off and good insulation. H: avoids wasting energy and reduces the electricity bill.","F4 随手关电、做好隔热。H：避免浪费，省电费"],["Socio-scientific issues: high installation cost, large land area for solar farms, dams may flood forests, and supply depends on the weather.","社会科学议题：安装成本高、占地大、水坝淹没森林、供电依赖天气"]],"","Tip: for evaluation, state both an advantage and a limitation."],["Energy Efficiency: Worked Example","能源效率：计算示例",[["Formula: energy used (kWh) = power (kW) × time (h); power in watts ÷ 1000 gives kW.","公式：能量(kWh)=功率(kW)×时间(h)；瓦特÷1000=千瓦"],["A filament bulb of 60 W is switched on for 5 hours: energy = 0.060 kW × 5 h = 0.30 kWh.","60 W灯泡开5小时：0.060×5=0.30 kWh"],["An LED lamp of 9 W gives similar brightness for 5 hours: energy = 0.009 kW × 5 h = 0.045 kWh.","9 W LED开5小时：0.009×5=0.045 kWh"],["Energy saved = 0.30 − 0.045 = 0.255 kWh each time. Conclusion: the LED lamp is more energy efficient (1m).","节省0.30−0.045=0.255 kWh；LED更节能"]],"","Tip: write the unit kWh and compare using ‘lower than’."],["Water and Waste Management: Issues","水和废物管理：问题",[["Solid waste is dumped in landfills; the rotting waste releases methane (a greenhouse gas) and a liquid called leachate that pollutes water.","固体废物填埋；腐烂释放甲烷（温室气体）和渗滤液污染水源"],["Open burning of waste releases smoke and toxic gases that pollute the air.","露天焚烧释放烟和有毒气体污染空气"],["Wastewater from homes, factories and farms contains detergent, oil, chemicals and fertiliser; if released untreated it pollutes rivers and kills aquatic life.","家庭、工厂、农场废水含洗涤剂、油、化学品、肥料；未处理排放会污染河流，杀死水生生物"],["Clean water is limited; water must be saved and reused.","洁净水有限，要节约和再利用"]],"","Tip: leachate pollutes water; methane causes global warming."],["Water and Waste Management: Solutions (F + H)","水和废物管理：解决方法（事实+解释）",[["F1 Practise the 3R: reduce, reuse and recycle. H: this lowers the amount of waste sent to landfills and saves resources.","F1 3R：减少、再用、回收。H：减少填埋量，节约资源"],["F2 Separate waste at source. H: so that recyclable and organic waste can be processed properly.","F2 源头分类。H：可回收和有机废物才能妥善处理"],["F3 Compost organic waste (food, leaves). H: it is changed by microorganisms into compost that is used as a natural fertiliser.","F3 有机废物堆肥。H：微生物转变为天然肥料"],["F4 Convert organic waste into biogas or burn waste in an incinerator that generates electricity. H: methane in biogas is a fuel; the energy is recovered.","F4 有机废物产沼气或焚烧发电。H：沼气（甲烷）是燃料，回收能量"],["F5 Treat wastewater and reuse the treated water. H: harmful substances are removed before release and clean water is saved.","F5 处理废水并再利用。H：排放前去除有害物质，节约水"],["Rainwater harvesting: collect rainwater in a tank for washing and watering plants.","雨水收集：储存雨水用于清洗和浇花"]],"","Tip: action + how it reduces waste or pollution."],["Agriculture and Forestry","农业与林业",[["Issues in agriculture: excess chemical fertilisers and pesticides pollute soil and water (eutrophication) and kill useful organisms; clearing land destroys habitats.","农业问题：过量化肥农药污染土壤水源（富营养化）、杀死有益生物；开垦破坏栖息地"],["Green solutions: organic farming, use of compost and biopesticides (natural predators), crop rotation, drip irrigation and hydroponics.","绿色方法：有机耕作、堆肥、生物农药（天敌）、轮作、滴灌、水培"],["Issues in forestry: illegal and uncontrolled logging cause soil erosion, floods, loss of biodiversity and less carbon dioxide absorbed.","林业问题：乱砍滥伐导致水土流失、洪水、生物多样性减少、吸收CO₂减少"],["Green solutions: selective logging, reforestation, forest reserves and the use of wood from managed forests.","绿色方法：选择性伐木、重新造林、森林保护区、使用管理良好的林木"],["Trees absorb carbon dioxide in photosynthesis, so forests help reduce global warming.","树木光合作用吸收CO₂，有助减缓全球变暖"]],"","Tip: state the problem, the green solution and the benefit."],["Transportation","交通",[["Issues: vehicles burn petrol and diesel which release carbon dioxide, carbon monoxide, nitrogen oxides and particles; traffic jams waste fuel.","问题：燃烧汽油柴油释放CO₂、CO、氮氧化物和微粒；塞车浪费燃料"],["Green solutions: electric vehicles and hybrid vehicles, biofuel such as biodiesel, and public transport, carpooling, cycling and walking.","绿色方法：电动车、混合动力车、生物燃料如生物柴油、公共交通、拼车、骑车和步行"],["An electric vehicle produces no exhaust gases while running, but the electricity used may come from burning fossil fuels.","电动车行驶时无废气，但电力可能来自化石燃料"],["Biofuel is made from plants such as palm oil, so it is renewable; but growing the crops needs land.","生物燃料来自植物（如棕榈油），可再生；但种植需要土地"]],"","Tip: evaluate with an advantage and a limitation."],["Carbon Footprint and the Role of Individuals","碳足迹与个人的角色",[["Carbon footprint is measured in the mass of carbon dioxide released (e.g. kg of CO₂).","碳足迹以释放的CO₂质量表示（如kg）"],["Activities that increase the carbon footprint: using electricity from fossil fuels, driving a private car alone, eating imported food, producing much waste.","增加碳足迹的活动：使用化石燃料电力、独自开车、吃进口食物、制造大量垃圾"],["Ways to reduce it: save electricity, use public transport, practise 3R, plant trees, buy local products, use reusable bags.","减少方法：节电、搭公共交通、3R、种树、买本地产品、用环保袋"],["Reducing the carbon footprint reduces the greenhouse effect and slows down global warming and climate change.","减少碳足迹可减弱温室效应，减缓全球变暖和气候变化"]],"","Tip: write ‘reduce the release of carbon dioxide’ as the reason."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Green Technology","示例题：试卷2 A部分（绿色科技）",[["(a) [1] State one renewable energy source. Scheme: solar / wind / hydro / biomass (1m).","(a)一种可再生能源"],["(b) [2] State why burning fossil fuels is not green technology. Scheme: releases carbon dioxide (1m); causes global warming / pollution (1m).","(b)为何燃烧化石燃料不是绿色科技"],["(c) [2] A bulb of 40 W is switched on for 3 hours. Calculate the energy used in kWh. Scheme: 0.040 × 3 (1m); 0.12 kWh (1m).","(c)计算耗电：0.040×3=0.12 kWh"],["(d) [2] Explain how composting helps the environment. Scheme: reduces the amount of waste in landfills (1m); produces natural fertiliser, so less chemical fertiliser is used (1m).","(d)堆肥如何帮助环境"],["(e) [1] State what 3R stands for. Scheme: reduce, reuse, recycle (1m).","(e)3R代表"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Green Technology (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（绿色科技）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain two ways of reducing the carbon footprint at home. Scheme: save electricity / use LED lamps (1m) so less fossil fuel is burnt (1m); recycle waste (1m) so less waste goes to landfill that releases methane (1m).","(a)在家减少碳足迹的两种方法"],["(b) [KBAT, 6] A town plans to build a solar farm. Evaluate the plan. Scheme: advantage: renewable energy (1m), no carbon dioxide released while operating (1m), reduces use of fossil fuels (1m); limitations: high cost (1m), needs a large land area (1m), supply depends on sunlight (1m). Suggest placing panels on rooftops (1m).","(b)KBAT：评估建太阳能发电场的计划"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying green technology ‘uses no energy’. Correct: it uses energy efficiently and reduces pollution.","错误：说绿色科技不用能源。正确：高效用能并减少污染"],["Mistake: writing 3R as reduce, replace, recover. Correct: reduce, reuse, recycle.","错误：3R写错。正确：reduce, reuse, recycle"],["Mistake: saying electric vehicles are completely pollution free. Correct: no exhaust while running, but electricity generation may pollute.","错误：说电动车完全无污染。正确：行驶无废气，但发电可能污染"],["Mistake: stating only the action. Correct: also state how it protects the environment.","错误：只写做法。正确：还要写对环境的好处"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Name the four sectors of green technology. J: Energy, water and waste management, agriculture and forestry, transportation.","问：绿色科技四大领域？答：能源、水和废物管理、农业与林业、交通"],["S: What does 3R stand for? J: Reduce, reuse, recycle.","问：3R代表？答：减少、再用、回收"],["S: What is a carbon footprint? J: The total amount of greenhouse gases released by an activity, person or product.","问：什么是碳足迹？答：活动、个人或产品释放的温室气体总量"],["S: Why is solar energy a green energy? J: It is renewable and releases no carbon dioxide during operation.","问：太阳能为何环保？答：可再生，运行时不排放CO₂"],["S: What gas is released from rotting waste in a landfill? J: Methane.","问：填埋场腐烂废物释放什么气体？答：甲烷"],["S: Give one limitation of a solar farm. J: High cost, large land area or dependence on sunlight.","问：太阳能发电场的一项局限？答：成本高、占地大或依赖阳光"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-5":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid): the molecule in the nucleus that carries genetic information.","DNA：细胞核内携带遗传信息的分子"],["Gene: a section of DNA that carries the information for one trait (characteristic).","基因：DNA上控制一个性状的片段"],["Chromosome: a thread-like structure in the nucleus made of tightly coiled DNA.","染色体：细胞核内由DNA紧密缠绕而成的丝状结构"],["Allele: an alternative form of a gene at the same position on a pair of chromosomes. Dominant allele: always expressed. Recessive allele: expressed only when two copies are present.","等位基因；显性：总会表现；隐性：需两个才表现"],["Genotype: the combination of alleles of an organism. Phenotype: the observable characteristic.","基因型：等位基因组合；表现型：可观察的性状"],["Mutation: a sudden change in the structure of a gene or in the number or structure of chromosomes.","突变：基因或染色体的突然改变"]],"华文：定义题用关键词作答。","Tip: gene = section of DNA; chromosome = coiled DNA in the nucleus; do not swap them."],["DNA, Genes and Chromosomes","DNA、基因与染色体",[["Order of size, from large to small: cell, nucleus, chromosome, DNA, gene (a gene is a section of DNA).","由大到小：细胞、细胞核、染色体、DNA、基因"],["Chromosomes are found in the nucleus and are made of DNA coiled tightly.","染色体在细胞核内，由DNA缠绕而成"],["Human body cells have 46 chromosomes (23 pairs): diploid. Gametes (sperm and egg) have 23 chromosomes: haploid.","人体细胞46条（23对）：二倍体；配子23条：单倍体"],["Each pair has one chromosome from the father and one from the mother.","每对染色体一条来自父亲，一条来自母亲"],["Genes control traits such as blood group, skin colour and the ability to roll the tongue.","基因控制血型、肤色、卷舌等性状"]],"华文：46条 = 23对。","Tip: state the number for both body cells (46) and gametes (23)."],["Structure of DNA","DNA的结构",[["DNA is a double helix: two strands twisted around each other like a spiral ladder.","DNA是双螺旋：两条链像螺旋梯"],["DNA is made of repeating units called nucleotides.","DNA由核苷酸重复单位组成"],["Each nucleotide has a sugar, a phosphate group and one nitrogenous base.","每个核苷酸含糖、磷酸和一个含氮碱基"],["Four bases: adenine (A), thymine (T), cytosine (C) and guanine (G).","四种碱基：A、T、C、G"],["Base pairing: A pairs with T; C pairs with G. The order of the bases carries the genetic information.","碱基配对：A-T，C-G；碱基顺序携带遗传信息"]],"华文：A-T，C-G 配对必背。","Tip: if one strand is A-T-C-G, the other strand is T-A-G-C."],["Genetic Terminology","遗传学术语",[["Trait: a characteristic of an organism, e.g. height, hair type. Gamete: a sex cell (sperm or egg cell).","性状；配子：性细胞（精子或卵细胞）"],["Homozygous: two identical alleles (TT or tt). Heterozygous: two different alleles (Tt).","纯合：两个相同（TT或tt）；杂合：两个不同（Tt）"],["Dominant allele is written with a capital letter (T); recessive allele with a small letter (t).","显性用大写字母，隐性用小写字母"],["Genotype Tt shows the dominant trait (tall) because T masks t.","基因型Tt表现显性性状，因为T掩盖t"],["Parental generation (P), first filial generation (F1) and second filial generation (F2) are used in crosses.","亲代P、子一代F1、子二代F2"],["Gregor Mendel studied inheritance using pea plants and is known as the father of genetics.","孟德尔用豌豆研究遗传，被称为遗传学之父"]],"华文：纯合 = 相同，杂合 = 不同。","Tip: always write the genotype using letters and the phenotype in words."],["Mitosis and Meiosis","有丝分裂与减数分裂",[["Mitosis: 1 parent cell divides to form 2 daughter cells that are genetically identical to the parent; chromosome number stays the same (diploid).","有丝分裂：1个细胞分成2个，与亲代相同，染色体数不变"],["Mitosis occurs in body cells for growth, replacing dead cells and repairing damaged tissues.","有丝分裂发生于体细胞：生长、替换、修复"],["Meiosis: 1 parent cell divides to form 4 daughter cells (gametes) with half the chromosome number (haploid).","减数分裂：1个细胞分成4个配子，染色体数减半"],["Meiosis occurs in the reproductive organs (testes and ovaries) to produce gametes.","减数分裂发生于生殖器官（睾丸、卵巢）"],["Fertilisation: a sperm (23) fuses with an egg (23) to form a zygote with 46 chromosomes; the diploid number is restored.","受精：精子+卵细胞形成46条染色体的受精卵"],["Meiosis and random fertilisation produce genetic variation.","减数分裂和随机受精产生遗传变异"]],"华文：有丝 = 2个相同；减数 = 4个减半。","Tip: compare using the same points: number of cells, chromosome number, where it happens, function."],["Why Meiosis Is Needed (F + H)","为何需要减数分裂（F + H）",[["F1 Meiosis halves the chromosome number in gametes (46 to 23). H: so that fertilisation restores 46 chromosomes in the zygote.","F1 减数分裂使配子染色体减半。H：受精后恢复46条"],["F2 Without meiosis, the chromosome number would double in every generation. H: this would cause serious abnormalities in the offspring.","F2 没有减数分裂染色体会逐代加倍。H：后代会严重异常"],["F3 Mitosis produces identical cells. H: so that growth and repair produce cells with the same genetic information as the parent cell.","F3 有丝分裂产生相同细胞。H：生长修复的细胞遗传信息一致"],["F4 Gametes produced by meiosis are genetically different. H: offspring show variation, which helps a species to survive changes in the environment.","F4 减数分裂配子各不相同。H：后代有变异，利于物种适应环境变化"]],"华文：F（事实）+ H（解释）。","Tip: give the fact and then link it to fertilisation or variation for the second mark."],["Monohybrid Inheritance","单因子遗传",[["Monohybrid inheritance: the inheritance of one trait controlled by one pair of alleles.","单因子遗传：一个性状由一对等位基因控制"],["Steps: 1 write the parental genotypes; 2 write the gametes; 3 draw a Punnett square; 4 write the genotypes and phenotypes of the offspring; 5 state the ratio.","步骤：亲代基因型、配子、方格图、子代基因型和表现型、比例"],["Each parent gives only one allele to each gamete because the allele pair separates during meiosis.","每个配子只得一个等位基因，因为减数分裂时等位基因分离"],["Cross Tt x Tt: offspring TT, Tt, Tt, tt. Genotype ratio TT : Tt : tt = 1 : 2 : 1. Phenotype ratio tall : short = 3 : 1.","Tt x Tt：基因型1:2:1，表现型3:1"],["Cross Tt x tt: offspring Tt, Tt, tt, tt. Genotype ratio Tt : tt = 1 : 1. Phenotype ratio tall : short = 1 : 1.","Tt x tt：基因型1:1，表现型1:1"],["Probability of the recessive phenotype in Tt x Tt is 1 in 4 (25 percent).","Tt x Tt 隐性性状概率为1/4（25%）"]],"华文：画方格图时每格写两个字母。","Tip: always show the gametes and the Punnett square, as marks are given for each step."],["Worked Example: Monohybrid Cross","例题：单因子杂交",[["Question: In pea plants, tall (T) is dominant over short (t). A heterozygous tall plant is crossed with a short plant. Find the ratio of the offspring.","题：杂合高茎豌豆与矮茎豌豆杂交，求子代比例"],["Step 1 Parents: Tt (tall) x tt (short). (1m)","步骤1：亲代 Tt x tt"],["Step 2 Gametes: T and t from the first parent; t and t from the second parent. (1m)","步骤2：配子 T、t；t、t"],["Step 3 Punnett square gives offspring: Tt, Tt, tt, tt. (1m)","步骤3：方格图得 Tt、Tt、tt、tt"],["Answer: genotype Tt : tt = 1 : 1; phenotype tall : short = 1 : 1, so the probability of a short plant is 1/2 or 50 percent. (1m)","答案：基因型1:1，表现型1:1，矮茎概率1/2"],["If 80 seeds grow, about 40 plants are expected to be tall and 40 short.","若长出80株，预期约40株高、40株矮"]],"华文：先写亲代，再写配子。","Tip: write the ratio as tall : short = 1 : 1 and state the probability as a fraction or percentage."],["Sex Determination","性别决定",[["Humans have 23 pairs of chromosomes: 22 pairs of autosomes and 1 pair of sex chromosomes.","人类23对染色体：22对常染色体、1对性染色体"],["Female: XX. Male: XY. Eggs always carry X; sperm carry either X or Y.","女XX，男XY；卵子都带X，精子带X或Y"],["If an X sperm fertilises the egg, the zygote is XX (girl). If a Y sperm fertilises the egg, the zygote is XY (boy).","X精子受精生女孩，Y精子受精生男孩"],["The father's sperm determines the sex of the baby.","由父亲的精子决定孩子性别"],["The probability of a boy or a girl is 1/2 (50 percent) each time.","每次生男或生女的概率各为1/2"]],"华文：不是母亲决定性别。","Tip: show the Punnett square XX x XY giving XX, XX, XY, XY to get the marks."],["Variation","变异",[["Variation: the differences in traits between individuals of the same species.","变异：同种个体间性状的差异"],["Continuous variation: a range of values between two extremes, e.g. height, mass, skin colour. The data give a smooth curve.","连续变异：两极端之间的一系列值，如身高、体重"],["Discontinuous variation: clearly separate groups with no in-between, e.g. blood group, ability to roll the tongue, attached or free earlobe.","不连续变异：明显分开的类别，如血型、卷舌"],["Causes of variation: genetic factors (meiosis, random fertilisation, mutation) and environmental factors (food, exercise, sunlight).","变异原因：遗传因素和环境因素"],["Identical twins have the same genes, but differences in mass can arise from differences in diet and lifestyle.","同卵双胞胎基因相同，体重差异来自饮食和生活方式"]],"华文：连续 = 一个范围；不连续 = 分类。","Tip: give an example for each type of variation, not only the definition."],["Investigation: Variation Among Students","探究：同学之间的变异",[["Aim: to study the variation in height (continuous) and tongue rolling (discontinuous) among students in the class. (1m)","目的：研究同学身高和卷舌的变异"],["Problem statement: do students in the same class show variation in height? (1m) Hypothesis: students of the same age show different heights. (1m)","问题陈述与假设：同龄同学身高不同"],["Variables: manipulated = the student (individual); responding = height and ability to roll the tongue; fixed = measuring method, e.g. standing straight without shoes. (3m)","变量：操纵=不同学生；响应=身高与卷舌能力；固定=测量方法"],["Apparatus and materials: measuring tape, graph paper, 30 students. (1m)","仪器：卷尺、方格纸、30名学生"],["Procedure: 1 Measure the height of each student using the measuring tape. 2 Record the data in a table. 3 Count the students who can roll the tongue and those who cannot. 4 Draw a bar chart for height groups and a bar chart for tongue rolling. (2m)","步骤：量身高、记录、统计卷舌、画条形图"],["Observation: height shows a range of values (continuous); tongue rolling gives only two groups (discontinuous). (1m) Conclusion: variation exists among individuals; hypothesis accepted. (1m)","观察：身高连续、卷舌两类；结论：个体存在变异，假设接受"]],"华文：用同一格式写任何探究题。","Tip: state the method of measurement and the type of graph drawn (bar chart for discontinuous variation)."],["Mutation","突变",[["Gene mutation: a change in the sequence of bases in DNA, which may change the trait.","基因突变：DNA碱基序列改变"],["Chromosome mutation: a change in the number or structure of chromosomes, e.g. Down syndrome has an extra chromosome 21 (47 chromosomes).","染色体突变：数目或结构改变，如唐氏综合征47条"],["Mutagens: factors that cause mutation, e.g. X-rays, ultraviolet rays, gamma rays, radioactive substances and certain chemicals such as tar in cigarettes.","诱变因素：X射线、紫外线、伽马射线、放射性物质、某些化学品"],["Most mutations are harmful, some have no effect, and a few are beneficial.","多数突变有害，部分无影响，少数有益"],["Only mutations in gametes can be passed to the next generation.","只有配子中的突变才能遗传给后代"]],"华文：突变是突然的、随机的。","Tip: name the type of mutation and give one mutagen as an example."],["Genetic Disorders","遗传疾病",[["Down syndrome: caused by an extra chromosome 21; the person has 47 chromosomes and shows learning difficulties and typical facial features.","唐氏综合征：多一条21号染色体，共47条"],["Thalassaemia: a disorder of haemoglobin; the body cannot produce enough healthy red blood cells, causing anaemia.","地中海贫血：血红蛋白异常，导致贫血"],["Haemophilia: blood does not clot properly, so bleeding is prolonged. It is carried on the X chromosome and is more common in males.","血友病：血液不易凝固，X染色体遗传，男性较常见"],["Colour blindness: unable to tell some colours apart, e.g. red and green. It is also carried on the X chromosome.","色盲：无法分辨某些颜色，X染色体遗传"],["Albinism: the body cannot produce the pigment melanin, so the skin, hair and eyes lack colour.","白化病：无法产生黑色素"]],"华文：血友病和色盲与X染色体有关。","Tip: state the cause and one symptom of each disorder."],["Genetic Engineering and Ethics","基因工程与伦理",[["Genetic engineering: changing the genes of an organism by transferring a gene from one organism to another to produce a desired trait.","基因工程：转移基因以获得所需性状"],["Examples: bacteria with a human gene produce insulin; genetically modified (GM) crops resist pests or last longer; cloning produces identical organisms, e.g. Dolly the sheep.","例：产胰岛素的细菌、转基因作物、克隆羊多莉"],["Benefits: more food, treatment of diseases, better crop quality.","好处：更多食物、治疗疾病、作物品质更好"],["Concerns: safety of GM food, effect on the environment and biodiversity, animal welfare and ethical or religious issues.","顾虑：食品安全、环境和生物多样性、动物福利、伦理宗教问题"],["Decisions should consider both benefits and risks, and follow laws and ethics.","决定要权衡利弊，遵守法律和伦理"]],"华文：KBAT题要写利与弊。","Tip: for evaluate or justify questions, give one benefit and one risk, then your opinion."],["Natural Selection (F + H)","自然选择（F + H）",[["F1 Individuals in a population show variation. H: some have traits that suit the environment better.","F1 种群中个体有变异。H：有些更适应环境"],["F2 Individuals with suitable traits survive and reproduce. H: they pass the genes for these traits to their offspring.","F2 适应者存活并繁殖。H：把基因传给后代"],["F3 Individuals with unsuitable traits die or reproduce less. H: the percentage of the suitable trait in the population increases over generations.","F3 不适应者死亡或少繁殖。H：适应性状比例逐代增加"],["F4 Example: dark peppered moths on dark, polluted tree trunks. H: they are hidden from birds, so more survive than light moths.","F4 例：污染树干上深色蛾被鸟发现少而存活更多"]],"华文：变异 → 生存 → 繁殖 → 遗传。","Tip: the chain is variation, survival, reproduction, passing on the genes."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Genetics","示例题：试卷2 A部分（遗传）",[["(a) [1] What is a gene? Scheme: a section of DNA that controls a trait (1m).","(a)基因：控制性状的DNA片段"],["(b) [2] Tall (T) is dominant over short (t). State the genotype of a heterozygous tall plant and a short plant. Scheme: Tt (1m); tt (1m).","(b)杂合高茎Tt；矮茎tt"],["(c) [3] Two heterozygous tall plants are crossed. Draw the Punnett square and state the phenotype ratio. Scheme: gametes T, t and T, t (1m); TT, Tt, Tt, tt (1m); tall : short = 3 : 1 (1m).","(c)配子、方格图、表现型3:1"],["(d) [2] State two functions of mitosis. Scheme: growth (1m); repair of damaged tissues / replace dead cells (1m).","(d)有丝分裂的功能：生长；修复"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Genetics and Society (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（遗传与社会）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain why meiosis is important in humans. Scheme: produces gametes with 23 chromosomes (1m); so that fertilisation restores 46 chromosomes (1m); produces genetic variation (1m); so offspring differ from each other and the species can survive changes (1m).","(a)减数分裂的重要性"],["(b) [3] A couple already has two daughters. A student says that the next baby must be a boy. Evaluate this statement. Scheme: the sperm decides the sex (1m); X or Y sperm have an equal chance of fertilising the egg (1m); the probability of a boy is 1/2, so the statement is wrong (1m).","(b)评价：下一个必是男孩？错，概率1/2"],["(c) [KBAT] A company wants to sell GM rice that resists pests. Justify whether the government should allow it. Scheme: benefit: higher yield / less pesticide (1m); risk: effect on the environment or human health is not fully known (1m); suggestion: allow after safety tests and label the food (1m).","(c)是否允许转基因稻米：利、弊、先测试并标示"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying a chromosome is a section of DNA. Correct: a gene is a section of DNA; a chromosome is coiled DNA.","错误：染色体是DNA片段。正确：基因是DNA片段"],["Mistake: saying meiosis produces 2 cells with 46 chromosomes. Correct: meiosis produces 4 cells with 23 chromosomes.","错误：减数分裂产生2个46条。正确：4个23条"],["Mistake: writing phenotype ratio as 1 : 2 : 1 for Tt x Tt. Correct: genotype 1 : 2 : 1, phenotype 3 : 1.","错误：表现型写1:2:1。正确：基因型1:2:1，表现型3:1"],["Mistake: saying the mother determines the baby's sex. Correct: the father's sperm (X or Y) determines it.","错误：母亲决定性别。正确：父亲精子决定"],["Mistake: not giving a letter key for the alleles. Correct: state T = tall, t = short before the cross.","错误：不写字母代表。正确：先写T=高，t=矮"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: How many chromosomes are in a human gamete? J: 23.","问：人类配子有多少条染色体？答：23条"],["S: Which base pairs with adenine in DNA? J: Thymine.","问：DNA中A与什么配对？答：T（胸腺嘧啶）"],["S: What is the phenotype ratio of Tt x Tt? J: 3 : 1.","问：Tt x Tt 表现型比？答：3:1"],["S: What decides the sex of a baby? J: The sperm (X or Y).","问：什么决定婴儿性别？答：精子（X或Y）"],["S: Name a type of discontinuous variation. J: Blood group (or tongue rolling).","问：举一个不连续变异？答：血型（或卷舌）"],["S: What causes Down syndrome? J: An extra chromosome 21.","问：唐氏综合征的原因？答：多一条21号染色体"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-6":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Skeleton: a framework of hard structures that supports the body, protects organs and allows movement.","骨骼：支撑身体、保护器官并使运动成为可能的框架"],["Exoskeleton: a hard outer covering of the body (e.g. insects, crabs). Endoskeleton: an internal skeleton of bone and cartilage (e.g. vertebrates). Hydrostatic skeleton: a fluid-filled body cavity supported by muscles (e.g. earthworm).","外骨骼；内骨骼；流体静力骨骼"],["Moulting (ecdysis): the shedding of the old exoskeleton so that the animal can grow.","蜕皮：脱去旧外骨骼以便生长"],["Joint: the place where two or more bones meet. Tendon: joins muscle to bone. Ligament: joins bone to bone.","关节；肌腱（肌肉连骨）；韧带（骨连骨）"],["Antagonistic muscles: a pair of muscles that work in opposite directions; when one contracts the other relaxes.","拮抗肌：作用相反的一对肌肉，一收缩另一放松"],["Turgor pressure: the pressure of water pushing the cell contents against the cell wall, which makes a plant cell firm.","膨压：水分推挤细胞内含物压向细胞壁的压力，使细胞坚挺"],["Growth: a permanent increase in size, mass or number of cells of an organism.","生长：生物体大小、质量或细胞数目的永久增加"]],"华文：定义题要写关键词，尤其是肌腱和韧带不要混淆。","Tip: tendon = muscle to bone; ligament = bone to bone."],["Types of Skeleton in Animals","动物骨骼的种类",[["Exoskeleton: insects, crabs, prawns. Hard and waterproof; protects the body and prevents water loss; must be moulted for the animal to grow.","外骨骼：昆虫、蟹、虾；坚硬防水、保护身体；需蜕皮才能生长"],["Endoskeleton: fish, birds, mammals (vertebrates). Made of bone and cartilage; grows together with the body; muscles attach to it.","内骨骼：脊椎动物；由骨和软骨组成，随身体一起生长"],["Hydrostatic skeleton: earthworm, jellyfish, sea anemone. Fluid in the body is held under pressure by muscles and gives the body its shape.","流体静力骨骼：蚯蚓、水母、海葵；体液受肌肉压力维持体形"],["Hollow bones in birds make the body lighter for flying yet remain strong.","鸟类空心骨使身体较轻便于飞行但仍坚固"],["Water supports the body of aquatic animals through buoyancy, so their skeleton can be lighter.","水的浮力支撑水生动物，骨骼可较轻"]],"华文：先判断动物属于哪一类骨骼，再写特征。","Tip: name the type of skeleton AND one feature to earn both marks."],["Exoskeleton and Moulting (F + H)","外骨骼与蜕皮（F + H）",[["F1 The exoskeleton of an insect is hard and cannot expand. H: the insect must shed it (moult) so that the body can grow bigger.","F1 昆虫外骨骼坚硬不能扩大。H：必须蜕皮身体才能长大"],["F2 A newly moulted animal has a soft new exoskeleton. H: it is easily attacked by predators until the new exoskeleton hardens.","F2 刚蜕皮的新外骨骼柔软。H：硬化前易被捕食者攻击"],["F3 The exoskeleton is waterproof. H: it reduces water loss from the body of land animals.","F3 外骨骼防水。H：减少陆生动物体内水分流失"],["F4 The exoskeleton is hard. H: it protects the soft internal organs from injury and enemies.","F4 外骨骼坚硬。H：保护柔软的内部器官"]],"华文：蜕皮题的标准答案：外骨骼坚硬不能生长，所以要蜕皮。","Tip: write 'exoskeleton cannot grow' (F) + 'moult so the body can enlarge' (H)."],["Movement of an Earthworm (F + H)","蚯蚓的运动（F + H）",[["F1 The earthworm has a hydrostatic skeleton of fluid and two sets of muscles: circular and longitudinal. H: the muscles squeeze the fluid so the body changes shape.","F1 蚯蚓有流体骨骼和环肌、纵肌两组肌肉。H：肌肉挤压体液使体形改变"],["F2 Circular muscles contract and longitudinal muscles relax. H: the body becomes longer and thinner and moves forward.","F2 环肌收缩、纵肌放松。H：身体变长变细并向前伸"],["F3 Longitudinal muscles contract and circular muscles relax. H: the body becomes shorter and fatter and pulls the rear part forward.","F3 纵肌收缩、环肌放松。H：身体变短变粗，把后部拉向前"],["F4 Chaetae (bristles) grip the soil. H: to anchor the body and prevent it slipping backwards.","F4 刚毛抓住泥土。H：固定身体防止后滑"],["F5 The body surface is kept moist with mucus. H: it helps the earthworm slide through the soil.","F5 体表有黏液保持湿润。H：帮助在土中滑行"]],"华文：这两组肌肉交替收缩，记得写「变长变细」和「变短变粗」。","Tip: name the muscle, say contract/relax, and state the change in body shape."],["Functions of the Human Skeleton","人体骨骼的功能",[["Support: gives the body its shape and holds the body upright.","支撑：赋予体形，保持身体直立"],["Protection: the skull protects the brain; the rib cage protects the heart and lungs; the vertebral column protects the spinal cord.","保护：颅骨护脑；胸廓护心肺；脊柱护脊髓"],["Movement: bones act as levers; muscles attach to bones through tendons.","运动：骨骼如杠杆，肌肉通过肌腱附着于骨"],["Blood cell production: the bone marrow makes red and white blood cells.","造血：骨髓制造红细胞和白细胞"],["Storage of minerals: bones store calcium and phosphorus.","矿物质储存：骨储存钙和磷"]],"华文：保护器官要配对记：颅骨-脑，胸廓-心肺，脊柱-脊髓。","Tip: match each bone with the organ it protects."],["Support in Plants","植物的支撑",[["Herbaceous plants: supported by turgor pressure; when the cells lose water the plant wilts.","草本植物：靠膨压支撑；细胞失水则萎蔫"],["Woody plants (trees): supported by xylem tissue hardened with lignin, which forms a strong trunk.","木本植物：靠含木质素的木质部形成坚固树干"],["Climbers: use tendrils or twining stems to hold onto other objects.","攀缘植物：用卷须或缠绕茎攀附物体"],["Mangrove plants: have stilt (prop) roots that support the plant in soft, muddy soil.","红树林植物：支柱根在软泥中支撑植物"],["Aquatic plants: supported by the buoyancy of water; stems are flexible and leaves may have air spaces so that they float.","水生植物：靠水的浮力支撑；茎柔软，叶有气室使其漂浮"]],"华文：先区分陆生与水生，再写支撑方式。","Tip: terrestrial = turgor pressure / lignin; aquatic = buoyancy of water."],["Turgor Pressure and Wilting (F + H)","膨压与萎蔫（F + H）",[["F1 When there is enough water, water enters the vacuole by osmosis. H: the cell becomes turgid and presses against the cell wall, so the plant stands firm.","F1 水充足时水渗入液泡。H：细胞膨胀压向细胞壁，植物挺立"],["F2 When the plant loses water faster than it absorbs it, the cells become flaccid. H: turgor pressure drops and the plant wilts.","F2 失水快于吸水，细胞变松弛。H：膨压下降，植物萎蔫"],["F3 Watering the wilted plant makes the cells turgid again. H: water enters the cells, turgor pressure rises and the plant recovers.","F3 浇水后细胞恢复膨胀。H：水进入细胞，膨压上升，植物恢复"],["F4 Woody stems do not wilt as easily. H: lignin in the xylem gives permanent support.","F4 木本茎不易萎蔫。H：木质素提供永久支撑"]],"华文：膨压题要写出水的进出和细胞的变化。","Tip: write 'cells become flaccid, turgor pressure decreases, plant wilts'."],["Human Joints","人体关节",[["Ball-and-socket joint (shoulder, hip): allows movement in all directions and rotation.","球窝关节（肩、髋）：可向各方向活动及旋转"],["Hinge joint (elbow, knee): allows movement in one direction only, like a door hinge.","铰链关节（肘、膝）：只能在一个方向活动"],["Pivot joint (between the first two vertebrae at the neck): allows the head to turn from side to side.","枢轴关节（颈部）：使头部左右转动"],["Cartilage at the ends of the bones reduces friction and absorbs shock; synovial fluid lubricates the joint.","软骨减少摩擦、吸收冲击；滑液润滑关节"]],"华文：关节题常配合部位一起考。","Tip: state the type of joint and the direction of movement it allows."],["Antagonistic Muscles in the Arm (F + H)","手臂的拮抗肌（F + H）",[["F1 To bend the arm, the biceps contracts and the triceps relaxes. H: the biceps pulls the forearm upwards through the tendon, with the elbow as the hinge joint.","F1 弯臂：二头肌收缩、三头肌放松。H：二头肌经肌腱拉前臂上抬，肘为铰链关节"],["F2 To straighten the arm, the triceps contracts and the biceps relaxes. H: the triceps pulls the forearm downwards.","F2 伸直手臂：三头肌收缩、二头肌放松。H：三头肌拉前臂下压"],["F3 Muscles can only pull, not push. H: so muscles must work in pairs (antagonistic) to move a bone in two directions.","F3 肌肉只能拉不能推。H：因此要成对工作才能使骨双向运动"],["F4 Muscles are attached to bones by tendons. H: the tendon transfers the force of the muscle to the bone.","F4 肌腱把肌肉连到骨。H：肌腱把肌肉的力传给骨"]],"华文：写「谁收缩、谁放松、拉动什么」三件事。","Tip: for each movement, name the contracting muscle AND the relaxing muscle."],["Tendon, Ligament and Cartilage","肌腱、韧带与软骨",[["Tendon: strong, inelastic, joins muscle to bone and transmits the force of muscle contraction.","肌腱：坚韧不伸缩，连肌肉与骨，传递肌肉收缩的力"],["Ligament: strong and slightly elastic, joins bone to bone and keeps the joint stable.","韧带：坚韧略有弹性，连骨与骨，稳固关节"],["Cartilage: smooth, flexible tissue at the ends of bones and in the ear and nose; reduces friction and absorbs shock.","软骨：骨端、耳、鼻中光滑柔韧的组织，减少摩擦、吸收冲击"],["Muscle: contracts to pull the bone and produce movement.","肌肉：收缩牵拉骨产生运动"]],"华文：三者的位置和功能要对应。","Tip: give the structure, what it joins, and its function."],["Problems of the Musculoskeletal System","肌肉骨骼系统的问题",[["Osteoporosis: bones lose calcium and become porous and brittle, so they break easily; common in the elderly.","骨质疏松：骨失钙变多孔易碎，易骨折，常见于老人"],["Arthritis: inflammation of the joints, causing pain, swelling and stiffness.","关节炎：关节发炎，疼痛、肿胀、僵硬"],["Scoliosis: the vertebral column curves sideways abnormally.","脊柱侧弯：脊柱异常向侧面弯曲"],["Sprain: ligament at a joint is stretched or torn by sudden twisting.","扭伤：关节处韧带因突然扭转被拉伤或撕裂"],["Prevention: enough calcium and vitamin D, regular exercise, correct posture, warm up before sport, avoid carrying heavy loads.","预防：足够钙与维生素D、规律运动、正确姿势、运动前热身、避免负重"]],"华文：每种问题配一个特征和一个预防方法。","Tip: state the problem, the cause or symptom, and one way to prevent it."],["Human Growth Pattern","人的生长模式",[["The growth curve of height against age is S-shaped (sigmoid).","身高随年龄的生长曲线呈S形"],["Infancy: rapid growth. Childhood: slower, steady growth.","婴儿期：快速生长；童年期：较慢稳定"],["Puberty: growth spurt; girls start earlier (about 10-12 years) than boys (about 12-14 years).","青春期：生长突增；女孩比男孩早"],["After puberty: growth slows down and stops when adult height is reached.","青春期后：生长减慢，成年后停止"],["Boys generally become taller and heavier adults than girls.","男孩成年后一般比女孩更高更重"]],"华文：看到S形曲线就写 sigmoid。","Tip: when reading a graph, state the stage and say 'rapid / slow / stops'."],["Factors Affecting Growth (F + H)","影响生长的因素（F + H）",[["F1 Balanced diet (protein, calcium, vitamins). H: protein builds new tissues; calcium and vitamin D make strong bones.","F1 均衡饮食。H：蛋白质构建新组织；钙与维生素D使骨坚固"],["F2 Hormones such as growth hormone and sex hormones. H: they control the rate of growth and the growth spurt in puberty.","F2 激素（生长激素、性激素）。H：控制生长速率和青春期突增"],["F3 Genetic factors. H: inherited genes determine the potential height of a person.","F3 遗传因素。H：遗传基因决定潜在身高"],["F4 Exercise and enough sleep. H: exercise strengthens bones and muscles; growth hormone is released mostly during sleep.","F4 运动与充足睡眠。H：运动强健骨肌；生长激素多在睡眠时分泌"],["F5 Disease and poor nutrition. H: they slow down growth because the body lacks nutrients and energy.","F5 疾病与营养不良。H：缺乏营养和能量，生长变慢"]],"华文：每个因素都要写出理由。","Tip: give the factor and explain how it affects growth."],["Growth in Plants and Annual Rings","植物的生长与年轮",[["Growth of a plant can be measured by height, dry mass or number of leaves over time.","植物生长可用高度、干重或叶数随时间测量"],["Dry mass is the most accurate measure because the water content of fresh mass changes.","干重最准确，因鲜重含水量会变"],["The growth curve of a seedling is S-shaped: slow start, rapid growth, then levelling off.","幼苗生长曲线呈S形：起初慢、然后快、最后趋平"],["Woody plants form annual rings in the trunk: each ring is one year; a wide ring means a good growth year (enough water and light).","木本植物树干形成年轮：一圈一年；宽年轮表示生长良好的一年"],["Age of a tree = number of annual rings.","树龄 = 年轮数"]],"华文：用干重而不是鲜重，是常考的理由。","Tip: explain 'dry mass is used because fresh mass includes water that varies'."],["Investigation: Growth Pattern of Green Bean Seedlings","探究：绿豆幼苗的生长模式",[["Aim: to study the growth pattern of a seedling. Problem statement: how does the height of a seedling change with time? Hypothesis: the height of the seedling increases with time. (3m)","目的：研究幼苗生长模式；假设：高度随时间增加"],["Variables: manipulated = time (days); responding = height of seedling; fixed = type of seed, amount of water, light, temperature. (3m)","变量：操纵=时间；响应=幼苗高度；固定=种子种类、水量、光照、温度"],["Apparatus and materials: pots, soil, green bean seeds, ruler, water. (1m)","仪器和材料"],["Procedure: 1 Plant 10 seeds in a pot of soil and water them equally each day. 2 When the seedlings appear, measure the height of each with a ruler every 2 days. 3 Calculate the average height and record in a table. 4 Plot a graph of average height against time. (2m)","步骤：种植、每2天测量高度、计算平均值、绘图"],["Observation: height increases slowly at first, then rapidly, then slowly; the graph is S-shaped. (1m)","观察：先慢后快再慢，S形曲线"],["Conclusion: the height of the seedling increases with time following a sigmoid pattern; the hypothesis is accepted. (1m)","结论：高度随时间增加，呈S形；假设被接受"]],"华文：用多棵幼苗取平均值，结果更可靠。","Tip: measure many seedlings and take the average to make results reliable."],["Calculating Growth Rate: Worked Example","计算生长速率：例题",[["Formula: growth rate = \\(\\dfrac{\\text{change in height}}{\\text{time taken}}\\). Percentage increase = \\(\\dfrac{\\text{increase}}{\\text{initial value}} \\times 100\\%\\).","公式：生长速率 = 高度变化 ÷ 时间；增长百分比 = 增加量 ÷ 初值 ×100%"],["Example: a seedling grows from 4 cm to 16 cm in 6 days. Find (a) the growth rate, (b) the percentage increase in height.","例题：幼苗6天内由4 cm长到16 cm，求生长速率和增长百分比"],["(a) Change in height = 16 - 4 = 12 cm (1m). Growth rate = \\(\\dfrac{12}{6}\\) = 2 cm per day (1m, with unit).","(a)变化=12 cm；速率=2 cm/天（要写单位）"],["(b) Percentage increase = \\(\\dfrac{12}{4} \\times 100\\%\\) (1m) = 300% (1m).","(b)12÷4×100% = 300%"]],"华文：每一步都有分，单位一定要写。","Tip: show the formula, substitution and the answer with unit."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Support, Movement and Growth","示例题：试卷2 A部分（支撑、运动与生长）",[["(a) [1] Name the type of skeleton in an earthworm. Scheme: hydrostatic skeleton (1m).","(a)蚯蚓的骨骼：流体静力骨骼"],["(b) [2] Why must a crab moult? Scheme: the exoskeleton is hard and cannot grow (1m); so that the body can enlarge (1m).","(b)蟹为何蜕皮：外骨骼不能生长；使身体变大"],["(c) [2] The arm is bent. State the muscle that contracts and the muscle that relaxes. Scheme: biceps contracts (1m); triceps relaxes (1m).","(c)弯臂：二头肌收缩；三头肌放松"],["(d) [2] Why does a plant wilt when it is not watered? Scheme: cells lose water (1m); turgor pressure decreases (1m).","(d)不浇水植物萎蔫：细胞失水；膨压下降"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Bones, Muscles and Growth (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（骨、肌肉与生长）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how the forearm is raised and lowered. Scheme: biceps contracts, triceps relaxes (1m); forearm is pulled up through the tendon (1m); triceps contracts, biceps relaxes (1m); forearm is pulled down (1m).","(a)前臂如何抬起与放下"],["(b) [2] State two differences between a tendon and a ligament. Scheme: tendon joins muscle to bone, ligament joins bone to bone (1m); tendon is inelastic, ligament is slightly elastic (1m).","(b)肌腱与韧带的两点区别"],["(c) [KBAT] A 70-year-old woman fractured her hip after a minor fall. Suggest two ways she could have reduced the risk and give a reason for each. Scheme: take food rich in calcium and vitamin D (1m) so that bones remain strong and dense (1m); do weight-bearing exercise such as walking (1m) to strengthen bones and muscles (1m).","(c)建议两种降低风险的方法并说明理由：补钙和维生素D；负重运动"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying tendon joins bone to bone. Correct: tendon joins muscle to bone; ligament joins bone to bone.","错误：肌腱连骨与骨。正确：肌腱连肌肉与骨；韧带连骨与骨"],["Mistake: writing that a muscle 'pushes' the bone. Correct: muscles only contract and pull.","错误：肌肉推骨。正确：肌肉只能收缩牵拉"],["Mistake: for bending the arm, writing only 'biceps contracts'. Correct: biceps contracts and triceps relaxes.","错误：只写二头肌收缩。正确：同时写三头肌放松"],["Mistake: answering that a plant wilts 'because it has no water' only. Correct: cells lose water, become flaccid, turgor pressure decreases.","错误：只写没有水。正确：细胞失水变松弛，膨压下降"],["Mistake: using fresh mass as the best measure of plant growth. Correct: dry mass, because water content varies.","错误：用鲜重。正确：用干重，因含水量会变"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Why must an insect moult? J: Its exoskeleton is hard and cannot grow, so it is shed so the body can enlarge.","问：昆虫为何要蜕皮？答：外骨骼坚硬不能生长，蜕去才能长大"],["S: What joins muscle to bone? J: Tendon.","问：什么连接肌肉和骨？答：肌腱"],["S: Which muscle contracts when the arm is straightened? J: Triceps.","问：伸直手臂时哪块肌肉收缩？答：三头肌"],["S: What type of joint is the shoulder? J: Ball-and-socket joint.","问：肩是什么关节？答：球窝关节"],["S: How is the age of a tree found? J: Count the annual rings.","问：如何得知树龄？答：数年轮"],["S: What is the shape of the human growth curve? J: S-shaped (sigmoid).","问：人的生长曲线形状？答：S形"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-7":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Hormone: a chemical substance produced by an endocrine gland and carried by the blood to a target organ to control its activity.","激素：内分泌腺产生、由血液运送到靶器官以调控其活动的化学物质"],["Endocrine gland: a ductless gland that releases hormones directly into the blood.","内分泌腺：无导管、把激素直接释放入血液的腺体"],["Target organ: the organ that responds to a particular hormone.","靶器官：对某种激素起反应的器官"],["Hormonal imbalance: the condition when a hormone is produced too little or too much.","激素失衡：激素分泌过少或过多"],["Drug: a substance that changes the way the body or mind works. Drug abuse: using drugs without medical reason or in wrong amounts.","药物；药物滥用：无医疗理由或错误剂量使用药物"],["Healthy mind: a mental state in which a person can cope with stress, think clearly, make decisions and get along with others.","健康心智：能应对压力、清晰思考、做决定并与人相处的心理状态"]],"华文：激素的定义要写出「血液」和「靶器官」两个关键词。","Tip: hormone definition must include 'carried by blood' and 'target organ'."],["Human Endocrine Glands and Hormones","人体内分泌腺与激素",[["Pituitary gland (below the brain): secretes growth hormone and controls other glands.","脑垂体：分泌生长激素并调控其他腺体"],["Thyroid gland (neck): secretes thyroxine, which controls the metabolic rate.","甲状腺：分泌甲状腺素，控制代谢率"],["Pancreas: secretes insulin (lowers blood glucose) and glucagon (raises blood glucose).","胰腺：分泌胰岛素（降血糖）和胰高血糖素（升血糖）"],["Adrenal glands (above the kidneys): secrete adrenaline, which prepares the body for emergency (fight or flight).","肾上腺：分泌肾上腺素，使身体应对紧急情况"],["Ovaries: secrete oestrogen and progesterone. Testes: secrete testosterone.","卵巢：雌激素、孕激素；睾丸：睾酮"]],"华文：腺体、激素、功能三样要配对。","Tip: name the gland, the hormone and the function in one sentence."],["Effects of Adrenaline and Sex Hormones","肾上腺素与性激素的作用",[["Adrenaline: increases heart rate, breathing rate and blood glucose level; blood flows more to the muscles.","肾上腺素：加快心跳和呼吸、升高血糖，更多血液流向肌肉"],["Oestrogen: develops female secondary sexual characteristics (e.g. broader hips, breast development) and controls the menstrual cycle.","雌激素：发展女性第二性征并调控月经周期"],["Testosterone: develops male secondary sexual characteristics (e.g. deeper voice, facial hair) and sperm production.","睾酮：发展男性第二性征（声音低沉、胡须）并促进精子生成"],["Growth hormone: stimulates growth of bones and muscles, especially in childhood and puberty.","生长激素：刺激骨与肌肉生长，特别在儿童和青春期"]],"华文：肾上腺素又叫「战或逃」激素。","Tip: link the hormone to its effect on the body, e.g. adrenaline - faster heartbeat."],["Nervous System and Endocrine System Compared (F + H)","神经系统与内分泌系统比较（F + H）",[["F1 Nervous system sends electrical impulses along nerves. H: the response is very fast.","F1 神经系统沿神经传电信号。H：反应非常快"],["F2 Endocrine system releases hormones into the blood. H: the response is slower because the blood carries the hormones to the target organ.","F2 内分泌系统把激素释放入血。H：血液运送，反应较慢"],["F3 The effect of nervous control is short-lived. H: the impulse stops quickly once the stimulus is gone.","F3 神经调控效果短暂。H：刺激消失冲动即停"],["F4 The effect of hormones lasts longer. H: hormones remain in the blood for some time.","F4 激素效果持久。H：激素在血中停留一段时间"]],"华文：快而短 vs 慢而久，是比较题的标准答案。","Tip: compare using 'faster than / slower than' and 'shorter / longer lasting'."],["Control of Blood Glucose Level (F + H)","血糖水平的调节（F + H）",[["F1 After a meal, the blood glucose level rises. H: the pancreas secretes more insulin.","F1 饭后血糖升高。H：胰腺分泌更多胰岛素"],["F2 Insulin causes the liver to change excess glucose into glycogen and the cells to take in glucose. H: the blood glucose level falls back to normal.","F2 胰岛素使肝脏把多余葡萄糖转为糖原、细胞吸收葡萄糖。H：血糖回落至正常"],["F3 When the blood glucose level is low (e.g. during fasting), the pancreas secretes glucagon. H: glucagon changes glycogen back into glucose and the level rises to normal.","F3 血糖低时胰腺分泌胰高血糖素。H：糖原变回葡萄糖，血糖升至正常"],["F4 The blood glucose level is kept constant by these two hormones. H: cells need a steady supply of glucose for respiration.","F4 两种激素使血糖保持稳定。H：细胞呼吸需稳定的葡萄糖供应"]],"华文：胰岛素降血糖，胰高血糖素升血糖，别写反。","Tip: insulin lowers and glucagon raises blood glucose; state the organ that responds (liver)."],["Hormonal Imbalance","激素失衡",[["Diabetes mellitus: too little insulin (or the body does not respond to insulin), so blood glucose stays high and glucose appears in the urine.","糖尿病：胰岛素不足（或身体不响应），血糖持续偏高，尿中有糖"],["Goitre: swelling of the thyroid gland in the neck, caused by lack of iodine, which is needed to make thyroxine.","甲状腺肿：缺碘导致甲状腺肿大；碘是制造甲状腺素所需"],["Gigantism: too much growth hormone in childhood causes abnormal tallness.","巨人症：童年期生长激素过多导致异常高大"],["Dwarfism: too little growth hormone in childhood causes very short height.","侏儒症：童年期生长激素过少导致极矮"],["Treatment: insulin injection for diabetes; iodised salt and seafood to prevent goitre; hormone therapy under a doctor.","治疗：糖尿病注射胰岛素；食用碘盐和海产预防甲状腺肿；医生指导的激素治疗"]],"华文：每种病写出「哪种激素、多还是少」。","Tip: state the hormone AND whether it is too much or too little."],["Diabetes and Goitre (F + H)","糖尿病与甲状腺肿（F + H）",[["F1 A diabetic person lacks insulin. H: glucose cannot be changed to glycogen and cells cannot take it in, so the blood glucose stays high.","F1 糖尿病人缺胰岛素。H：葡萄糖不能转成糖原，细胞无法吸收，血糖偏高"],["F2 Diabetics should control the intake of sugar and take regular exercise. H: to keep the blood glucose level near normal.","F2 糖尿病人要控制糖分、规律运动。H：使血糖接近正常"],["F3 Lack of iodine in the diet reduces thyroxine production. H: the pituitary gland stimulates the thyroid more and it swells, forming a goitre.","F3 饮食缺碘使甲状腺素减少。H：垂体更多刺激甲状腺使其肿大"],["F4 Eat iodised salt and seafood. H: to supply iodine for making thyroxine.","F4 吃碘盐和海产。H：提供合成甲状腺素的碘"]],"华文：原因+后果，别只写病名。","Tip: link the cause (lack of hormone / iodine) to the effect on the body."],["Types of Drugs","药物的种类",[["Stimulants: speed up the nervous system (e.g. caffeine, nicotine, amphetamine).","兴奋剂：加速神经系统（咖啡因、尼古丁、安非他命）"],["Depressants: slow down the nervous system (e.g. alcohol, barbiturates).","抑制剂：减慢神经系统（酒精、巴比妥类）"],["Hallucinogens: change perception and cause hallucinations (e.g. LSD).","致幻剂：改变感知并引起幻觉（如LSD）"],["Analgesics: relieve pain (e.g. aspirin, paracetamol; stronger ones such as morphine).","镇痛剂：缓解疼痛（阿司匹林、扑热息痛；吗啡较强）"],["Narcotics: strong pain-killing drugs that are addictive (e.g. heroin, morphine); illegal when used without medical reason.","麻醉药：强效止痛、易上瘾（海洛因、吗啡）；无医疗理由使用属违法"]],"华文：配对记：类型 + 例子 + 对神经系统的作用。","Tip: give the type of drug and one example."],["Effects of Drug and Alcohol Abuse (F + H)","药物与酒精滥用的影响（F + H）",[["F1 Alcohol is a depressant. H: it slows down the nervous system, so reaction time is longer and balance and coordination are poor.","F1 酒精是抑制剂。H：减慢神经系统，反应变慢、平衡协调差"],["F2 Drug and alcohol abuse cause addiction. H: the person depends on the drug and cannot stop easily.","F2 滥用导致成瘾。H：依赖药物，难以戒除"],["F3 Long-term alcohol damages the liver and brain. H: the liver cannot remove toxic substances, leading to liver disease.","F3 长期饮酒损害肝和脑。H：肝脏无法排毒，引发肝病"],["F4 Abuse causes accidents, crime and family problems. H: the person has poor judgement and loses control.","F4 滥用引发事故、犯罪、家庭问题。H：判断力差、失控"],["F5 Sharing needles may spread diseases such as HIV and hepatitis. H: infected blood passes from one person to another.","F5 共用针头可传播HIV和肝炎。H：带病毒的血液在人与人之间传播"]],"华文：酒驾题：反应变慢+判断力差→事故。","Tip: write the effect (F) and its reason on the nervous system (H)."],["Preventing Drug Abuse","预防药物滥用",[["Individuals: say no to drugs; take part in sports and hobbies; seek help from family or counsellors when stressed.","个人：拒绝毒品；参加运动与兴趣；有压力时向家人或辅导员求助"],["Family and school: give attention and advice; organise anti-drug campaigns and talks.","家庭和学校：关心与教导；举办反毒宣传与讲座"],["Government: enforce the law (the Dangerous Drugs Act) and run rehabilitation centres.","政府：执行法律（危险药物法令）并设立康复中心"],["Rehabilitation: counselling, medical treatment and skills training help drug addicts return to society.","康复：辅导、医疗和技能培训帮助瘾君子重返社会"]],"华文：写出至少两个层面（个人、家庭/学校、政府）。","Tip: give actions by the individual, the family and the government."],["Healthy Mind","健康的心智",[["A person with a healthy mind copes with stress, thinks positively, controls emotions and has good relationships.","心智健康者能应对压力、积极思考、控制情绪并有良好人际关系"],["Stress is the body's reaction to pressure; too much stress may cause headaches, poor sleep, anxiety or depression.","压力是身体对压力源的反应；过大可致头痛、失眠、焦虑或抑郁"],["Signs of poor mental health: always sad, loss of interest, isolating oneself, sudden mood changes.","心理不健康的迹象：长期悲伤、失去兴趣、孤立自己、情绪骤变"],["Importance: a community of people with healthy minds is productive, harmonious and has fewer social problems.","重要性：心智健康的社会更有生产力、和谐、社会问题较少"]],"华文：压力过大要及早求助。","Tip: link a healthy mind to productivity and a harmonious society."],["Keeping a Healthy Mind (F + H)","保持健康心智（F + H）",[["F1 Do regular exercise. H: exercise releases chemicals that make a person feel happy and relieve stress.","F1 规律运动。H：运动释放使人愉快的物质，缓解压力"],["F2 Get enough sleep (about 8 hours for teenagers). H: the brain and body can rest and recover.","F2 睡眠充足。H：脑与身体得以休息恢复"],["F3 Share problems with family, friends or a counsellor. H: to get support and advice so that stress does not build up.","F3 与家人朋友或辅导员倾诉。H：获得支持和建议，压力不积压"],["F4 Manage time and do hobbies or relaxation. H: to reduce pressure and stay calm.","F4 管理时间、培养兴趣、放松。H：减轻压力保持平静"],["F5 Avoid drugs and alcohol. H: they damage the nervous system and worsen mental problems.","F5 远离毒品和酒精。H：损害神经系统、加重心理问题"]],"华文：方法 + 原因，各得一分。","Tip: every method needs a reason after 'H:' to earn the second mark."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Body Coordination","示例题：试卷2 A部分（身体协调）",[["(a) [1] Name the hormone that lowers the blood glucose level. Scheme: insulin (1m).","(a)降血糖的激素：胰岛素"],["(b) [1] Name the gland that secretes this hormone. Scheme: pancreas (1m).","(b)分泌该激素的腺体：胰腺"],["(c) [2] Why does a person who lacks iodine develop goitre? Scheme: iodine is needed to make thyroxine (1m); the thyroid gland swells (1m).","(c)缺碘为何患甲状腺肿：碘用于合成甲状腺素；甲状腺肿大"],["(d) [2] State two effects of alcohol on the body. Scheme: slower reaction time (1m); poor balance / coordination / liver damage (1m).","(d)酒精的两种影响：反应变慢；平衡协调差/肝损伤"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Hormones, Drugs and Mind (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（激素、药物与心智）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how the blood glucose level is controlled after a meal. Scheme: blood glucose rises (1m); pancreas secretes insulin (1m); liver changes glucose to glycogen (1m); blood glucose falls to normal (1m).","(a)饭后血糖如何被调节"],["(b) [2] Compare the nervous system and the endocrine system. Scheme: nervous - fast response, short-lived (1m); endocrine - slower response, longer lasting (1m).","(b)比较神经系统与内分泌系统"],["(c) [KBAT] A teenager is often tired, sad and starts to take drugs to feel better. Evaluate this action and suggest two better ways. Scheme: drugs cause addiction and damage the nervous system (1m) so the problem becomes worse (1m); talk to a counsellor or family (1m) to get support (1m); do exercise (1m) to relieve stress (1m).","(c)评价吸毒并提出两种更好的方法：倾诉求助；运动"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying hormones are carried by nerves. Correct: hormones are carried by the blood; nerves carry impulses.","错误：激素由神经运送。正确：激素由血液运送"],["Mistake: mixing up insulin and glucagon. Correct: insulin lowers blood glucose; glucagon raises it.","错误：混淆胰岛素与胰高血糖素"],["Mistake: writing that alcohol is a stimulant. Correct: alcohol is a depressant that slows down the nervous system.","错误：酒精是兴奋剂。正确：酒精是抑制剂"],["Mistake: naming a disease without the hormone. Correct: goitre - lack of iodine so less thyroxine; diabetes - lack of insulin.","错误：只写病名。正确：要写出缺哪种激素/物质"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Which hormone lowers blood glucose? J: Insulin, secreted by the pancreas.","问：哪种激素降低血糖？答：胰岛素，由胰腺分泌"],["S: What causes goitre? J: Lack of iodine, so thyroxine cannot be made and the thyroid gland swells.","问：甲状腺肿的原因？答：缺碘，无法合成甲状腺素，甲状腺肿大"],["S: What does adrenaline do? J: Increases heart rate, breathing rate and blood glucose for fight or flight.","问：肾上腺素的作用？答：加快心跳、呼吸并升血糖，应对战或逃"],["S: Give one effect of alcohol on coordination. J: Slower reaction time and poor balance.","问：酒精对协调的影响？答：反应变慢、平衡差"],["S: Why is hormonal control slower than nervous control? J: Hormones are carried by the blood, while impulses travel along nerves.","问：激素调控为何较慢？答：激素靠血液运送，神经冲动沿神经传导"],["S: Give one way to keep a healthy mind. J: Exercise / enough sleep / talk to a counsellor.","问：保持健康心智的一种方法？答：运动/睡眠充足/向辅导员倾诉"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-8":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Atom: the smallest particle of an element that can take part in a chemical reaction.","原子：元素中能参与化学反应的最小粒子"],["Molecule: a particle made of two or more atoms joined together by chemical bonds. Ion: a charged particle formed when an atom gains or loses electrons.","分子：两个或以上原子结合；离子：得失电子后带电的粒子"],["Proton number: the number of protons in the nucleus of an atom. Nucleon number: the total number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus.","质子数：核内质子数；核子数：质子加中子总数"],["Electron arrangement: the number of electrons in each shell of an atom, starting from the shell nearest the nucleus.","电子排列：各电子层的电子数"],["Valence electrons: the electrons in the outermost occupied shell.","价电子：最外层电子"],["Isotopes: atoms of the same element with the same proton number but different nucleon numbers (different numbers of neutrons).","同位素：质子数相同、核子数（中子数）不同的同一元素原子"]],"华文：定义要写「相同…但不同…」。","Tip: for isotopes write both parts: same proton number, different number of neutrons."],["Atoms, Molecules and Ions","原子、分子与离子",[["Matter is made up of tiny particles: atoms, molecules or ions.","物质由原子、分子或离子组成"],["Atoms: elements such as helium, neon, argon (monoatomic), and metals such as iron and copper.","原子构成：氦、氖、氩及铁、铜等金属"],["Molecules: diatomic, e.g. \\(\\ce{O2}\\), \\(\\ce{N2}\\), \\(\\ce{H2}\\), \\(\\ce{Cl2}\\); polyatomic, e.g. \\(\\ce{H2O}\\), \\(\\ce{CO2}\\), \\(\\ce{NH3}\\).","分子：双原子如O2；多原子如H2O、CO2"],["Ions: positive ion (cation) e.g. \\(\\ce{Na+}\\), \\(\\ce{Mg^2+}\\); negative ion (anion) e.g. \\(\\ce{Cl-}\\), \\(\\ce{O^2-}\\).","离子：阳离子如Na+；阴离子如Cl-"],["Ionic compounds such as sodium chloride are made up of ions; covalent substances such as water are made up of molecules.","离子化合物由离子构成；共价物质由分子构成"]],"华文：先判断粒子类型再作答。","Tip: state the particle type: atoms, molecules or ions, with an example."],["Subatomic Particles","亚原子粒子",[["Proton: charge +1, relative mass 1, found in the nucleus.","质子：电荷+1，相对质量1，在原子核"],["Neutron: no charge (0), relative mass 1, found in the nucleus.","中子：不带电，相对质量1，在原子核"],["Electron: charge -1, negligible mass, moves around the nucleus in shells.","电子：电荷-1，质量可忽略，在电子层中绕核运动"],["The nucleus is positively charged and contains almost all the mass of the atom.","原子核带正电，几乎集中全部质量"],["In a neutral atom, number of protons = number of electrons, so the overall charge is zero.","中性原子：质子数=电子数，总电荷为零"]],"华文：质子 + 中子在核内。","Tip: when asked why an atom is neutral, write: number of protons equals number of electrons."],["Development of the Atomic Model","原子模型的发展",[["Dalton: the atom is a solid, indivisible sphere.","道尔顿：实心不可分的球"],["Thomson: the atom is a positive sphere with electrons embedded in it (plum pudding); he discovered the electron.","汤姆生：正电球中嵌着电子；发现电子"],["Rutherford: the atom has a small, dense, positively charged nucleus with electrons around it; he discovered the nucleus.","卢瑟福：小而致密带正电的原子核，电子在周围"],["Bohr: electrons move in fixed shells around the nucleus.","玻尔：电子在固定电子层中运动"],["Chadwick: discovered the neutron in the nucleus.","查德威克：发现中子"]],"华文：配对「科学家 + 贡献」。","Tip: link each scientist with one discovery or model feature."],["Proton Number and Nucleon Number","质子数与核子数",[["Proton number = number of protons = number of electrons in a neutral atom.","质子数 = 质子数 = 中性原子的电子数"],["Nucleon number = number of protons + number of neutrons.","核子数 = 质子数 + 中子数"],["Number of neutrons = nucleon number - proton number.","中子数 = 核子数 - 质子数"],["Standard notation: \\(\\ce{^{A}_{Z}X}\\), where A is the nucleon number (top) and Z is the proton number (bottom).","标准符号：A在上（核子数），Z在下（质子数）"],["Elements in the periodic table are arranged in order of increasing proton number.","元素按质子数递增排列"]],"华文：中子数 = 核子数 - 质子数。","Tip: show the working: neutrons = nucleon number - proton number."],["Worked Example: Particles in an Atom","例题：原子内的粒子",[["Question: An atom of sodium is written as \\(\\ce{^{23}_{11}Na}\\). State the number of protons, electrons and neutrons.","题：钠原子 23/11 Na，求质子、电子、中子数"],["Protons = proton number = 11. (1m)","质子数 = 11"],["Electrons = protons in a neutral atom = 11. (1m)","电子数 = 11"],["Neutrons = nucleon number - proton number = 23 - 11 = 12. (1m)","中子数 = 23 - 11 = 12"],["Another atom has 17 protons and 18 neutrons: nucleon number = 17 + 18 = 35, so it is \\(\\ce{^{35}_{17}Cl}\\). (1m)","17质子18中子：核子数35，即35/17 Cl"]],"华文：先公式，再代入，再答案。","Tip: write the formula and substitution; marks are given for the method."],["Electron Arrangement","电子排列",[["Electrons fill the shells from the one nearest the nucleus: first shell maximum 2, second shell maximum 8, third shell up to 8 for the first 20 elements.","电子由内向外填充：第一层最多2，第二层最多8，前20号元素第三层最多8"],["Duplet arrangement: 2 electrons in the first shell (helium). Octet arrangement: 8 electrons in the outer shell (neon, argon).","稳定结构：氦为2电子；氖、氩为8电子"],["Examples: H 1; He 2; C 2.4; N 2.5; O 2.6; Na 2.8.1; Mg 2.8.2; Al 2.8.3; Cl 2.8.7; Ar 2.8.8; K 2.8.8.1; Ca 2.8.8.2.","例：Na 2.8.1；Cl 2.8.7；K 2.8.8.1"],["Write the electron arrangement with full stops between the shells, e.g. 2.8.1.","电子排列用点分隔，如2.8.1"],["Draw the shells as circles around the nucleus, with the proton and neutron numbers in the nucleus.","画图：原子核写质子和中子数，外围画电子层"]],"华文：先数总电子，再逐层填。","Tip: check that the total number of electrons equals the proton number."],["The Modern Periodic Table","现代元素周期表",[["Elements are arranged in order of increasing proton number.","元素按质子数递增排列"],["Vertical columns are groups (Group 1 to 18); horizontal rows are periods (Period 1 to 7).","纵列为族（1至18族），横行为周期（1至7）"],["Elements in the same group have the same number of valence electrons, so they have similar chemical properties.","同族价电子数相同，化学性质相似"],["Metals are on the left and in the middle; non-metals are on the right; metalloids (e.g. silicon) lie between them.","金属在左和中间，非金属在右，类金属（如硅）在其间"],["Transition elements are found in Groups 3 to 12.","过渡元素在第3至12族"]],"华文：同族 = 价电子数相同。","Tip: link the group to valence electrons, and say similar chemical properties as the reason."],["Group and Period from Electron Arrangement (F + H)","由电子排列判断族与周期（F + H）",[["F1 Group number (Groups 1 and 2) = number of valence electrons; for Groups 13 to 18 the group number = valence electrons + 10. H: the valence electrons decide the chemical properties.","F1 第1、2族族数=价电子数；13至18族=价电子数+10"],["F2 Period number = number of shells occupied by electrons. H: each period starts a new shell.","F2 周期数 = 有电子的电子层数"],["F3 Example: Na 2.8.1 has 1 valence electron and 3 shells. H: it is in Group 1, Period 3.","F3 例：Na 2.8.1，1个价电子3层：第1族第3周期"],["F4 Example: Cl 2.8.7 has 7 valence electrons and 3 shells. H: it is in Group 17, Period 3.","F4 例：Cl 2.8.7：第17族第3周期"]],"华文：族看价电子，周期看层数。","Tip: write the number of valence electrons and the number of shells to support the group and period."],["Group 18: The Noble Gases","第18族：稀有气体",[["Group 18 elements: helium, neon, argon, krypton, xenon, radon.","第18族：氦、氖、氩、氪、氙、氡"],["They have a stable duplet (helium) or octet electron arrangement, so they do not gain, lose or share electrons.","具稳定的2或8电子结构，不得失或共用电子"],["Therefore they are chemically unreactive (inert) and exist as monoatomic gases.","因此化学性质不活泼，以单原子气体存在"],["Uses: helium in weather balloons and airships; neon in advertising lights; argon in filament light bulbs.","用途：氦用于气球；氖用于广告灯；氩用于灯泡"],["Argon is used in light bulbs because it is unreactive and prevents the hot tungsten filament from reacting with oxygen.","灯泡用氩：不活泼，防止灯丝与氧气反应"]],"华文：不活泼的原因 = 稳定电子排列。","Tip: reason first (stable electron arrangement), then the use."],["Formation of Ions","离子的形成",[["Atoms form ions to achieve a stable duplet or octet electron arrangement like a noble gas.","原子形成离子以达到稀有气体般的稳定结构"],["Metal atoms lose valence electrons to form positive ions (cations): \\(\\ce{Na -> Na+ + e-}\\); \\(\\ce{Mg -> Mg^2+ + 2e-}\\).","金属失去价电子形成阳离子"],["Non-metal atoms gain electrons to form negative ions (anions): \\(\\ce{Cl + e- -> Cl-}\\); \\(\\ce{O + 2e- -> O^2-}\\).","非金属得到电子形成阴离子"],["The number of protons does not change, so a positive ion has more protons than electrons and a negative ion has more electrons than protons.","质子数不变：阳离子质子多于电子；阴离子电子多于质子"],["The ion has the same electron arrangement as the nearest noble gas, e.g. \\(\\ce{Na+}\\) is 2.8 like neon.","离子电子排列与最近的稀有气体相同，如Na+为2.8"]],"华文：金属失，非金属得。","Tip: state the electron arrangement before and after, and the charge of the ion."],["Why Atoms Form Ions (F + H)","原子为何形成离子（F + H）",[["F1 A sodium atom (2.8.1) loses 1 electron. H: it achieves a stable octet arrangement (2.8) and becomes \\(\\ce{Na+}\\).","F1 钠失去1个电子。H：达到稳定八隅体，成为Na+"],["F2 A chlorine atom (2.8.7) gains 1 electron. H: it achieves a stable octet arrangement (2.8.8) and becomes \\(\\ce{Cl-}\\).","F2 氯得到1个电子。H：达到2.8.8，成为Cl-"],["F3 Metal atoms have few valence electrons. H: it is easier to lose them than to gain many electrons.","F3 金属价电子少。H：失去比得到多个电子容易"],["F4 Non-metal atoms have nearly full outer shells. H: it is easier to gain electrons to complete the shell.","F4 非金属外层接近满。H：得电子补满更容易"]],"华文：得失电子的目的 = 稳定。","Tip: always include the words stable octet (or duplet) arrangement as the reason."],["Worked Example: Ion Formation","例题：离子的形成",[["Question: Magnesium has proton number 12. Show how a magnesium atom forms a magnesium ion.","题：镁质子数12，写出镁离子形成过程"],["Electron arrangement of the Mg atom = 2.8.2 (12 electrons). (1m)","镁原子电子排列 2.8.2"],["The atom loses 2 valence electrons to achieve the stable octet arrangement 2.8. (1m)","失去2个价电子，达到稳定2.8"],["Ion formed: \\(\\ce{Mg^2+}\\) with 12 protons and 10 electrons. (1m)","形成Mg2+：12质子、10电子"],["Similarly, oxygen (proton number 8, arrangement 2.6) gains 2 electrons to form \\(\\ce{O^2-}\\) with arrangement 2.8. (1m)","同理氧（2.6）得2电子形成O2-（2.8）"]],"华文：写出前后电子排列。","Tip: give the number of protons and electrons in the ion to show the charge."],["Isotopes","同位素",[["Isotopes are atoms of the same element with the same proton number but different nucleon numbers.","同位素：质子数相同、核子数不同"],["They have a different number of neutrons.","中子数不同"],["Examples: hydrogen-1, hydrogen-2 and hydrogen-3; carbon-12 (6 protons, 6 neutrons) and carbon-14 (6 protons, 8 neutrons); chlorine-35 and chlorine-37.","例：氢-1、-2、-3；碳-12与碳-14；氯-35与氯-37"],["Isotopes have the same chemical properties because they have the same electron arrangement and valence electrons.","化学性质相同：电子排列和价电子数相同"],["Isotopes have different physical properties, such as mass and density, because they have different numbers of neutrons.","物理性质不同（质量、密度）：中子数不同"]],"华文：化学性质同，物理性质异。","Tip: explain same chemical properties by same number of valence electrons."],["Worked Example: Isotopes","例题：同位素",[["Question: Atom X has 17 protons and 18 neutrons; atom Y has 17 protons and 20 neutrons. Are X and Y isotopes?","题：X 17质子18中子；Y 17质子20中子，是否同位素？"],["Nucleon number of X = 17 + 18 = 35; nucleon number of Y = 17 + 20 = 37. (1m)","X核子数35；Y核子数37"],["Both have the same proton number (17) but different nucleon numbers (35 and 37). (1m)","质子数同为17，核子数不同"],["Answer: yes, X and Y are isotopes of chlorine. (1m)","答案：是，同为氯的同位素"],["The two isotopes have the same electron arrangement 2.8.7, so they have the same chemical properties. (1m)","电子排列同为2.8.7，化学性质相同"]],"华文：先算核子数再比较。","Tip: show the nucleon number of each atom before concluding."],["Uses of Isotopes (F + H)","同位素的用途（F + H）",[["F1 Carbon-14 is used to estimate the age of fossils and archaeological finds. H: it decays at a known rate, so the remaining amount shows the age.","F1 碳-14用于测定化石年代。H：衰变速率已知"],["F2 Iodine-131 is used to diagnose and treat thyroid disorders. H: the thyroid gland absorbs iodine, so the radiation acts on that gland.","F2 碘-131用于甲状腺。H：甲状腺吸收碘"],["F3 Cobalt-60 is used in radiotherapy and to sterilise medical equipment. H: gamma rays kill cancer cells and bacteria.","F3 钴-60用于放射治疗和消毒。H：伽马射线杀死癌细胞和细菌"],["F4 Uranium-235 is used as nuclear fuel in power stations. H: it releases a large amount of energy during nuclear fission.","F4 铀-235作核燃料。H：核裂变释放大量能量"]],"华文：用途 + 原因。","Tip: name the isotope, its use, and the reason in one sentence each."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Elements and Atomic Structure","示例题：试卷2 A部分（元素与原子结构）",[["(a) [1] What is the nucleon number of an atom? Scheme: total number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus (1m).","(a)核子数：核内质子和中子总数"],["(b) [3] An atom of element Q has proton number 13 and nucleon number 27. State the number of neutrons and the electron arrangement; state its group. Scheme: 27 - 13 = 14 neutrons (1m); 2.8.3 (1m); Group 13 (1m).","(b)中子14；电子排列2.8.3；第13族"],["(c) [2] Why is argon used to fill light bulbs? Scheme: argon is unreactive / inert (1m); prevents the filament from reacting with oxygen (1m).","(c)灯泡充氩：不活泼；防止灯丝氧化"],["(d) [2] Chlorine-35 and chlorine-37 are isotopes. State two ways in which they are the same. Scheme: same proton number (1m); same electron arrangement / chemical properties (1m).","(d)Cl-35与Cl-37相同之处：质子数；电子排列"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Ions and Isotopes (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（离子与同位素）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how a sodium atom (proton number 11) and a chlorine atom (proton number 17) form ions. Scheme: Na is 2.8.1 and loses 1 electron (1m) to achieve stable octet, forming Na+ (1m); Cl is 2.8.7 and gains 1 electron (1m) to achieve stable octet, forming Cl- (1m).","(a)Na和Cl形成离子的过程"],["(b) [3] Compare carbon-12 and carbon-14. Scheme: both have 6 protons (1m); carbon-12 has 6 neutrons, carbon-14 has 8 neutrons (1m); same chemical properties but different mass (1m).","(b)比较碳-12与碳-14"],["(c) [KBAT] A museum wants to know the age of an ancient wooden tool. Suggest the isotope and justify your choice. Scheme: carbon-14 (1m); it is present in living things and decays at a known rate (1m); compare the remaining amount with the amount in living wood to estimate the age (1m).","(c)测定古木器年代：选碳-14，衰变速率已知，比较剩余量"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: writing that isotopes have different proton numbers. Correct: same proton number, different number of neutrons.","错误：同位素质子数不同。正确：质子数相同，中子数不同"],["Mistake: using the nucleon number as the number of protons. Correct: protons = proton number; neutrons = nucleon number - proton number.","错误：把核子数当质子数"],["Mistake: saying a metal atom gains electrons to form a positive ion. Correct: metals lose electrons to form positive ions.","错误：金属得电子成阳离子。正确：金属失电子"],["Mistake: writing the electron arrangement as 2,8,1 or without checking the total. Correct: 2.8.1 and the total equals the proton number.","错误：排列不核对总数。正确：总数等于质子数"],["Mistake: saying noble gases are unreactive because they are gases. Correct: because of the stable duplet or octet arrangement.","错误：稀有气体不活泼因为是气体。正确：因稳定电子排列"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is the electron arrangement of sodium (proton number 11)? J: 2.8.1.","问：钠（质子数11）的电子排列？答：2.8.1"],["S: What is an isotope? J: Atoms of the same element with the same proton number but different number of neutrons.","问：什么是同位素？答：质子数相同、中子数不同的同一元素原子"],["S: How does a chlorine atom become a chloride ion? J: It gains one electron to achieve a stable octet arrangement.","问：Cl如何变成Cl-？答：得到一个电子，达到稳定八隅体"],["S: How do you find the number of neutrons? J: Nucleon number minus proton number.","问：如何求中子数？答：核子数减质子数"],["S: Which group and period is an atom with arrangement 2.8.2 in? J: Group 2, Period 3.","问：电子排列2.8.2的原子在哪一族哪一周期？答：第2族第3周期"],["S: Which isotope is used to date fossils? J: Carbon-14.","问：哪种同位素用于测定化石年代？答：碳-14"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-9":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Alloy: a mixture of a metal with one or more other elements (metal or non-metal) in a fixed proportion.","合金：金属与其他元素按一定比例混合"],["Glass: a hard, transparent, brittle material made by heating silica (silicon dioxide) with other substances and then cooling it.","玻璃：硅砂与其他物质加热后冷却制成"],["Ceramic: a hard, brittle, heat-resistant material made from clay (or other inorganic compounds) that is shaped and fired at high temperature.","陶瓷：黏土等成型后高温烧制"],["Monomer: a small molecule that joins with many others. Polymer: a long-chain molecule made from many monomers joined together.","单体：小分子；聚合物：许多单体连成的长链分子"],["Polymerisation: the process of joining many monomers to form a polymer.","聚合反应：单体连接成聚合物"],["Vulcanisation: the process of heating natural rubber with sulphur to form sulphur cross-links between the rubber chains.","硫化：橡胶加硫加热，链间形成硫交联"]],"华文：定义要写关键词：mixture、silica、clay、monomer、cross-links。","Tip: an alloy is a mixture, not a compound; write 'mixture of a metal with another element'."],["Alloys: Composition and Uses","合金：成分与用途",[["Brass: copper + zinc; used for musical instruments, door handles, taps.","黄铜：铜+锌；乐器、门把手、水龙头"],["Bronze: copper + tin; used for statues, medals, bells.","青铜：铜+锡；雕像、奖牌、钟"],["Steel: iron + carbon; used for building structures, bridges, vehicle bodies.","钢：铁+碳；建筑结构、桥梁、车身"],["Stainless steel: iron + carbon + chromium + nickel; used for cutlery, surgical instruments, sinks.","不锈钢：铁+碳+铬+镍；餐具、手术器械、水槽"],["Duralumin: aluminium + copper + magnesium + manganese; light and strong, used in aircraft bodies.","硬铝：铝+铜+镁+锰；轻而强，用于飞机机身"],["Pewter: tin + antimony + copper; used for souvenirs, decorative items and tankards.","锡镴：锡+锑+铜；纪念品、装饰品"]],"华文：每种合金背「成分 + 用途」。","Tip: when asked to name an alloy, give its composition too, e.g. 'brass: copper and zinc'."],["Properties of Alloys Compared with Pure Metals","合金与纯金属的性质比较",[["Alloys are harder and stronger than pure metals.","合金比纯金属更硬更强"],["Alloys are more resistant to corrosion (rusting) than pure metals.","合金更耐腐蚀"],["Alloys have a better appearance (shiny, attractive) and a lower melting point in some cases.","合金外观更好，有些熔点更低"],["Pure metals are soft and ductile because the layers of identical atoms slide easily over each other when a force is applied.","纯金属软且有延展性：相同原子层易滑动"],["In an alloy, atoms of other elements have different sizes and disturb the orderly arrangement of atoms.","合金中其他原子大小不同，打乱原子排列"],["The layers of atoms cannot slide easily over each other, so the alloy is harder and stronger.","原子层不易滑动，所以更硬更强"]],"华文：合金变硬的原因一定要写「不同大小原子」+「阻止滑动」。","Tip: always include 'atoms of different sizes' and 'prevent layers of atoms from sliding' to get both marks."],["Explain: Why Alloys Are Harder (F + H)","解释：合金为何更硬（F + H）",[["F1 Pure metal atoms are all the same size and arranged in orderly layers. H: the layers slide easily over each other when a force is applied, so a pure metal is soft.","F1 纯金属原子大小相同、排列整齐。H：受力时层易滑动，所以软"],["F2 An alloy contains atoms of other elements of different sizes. H: they disturb the orderly arrangement of the atoms in the pure metal.","F2 合金含大小不同的其他原子。H：扰乱原子排列"],["F3 The layers of atoms in an alloy cannot slide easily. H: more force is needed to deform it, so the alloy is harder and stronger.","F3 合金原子层不易滑动。H：需要更大力才变形，所以更硬更强"],["F4 Stainless steel contains chromium. H: chromium forms a protective oxide layer that prevents iron from rusting.","F4 不锈钢含铬。H：铬形成保护氧化层，防止铁生锈"]],"华文：F 是事实，H 是原因，各 1 分。","Tip: use the structure 'different sizes -> disturb arrangement -> layers cannot slide -> harder'."],["Experiment: Hardness of Pure Metal and Alloy","实验：纯金属与合金的硬度",[["Aim: to compare the hardness of a pure metal (copper) and its alloy (brass / bronze).","目的：比较铜与其合金的硬度"],["Problem statement: is an alloy harder than its pure metal? Hypothesis: the alloy is harder than the pure metal, so the dent made is smaller.","问题：合金是否比纯金属更硬？假设：合金更硬，凹痕更小"],["Variables: Manipulated: type of block (copper / brass). Responding: diameter of the dent. Fixed: mass of the steel ball, height it is dropped from, size of the blocks.","变量：操纵：金属块种类；响应：凹痕直径；固定：钢珠质量、下落高度、金属块大小"],["Apparatus and materials: copper block, brass block, steel ball bearing, retort stand with clamp, plasticine/tube guide, ruler (or vernier calliper).","仪器材料：铜块、黄铜块、钢珠、铁架夹、尺或游标卡尺"],["Procedure: (1) place the copper block under the retort stand; (2) hold the steel ball at a fixed height (e.g. 50 cm) and release it onto the block; (3) measure the diameter of the dent; (4) repeat with the brass block using the same ball and height.","步骤：钢珠从固定高度落在铜块，量凹痕直径；用黄铜块重复"],["Observation: the dent on the copper block is bigger than the dent on the brass block. Conclusion: brass (alloy) is harder than copper (pure metal); hypothesis accepted.","观察：铜块凹痕更大。结论：黄铜比铜更硬，假设成立"]],"华文：看凹痕大小，凹痕越小越硬。","Tip: write 'the smaller the diameter of the dent, the harder the material' and name all three variables."],["Glass: Composition, Types and Uses","玻璃：成分、种类与用途",[["Main component of glass: silica (silicon dioxide, from sand).","玻璃主要成分：二氧化硅（硅砂）"],["Soda-lime glass: silica + sodium carbonate (soda ash) + calcium carbonate (limestone); cheap, easily shaped; used for bottles, windows, light bulbs.","钠钙玻璃：硅砂+纯碱+石灰石；瓶子、窗、灯泡"],["Borosilicate glass: silica + boron oxide; resists sudden temperature change, heat-resistant; used for laboratory apparatus, ovenware.","硼硅玻璃：硅砂+氧化硼；耐热、耐骤变温度；实验仪器、烤箱用具"],["Lead crystal glass: silica + lead(II) oxide; high refractive index, sparkles, heavy; used for decorative items and expensive glassware.","铅晶玻璃：含氧化铅；折射率高，闪亮；装饰品"],["Fused glass (pure silica): very high melting point, can withstand high temperature; used for optical fibres, lenses, telescopes.","熔融玻璃（纯硅砂）：熔点高；光纤、透镜、望远镜"],["Photochromic glass: darkens in bright light; used in sunglasses.","光致变色玻璃：强光下变暗；太阳镜"]],"华文：每种玻璃背「成分 + 特性 + 用途」。","Tip: for 'name a glass and give its use' write type + property + use, e.g. 'borosilicate glass, heat-resistant, laboratory apparatus'."],["Properties of Glass and Why It Is Useful","玻璃的性质与用途理由",[["Transparent: allows light to pass through, used for windows and lenses.","透明：光能通过，用于窗和镜片"],["Hard but brittle: breaks easily when hit; can be made stronger by adding other substances or by laminating.","硬但脆：易碎；可加其他物质或夹层增强"],["Chemically inert (unreactive): does not react with most chemicals, so it is used to store food, drinks and chemicals.","化学惰性：不与多数化学品反应，用于盛装食物和化学品"],["Poor conductor of heat and electricity: used as an insulator.","热和电的不良导体：用作绝缘体"],["Can be moulded into any shape when hot; can be recycled.","加热时可塑形；可回收"]],"华文：玻璃不导电、不反应、透明。","Tip: link the property to the use, e.g. 'unreactive, so it does not contaminate the chemicals stored'."],["Ceramics: Types, Properties and Uses","陶瓷：种类、性质与用途",[["Traditional ceramics: made from clay and shaped then fired at high temperature; used for tiles, bricks, plates, cups, toilets.","传统陶瓷：黏土烧制；砖瓦、碟、杯、马桶"],["Engineering (advanced) ceramics: made from pure compounds such as silicon carbide and alumina; used for engine parts, cutting tools, spacecraft tiles.","工程陶瓷：碳化硅、氧化铝等；引擎零件、切削工具、航天隔热瓦"],["Properties: very hard, strong under compression, high melting point (heat-resistant).","性质：很硬，抗压，熔点高（耐热）"],["Properties: chemically inert and does not corrode; poor conductor of heat and electricity (insulator).","性质：化学惰性、不腐蚀；热电不良导体"],["Weakness: brittle; breaks or cracks when hit or when dropped.","缺点：脆，受撞或掉落会裂"]],"华文：陶瓷=硬、耐热、绝缘、脆。","Tip: state one property and its use together, e.g. 'high melting point, used for spacecraft heat-shield tiles'."],["Explain: Glass and Ceramic Uses (F + H)","解释：玻璃与陶瓷的用途（F + H）",[["F1 Borosilicate glass is used to make laboratory apparatus. H: it is heat-resistant and does not crack when heated or cooled suddenly.","F1 硼硅玻璃做实验仪器。H：耐热，骤冷骤热不裂"],["F2 Ceramics are used to make electrical insulators for power lines. H: ceramics are poor conductors of electricity and do not corrode.","F2 陶瓷做电线绝缘体。H：不导电且不腐蚀"],["F3 Glass is used to store food and chemicals. H: glass is chemically inert, so it does not react with the contents.","F3 玻璃盛装食物化学品。H：化学惰性，不与内容物反应"],["F4 Ceramic tiles cover the surface of a spacecraft. H: ceramics have a very high melting point and are poor heat conductors, so they protect the craft from heat.","F4 陶瓷瓦覆盖航天器。H：熔点高、导热差，保护航天器"]],"华文：先说用途，再说性质原因。","Tip: 'used for X (1m) because it is Y (1m)'."],["Polymers: Natural and Synthetic","聚合物：天然与合成",[["Polymer: long chain made of many repeating monomers joined by polymerisation.","聚合物：许多重复单体连接成的长链"],["Natural polymers: starch (monomer: glucose), protein (monomer: amino acid), cellulose, natural rubber (monomer: isoprene).","天然聚合物：淀粉（葡萄糖）、蛋白质（氨基酸）、纤维素、天然橡胶（异戊二烯）"],["Synthetic polymers: polyethene (monomer: ethene), polypropene, polyvinyl chloride (PVC), polystyrene, nylon, perspex (acrylic).","合成聚合物：聚乙烯、聚丙烯、PVC、聚苯乙烯、尼龙、有机玻璃"],["Polyethene: plastic bags, bottles. PVC: pipes, raincoats, cable cover. Polystyrene: food containers, packaging foam. Nylon: ropes, fishing lines, clothes. Perspex: transparent lenses, signboards.","聚乙烯：塑料袋；PVC：水管、雨衣；聚苯乙烯：食物盒、泡沫；尼龙：绳、鱼线；有机玻璃：透明板"],["Addition polymerisation: many ethene molecules join to form polyethene, with no other product.","加聚反应：许多乙烯分子连成聚乙烯，无其他产物"]],"华文：知道单体与聚合物的对应。","Tip: write the monomer when asked about a polymer, e.g. 'ethene is the monomer of polyethene'."],["Properties and Problems of Synthetic Polymers","合成聚合物的性质与问题",[["Synthetic polymers are light, strong, cheap, easily moulded into any shape and can be coloured.","合成聚合物：轻、强、便宜、易塑形、可上色"],["They are poor conductors of electricity and heat, and unreactive towards water, acids and alkalis.","不良导体，不与水、酸、碱反应"],["Problem: most are non-biodegradable, so they remain in the environment for a long time and cause pollution and blocked drains.","问题：多数不可生物降解，长期留在环境造成污染和堵塞"],["Problem: burning plastics releases toxic gases and causes air pollution.","问题：燃烧塑料释放有毒气体污染空气"],["Solution: reduce, reuse, recycle (3R); use biodegradable polymers made from starch.","解决：减少、再用、回收；使用淀粉制可降解塑料"]],"华文：写问题时要说明原因（不可降解、释放毒气）。","Tip: give the problem AND the reason AND the solution (3R) in an essay."],["Rubber: Latex and Coagulation","橡胶：乳胶与凝固",[["Natural rubber is obtained from latex, the white liquid tapped from rubber trees (Hevea brasiliensis).","天然橡胶取自橡胶树乳胶"],["Natural rubber is a polymer of isoprene; the long chains are coiled and can be stretched.","天然橡胶是异戊二烯聚合物，长链卷曲可拉伸"],["Latex coagulates when an acid (e.g. ethanoic acid, methanoic acid) is added.","加酸（乙酸、甲酸）使乳胶凝固"],["Latex stays liquid (does not coagulate) when an alkali such as ammonia solution is added, because the alkali neutralises the acid produced by bacteria.","加碱（氨水）乳胶不凝固：碱中和细菌产生的酸"],["Coagulated latex is pressed into sheets, washed and dried to make rubber sheets.","凝固乳胶压成片、洗净、干燥成橡胶片"]],"华文：酸使乳胶凝固，氨水防止凝固。","Tip: acid = coagulate; ammonia (alkali) = prevent coagulation; write both with the reason."],["Vulcanised Rubber and Synthetic Rubber","硫化橡胶与合成橡胶",[["Natural rubber is soft and sticky, becomes weak when heated and is not very elastic after repeated stretching.","天然橡胶软、黏，受热变弱，反复拉伸弹性变差"],["Vulcanisation: natural rubber is heated with sulphur; sulphur atoms form cross-links between the rubber chains.","硫化：橡胶加硫加热，硫原子在链间形成交联"],["Vulcanised rubber is harder, stronger, more elastic, more durable and more heat-resistant, and returns to its shape after stretching.","硫化橡胶更硬、更强、更有弹性、更耐用耐热"],["Cross-links prevent the rubber chains from sliding over each other, so the rubber returns to its original shape.","交联阻止橡胶链滑动，所以能恢复原状"],["Synthetic rubber (e.g. styrene-butadiene, neoprene): more resistant to heat, oil, chemicals and ageing; used for tyres, hoses, seals.","合成橡胶：更耐热、油、化学品；轮胎、胶管、密封圈"],["Uses of vulcanised rubber: tyres, shoe soles, gloves, rubber bands, conveyor belts.","硫化橡胶用途：轮胎、鞋底、手套、橡皮筋"]],"华文：硫化关键词：sulphur cross-links。","Tip: mention 'sulphur', 'cross-links' and 'elastic' in a vulcanisation answer."],["Explain: Vulcanisation and Rubber (F + H)","解释：硫化与橡胶（F + H）",[["F1 Vulcanised rubber is harder and more elastic than natural rubber. H: sulphur cross-links form between the rubber chains and stop them from sliding past each other.","F1 硫化橡胶更硬更有弹性。H：硫交联阻止链滑动"],["F2 Tyres are made of vulcanised rubber. H: it is strong, durable and heat-resistant, so it does not wear out or soften easily on the road.","F2 轮胎用硫化橡胶。H：强、耐用、耐热，不易磨损变软"],["F3 Ammonia solution is added to latex in a container. H: it neutralises the acid produced by bacteria and prevents the latex from coagulating.","F3 乳胶加氨水。H：中和细菌产生的酸，防止凝固"],["F4 Gloves for handling chemicals are made of rubber. H: rubber is elastic and does not conduct electricity or react with many chemicals.","F4 手套用橡胶。H：有弹性、不导电、不与多种化学品反应"]],"华文：先写结论 F，再写原因 H。","Tip: always write 'sulphur cross-links' as the H for vulcanisation."],["Experiment: Vulcanised and Unvulcanised Rubber","实验：硫化与未硫化橡胶",[["Aim: to compare the elasticity of vulcanised and unvulcanised rubber strips.","目的：比较硫化与未硫化橡胶条的弹性"],["Hypothesis: vulcanised rubber is more elastic than unvulcanised rubber, so it returns closer to its original length.","假设：硫化橡胶更有弹性，更接近恢复原长"],["Variables: Manipulated: type of rubber (vulcanised / unvulcanised). Responding: length of the rubber strip after the load is removed. Fixed: size of the strips, mass of the load, time of hanging.","变量：操纵：橡胶种类；响应：卸下重物后长度；固定：橡胶条大小、重物质量、悬挂时间"],["Apparatus and materials: two rubber strips of the same size, retort stand, weights, ruler.","仪器材料：两条同样大小的橡胶条、铁架、砝码、尺"],["Procedure: (1) measure the original length of each strip; (2) hang the same load on each strip for the same time; (3) remove the load and measure the length; (4) calculate the difference from the original length.","步骤：量原长；挂相同重物相同时间；卸重物量长度；计算与原长之差"],["Observation: the vulcanised strip returns almost to its original length; the unvulcanised strip stays longer. Conclusion: vulcanised rubber is more elastic; hypothesis accepted.","观察：硫化橡胶几乎恢复原长；结论：硫化橡胶更有弹性"]],"华文：延长越小，弹性越好。","Tip: write all three variable types and use 'higher/smaller than' comparison in the conclusion."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Materials in Industry","示例题：试卷2 A部分（工业材料）",[["(a) [1] Name the alloy made from copper and zinc. Scheme: brass (1m).","(a)黄铜"],["(b) [2] Explain why an alloy is harder than a pure metal. Scheme: atoms of different sizes disturb the arrangement of atoms (1m); layers of atoms cannot slide easily (1m).","(b)合金更硬：原子大小不同；层不易滑动"],["(c) [2] Name the glass used to make laboratory beakers and give a reason. Scheme: borosilicate glass (1m); heat-resistant (1m).","(c)烧杯：硼硅玻璃；耐热"],["(d) [2] State the monomer of polyethene and the name of the process. Scheme: ethene (1m); (addition) polymerisation (1m).","(d)聚乙烯单体：乙烯；聚合反应"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Vulcanisation and Alloys (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（硫化与合金）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how vulcanisation improves natural rubber. Scheme: heated with sulphur (1m); sulphur cross-links form between the rubber chains (1m); chains cannot slide over each other (1m); rubber is harder / more elastic / more durable (1m).","(a)硫化如何改良橡胶"],["(b) [4] Describe an experiment to compare the hardness of brass and copper. Scheme: manipulated: type of metal (1m); responding: diameter of dent (1m); fixed: mass of ball and height (1m); procedure and conclusion: smaller dent = harder (1m).","(b)比较黄铜与铜的硬度的实验"],["(c) [KBAT] A company wants to make a bicycle frame that is strong, light and does not rust. Suggest a suitable material and justify. Scheme: duralumin / aluminium alloy (1m); strong and light (1m); resistant to corrosion (1m).","(c)自行车架：硬铝合金；强而轻、耐腐蚀"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying an alloy is a compound. Correct: an alloy is a mixture of a metal with another element.","错误：说合金是化合物。正确：合金是混合物"],["Mistake: writing only 'atoms are different' for hardness of alloys. Correct: atoms of different sizes prevent the layers from sliding.","错误：只写原子不同。正确：大小不同的原子阻止层滑动"],["Mistake: saying vulcanisation uses oxygen or acid. Correct: rubber is heated with sulphur to form cross-links.","错误：说硫化用氧或酸。正确：用硫加热形成交联"],["Mistake: saying acid prevents coagulation of latex. Correct: acid causes coagulation; ammonia solution prevents it.","错误：说酸防止凝固。正确：酸使凝固，氨水防止"],["Mistake: saying ceramic is a good conductor or flexible. Correct: ceramic is hard and brittle, and an insulator.","错误：说陶瓷导电或柔软。正确：硬、脆、绝缘"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Name the composition of brass and bronze. J: Brass: copper and zinc; bronze: copper and tin.","问：黄铜与青铜成分？答：黄铜：铜+锌；青铜：铜+锡"],["S: Why are alloys harder than pure metals? J: Atoms of different sizes disturb the arrangement and the layers cannot slide easily.","问：合金为何更硬？答：原子大小不同，层不易滑动"],["S: Which glass is heat-resistant and what is its use? J: Borosilicate glass; laboratory apparatus.","问：耐热玻璃及用途？答：硼硅玻璃；实验仪器"],["S: State two properties of ceramics. J: Hard and heat-resistant (also brittle, insulator).","问：陶瓷两个性质？答：硬、耐热（也脆、绝缘）"],["S: What is the monomer of polyethene? J: Ethene.","问：聚乙烯单体？答：乙烯"],["S: What happens during vulcanisation? J: Rubber is heated with sulphur and sulphur cross-links form between the chains.","问：硫化过程？答：橡胶加硫加热，链间形成硫交联"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-10":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Medicine: a substance used to prevent, treat or cure a disease or reduce its symptoms.","药物：用于预防、治疗疾病或减轻症状的物质"],["Traditional medicine: medicine from natural sources (plants, animals, minerals) based on knowledge and experience passed down through generations.","传统药物：来自天然资源，凭世代经验传承"],["Modern medicine: medicine produced using scientific research and tested in clinical trials; the dose is exact.","现代药物：经科学研究与临床试验，剂量精确"],["Complementary medicine: treatment used together with modern medicine to help recovery, e.g. acupuncture and aromatherapy.","辅助疗法：与现代药物并用帮助康复"],["Free radical: an atom or molecule that is unstable and very reactive because it has an unpaired electron.","自由基：带不成对电子、不稳定且很活泼的原子/分子"],["Antioxidant: a substance that donates electrons to free radicals to neutralise them and prevent oxidation damage.","抗氧化剂：供给电子给自由基使其稳定，防止氧化损伤"]],"华文：定义关键词：unpaired electron、donate electrons。","Tip: free radical = unpaired electron; antioxidant = donates electron. Write both keywords."],["Types of Medicine: Traditional, Modern, Complementary","药物种类：传统、现代、辅助",[["Traditional medicine: herbs such as tongkat ali, kacip fatimah and ginger; the dose is not exact and the effect is not always tested scientifically.","传统药物：东革阿里、法蒂玛草、姜；剂量不精确，疗效未必经科学验证"],["Modern medicine: tablets, capsules, syrup, injection; the active ingredient is known and the dose is exact.","现代药物：片剂、胶囊、糖浆、注射；成分明确、剂量精确"],["Complementary medicine: acupuncture, massage, aromatherapy, reflexology; used to support (not replace) modern treatment.","辅助疗法：针灸、按摩、芳香疗法、足底按摩；辅助而非取代现代治疗"],["Modern medicine is tested through research and clinical trials before it is sold.","现代药物上市前须经研究和临床试验"],["Traditional and complementary medicine should be used from registered, safe sources.","传统与辅助药物应选用注册、安全的来源"]],"华文：比较三类：来源、证据、剂量。","Tip: when comparing, use pairs: 'traditional: natural source, experience; modern: scientific research, exact dose'."],["Modern Medicine and Their Uses","现代药物及其用途",[["Analgesic: relieves pain without making the patient unconscious, e.g. paracetamol, aspirin.","止痛药：减轻疼痛，如扑热息痛、阿司匹林"],["Antibiotic: kills or stops the growth of bacteria, e.g. penicillin; it does not work against viruses.","抗生素：杀死或抑制细菌，如青霉素；对病毒无效"],["Antifungal: treats fungal infections such as athlete's foot and ringworm.","抗真菌药：治疗脚癣、癣等真菌感染"],["Antiviral: reduces the effect of virus infections, e.g. medicines for influenza.","抗病毒药：减轻病毒感染，如流感药物"],["Antihistamine: reduces allergic reactions such as sneezing, itching and rashes.","抗组胺药：减轻过敏反应，如打喷嚏、瘙痒、皮疹"]],"华文：药物名称对应功能。","Tip: match the medicine with its function; never write that an antibiotic cures flu (virus)."],["Correct Use of Medicine and Side Effects","药物的正确使用与副作用",[["Follow the doctor's or pharmacist's instructions on the dose, time and duration.","遵照医生/药剂师的剂量、时间、疗程"],["Read the label: name, dosage, expiry date, storage, side effects.","阅读标签：名称、剂量、有效期、储存、副作用"],["Finish the whole course of antibiotics, even if the symptoms disappear.","即使症状消失，也要吃完整个抗生素疗程"],["Do not share medicine and do not take medicine that has expired.","不可与他人共用药物，不可服用过期药"],["Misuse or overdose of medicine can cause side effects (e.g. drowsiness, allergy), poisoning and addiction.","滥用或过量会造成副作用（昏睡、过敏）、中毒和上瘾"],["Store medicine in a cool dry place, out of reach of children.","药物存放于阴凉干燥处，远离儿童"]],"华文：用药规则都要写原因。","Tip: give the rule + reason, e.g. 'finish the antibiotics to kill all bacteria'."],["Explain: Antibiotics and Medicine Use (F + H)","解释：抗生素与用药（F + H）",[["F1 A patient must complete the full course of antibiotics. H: if stopped early, some bacteria survive and may become resistant to the antibiotic.","F1 须吃完抗生素疗程。H：中途停药，部分细菌存活并可能产生抗药性"],["F2 Antibiotics are not given for flu. H: flu is caused by a virus and antibiotics only act on bacteria.","F2 流感不用抗生素。H：流感由病毒引起，抗生素只作用于细菌"],["F3 Medicine must be taken at the dose stated. H: an overdose may cause poisoning and side effects.","F3 须按剂量服药。H：过量会中毒、出现副作用"],["F4 Medicine must be kept in a cool dry place away from children. H: heat and moisture spoil the medicine and children may swallow it by mistake.","F4 药物放阴凉干燥处并远离儿童。H：热和湿会使药变质，儿童可能误服"]],"华文：F 是做法，H 是原因。","Tip: antibiotic resistance = bacteria survive and become resistant; write this phrase."],["Free Radicals: Sources and Effects","自由基：来源与影响",[["A free radical has an unpaired electron, so it is unstable and reacts with other molecules to take electrons from them.","自由基有不成对电子，不稳定，会抢走其他分子的电子"],["Sources: cigarette smoke, air pollution, UV radiation from sunlight, processed and fried food, stress.","来源：香烟烟雾、空气污染、紫外线、加工/油炸食物、压力"],["Free radicals damage cell membranes, proteins and DNA in a process called oxidation.","自由基通过氧化作用损伤细胞膜、蛋白质和 DNA"],["Effects: faster ageing (wrinkles), and a higher risk of cancer, heart disease and other chronic diseases.","影响：加速衰老（皱纹），增加癌症、心脏病等慢性病风险"],["Oxidation also causes cut fruit to turn brown and fats to turn rancid.","氧化也使切开的水果变褐、油脂变臭"]],"华文：自由基「抢电子」造成氧化损伤。","Tip: link the cause and the effect: 'free radical takes electron -> cell damaged -> ageing / disease'."],["Antioxidants: Types and Sources","抗氧化剂：种类与来源",[["An antioxidant donates an electron to a free radical, so the free radical becomes stable and the cells are protected.","抗氧化剂给自由基电子，使其稳定，保护细胞"],["Natural antioxidants: vitamin C (citrus fruits, guava), vitamin E (nuts, vegetable oil), beta-carotene (carrot, papaya), flavonoids (tea, berries).","天然抗氧化剂：维生素 C、E、β-胡萝卜素、类黄酮"],["Synthetic antioxidants: BHA and BHT, added to food as preservatives to stop fats from becoming rancid.","合成抗氧化剂：BHA、BHT，作食品防腐剂防油脂变臭"],["Eating a balanced diet with plenty of fruit and vegetables supplies antioxidants.","均衡饮食、多吃蔬果可摄取抗氧化剂"],["Antioxidants are also used in food and cosmetics to slow down spoilage and skin ageing.","抗氧化剂也用于食品与化妆品，减缓变质与肌肤老化"]],"华文：抗氧化剂来自蔬果，也可人工合成。","Tip: name the antioxidant AND a food source, e.g. 'vitamin C: orange'."],["Explain: Free Radicals and Antioxidants (F + H)","解释：自由基与抗氧化剂（F + H）",[["F1 Free radicals are harmful to the body. H: they take electrons from cell molecules and damage cells, proteins and DNA.","F1 自由基有害。H：抢细胞分子电子，损伤细胞、蛋白质、DNA"],["F2 Antioxidants protect the body. H: they donate electrons to free radicals, making the free radicals stable.","F2 抗氧化剂保护身体。H：供给电子使自由基稳定"],["F3 Lemon juice slows the browning of a cut apple. H: vitamin C in lemon juice is an antioxidant that prevents oxidation of the apple.","F3 柠檬汁减缓苹果变褐。H：维生素 C 是抗氧化剂，防止苹果氧化"],["F4 Food manufacturers add antioxidants to cooking oil and snacks. H: it prevents the fats from oxidising so the food stays fresh longer.","F4 厂商在食用油和零食中加抗氧化剂。H：防止油脂氧化，保持新鲜更久"]],"华文：写出「提供电子」才得分。","Tip: always write 'donate electron' for the H mark."],["Experiment: Antioxidant and Browning of Apple","实验：抗氧化剂与苹果变褐",[["Aim: to study the effect of antioxidant (vitamin C / lemon juice) on the browning of cut apple.","目的：研究抗氧化剂对切开苹果变褐的影响"],["Problem statement: does vitamin C slow down the browning of cut apple? Hypothesis: apple slices treated with vitamin C solution turn brown more slowly than untreated slices.","问题：维生素 C 是否减缓变褐？假设：用维生素 C 处理的苹果片变褐更慢"],["Variables: Manipulated: presence of vitamin C solution (or lemon juice). Responding: degree / time of browning. Fixed: type and size of apple, thickness of slices, time of exposure to air, temperature.","变量：操纵：有无维生素 C 溶液（柠檬汁）；响应：变褐程度/时间；固定：苹果种类、大小、厚度、暴露时间、温度"],["Apparatus and materials: apple, knife, tile, 3 petri dishes, vitamin C solution (or lemon juice), distilled water, dropper, stopwatch.","仪器材料：苹果、刀、砧板、培养皿、维生素 C 溶液/柠檬汁、蒸馏水、滴管、秒表"],["Procedure: (1) cut the apple into slices of equal size; (2) put one slice in each dish; (3) add vitamin C solution to dish A, lemon juice to B and distilled water to C (control); (4) leave for 30 minutes and observe the colour.","步骤：切成相同大小；分别加维生素 C、柠檬汁、蒸馏水（对照）；30 分钟后观察颜色"],["Observation: slices A and B stay light in colour; slice C turns brown. Conclusion: antioxidants slow down browning; hypothesis accepted.","观察：A、B 颜色较浅，C 变褐。结论：抗氧化剂减缓变褐，假设成立"]],"华文：要有对照组（蒸馏水）。","Tip: include a control (distilled water) and state the colour change for each slice."],["Health Products","保健产品",[["Health products: vitamins, minerals, herbal supplements, probiotics, health drinks and functional food to maintain or improve health.","保健产品：维生素、矿物质、草本补品、益生菌、保健饮品"],["Active ingredient: the substance in the product that gives the health effect.","活性成分：产生保健效果的物质"],["Health products help to improve health but do not cure disease and do not replace medicine or a balanced diet.","保健产品有助改善健康，但不能治病，也不能取代药物或均衡饮食"],["Health products in excess can be harmful, e.g. too much of vitamin A is toxic.","过量有害，如维生素 A 过多有毒"],["Pregnant women, children and patients should consult a doctor before taking health products.","孕妇、儿童、病人服用前应咨询医生"]],"华文：保健产品≠药物。","Tip: state 'does not replace medicine / balanced diet' when asked about the use of health products."],["Choosing Health Products Wisely","明智选择保健产品",[["Check that the product is registered with the Ministry of Health Malaysia (registration number and hologram on the label).","确认产品已向马来西亚卫生部注册（标签上有注册号和全息标）"],["Check the label: ingredients, expiry date, manufacturer, dosage and side effects.","检查标签：成分、有效期、制造商、剂量、副作用"],["Do not trust exaggerated claims such as 'cures all diseases' or 'instant results'.","不要相信夸大宣传，如「包治百病」「立竿见影」"],["Compare the price and buy from reliable shops; consult a doctor or pharmacist.","比较价格，到可靠店铺购买，咨询医生/药剂师"],["Stop using the product and see a doctor if side effects appear.","出现副作用立即停用并就医"]],"华文：选择产品先看注册，再看标签。","Tip: give the point and the reason, e.g. 'check the registration to make sure it is safe'."],["Explain: Health Products and Choices (F + H)","解释：保健产品与选择（F + H）",[["F1 Check the expiry date before buying health products. H: expired products may be spoilt and harmful.","F1 购买前查看有效期。H：过期产品可能变质有害"],["F2 Choose products registered with the Ministry of Health. H: registered products have been checked for safety and quality.","F2 选择卫生部注册产品。H：注册产品已检验安全与质量"],["F3 Health products should not replace a balanced diet. H: a balanced diet provides all the nutrients and fibre in the right amount.","F3 保健产品不能取代均衡饮食。H：均衡饮食提供各种营养及适量纤维"],["F4 Do not take health products in excess. H: too much of some vitamins or minerals can cause poisoning.","F4 勿过量服用。H：某些维生素或矿物质过多会中毒"]],"华文：每个建议配一个原因。","Tip: 'F = advice (1m); H = reason (1m)'."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Medicine and Health","示例题：试卷2 A部分（药物与健康）",[["(a) [1] Name one type of modern medicine used to relieve pain. Scheme: analgesic (1m).","(a)止痛药"],["(b) [2] A patient stops taking antibiotics after two days when the fever has gone. Explain why this is wrong. Scheme: some bacteria survive (1m); and become resistant to the antibiotic (1m).","(b)提早停药：部分细菌存活并产生抗药性"],["(c) [2] What is a free radical? Scheme: atom / molecule (1m); with an unpaired electron (1m).","(c)自由基：带不成对电子的原子/分子"],["(d) [2] Why does lemon juice slow the browning of a cut apple? Scheme: contains vitamin C (antioxidant) (1m); donates electron to free radicals / prevents oxidation (1m).","(d)柠檬汁含维生素 C，供电子，防止氧化"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Antioxidants and Health Products (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（抗氧化剂与保健产品）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how free radicals harm the body and how antioxidants help. Scheme: free radical has unpaired electron (1m); takes electrons from cells / damages cells and DNA (1m); antioxidant donates electron (1m); free radical becomes stable (1m).","(a)自由基如何伤害身体，抗氧化剂如何帮助"],["(b) [4] Design a simple experiment to show that vitamin C slows the browning of apple slices. Scheme: manipulated: vitamin C (1m); responding: browning (1m); fixed: size of apple slice / time (1m); control with distilled water and conclusion (1m).","(b)设计实验：维生素 C 减缓苹果变褐"],["(c) [KBAT] Aini wants to buy a health supplement advertised as 'cures all diseases'. Evaluate and advise her. Scheme: do not believe the claim (1m); no health product can cure all diseases (1m); check the registration and label (1m); consult a doctor or pharmacist (1m).","(c)评价并建议：不可轻信；检查注册与标签；咨询医生"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying antibiotics cure flu. Correct: antibiotics work on bacteria, not viruses.","错误：抗生素治流感。正确：抗生素只对细菌有效"],["Mistake: saying antioxidants 'kill' free radicals. Correct: antioxidants donate electrons to free radicals to make them stable.","错误：抗氧化剂「杀死」自由基。正确：供给电子使其稳定"],["Mistake: writing only 'unstable' for free radicals. Correct: unstable because of an unpaired electron.","错误：只写不稳定。正确：因不成对电子而不稳定"],["Mistake: saying health products can replace medicine. Correct: they support health but do not replace medicine or a balanced diet.","错误：保健产品可取代药物。正确：只辅助，不能取代"],["Mistake: no control in the antioxidant experiment. Correct: include a control with distilled water.","错误：抗氧化实验没有对照。正确：加蒸馏水对照组"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Name three types of medicine by source and testing. J: Traditional, modern and complementary medicine.","问：药物三大类？答：传统、现代、辅助"],["S: Why must a patient finish the antibiotic course? J: Otherwise some bacteria survive and become resistant.","问：为何要吃完抗生素？答：否则部分细菌存活并产生抗药性"],["S: What is a free radical? J: An atom or molecule with an unpaired electron, unstable and reactive.","问：自由基？答：带不成对电子，不稳定且活泼的原子/分子"],["S: How do antioxidants work? J: They donate electrons to free radicals to neutralise them.","问：抗氧化剂如何作用？答：供电子中和自由基"],["S: Give two antioxidants and a source. J: Vitamin C (orange); vitamin E (nuts).","问：两种抗氧化剂及来源？答：维生素 C（橙）；维生素 E（坚果）"],["S: What should you check before buying a health product? J: Registration, label, expiry date, and consult a doctor.","问：买保健产品前检查什么？答：注册、标签、有效期，并咨询医生"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-11":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Distance: the total length of the path travelled (scalar, unit m). Displacement: the shortest distance from the starting point to the end point in a stated direction (vector, unit m).","距离：走过的总路程（标量）；位移：起点到终点的最短距离并有方向（矢量）"],["Speed: distance travelled per unit time (scalar). Velocity: displacement per unit time (vector).","速率：单位时间内的路程；速度：单位时间内的位移"],["Acceleration: the rate of change of velocity (unit m/s²). Deceleration: negative acceleration, the velocity decreases.","加速度：速度变化率；减速：负加速度"],["Free fall: the motion of an object under the force of gravity only. Gravitational acceleration, g: the acceleration of a freely falling object towards the Earth.","自由落体：只受重力的运动；重力加速度 g"],["Mass: the amount of matter in an object (kg). Weight: the gravitational force acting on an object (N).","质量：物质的量；重量：重力（牛顿）"],["Inertia: the tendency of an object to resist any change in its state of rest or of uniform motion.","惯性：物体抗拒静止或匀速运动状态改变的趋势"]],"华文：定义要写关键词：标量/矢量、单位时间、变化率。","Tip: for distance vs displacement, write that displacement has direction (vector) and is the shortest straight-line distance."],["Distance, Displacement, Speed and Velocity","距离、位移、速率和速度",[["Scalar quantity: has magnitude only (distance, speed, mass, time). Vector quantity: has magnitude and direction (displacement, velocity, acceleration, force).","标量只有大小；矢量有大小和方向"],["Displacement is never longer than the distance travelled; they are equal only when the motion is in a straight line without changing direction.","位移不会大于路程；只有沿直线不转向时才相等"],["Average speed = total distance ÷ total time. Average velocity = total displacement ÷ total time.","平均速率 = 总路程 ÷ 总时间；平均速度 = 总位移 ÷ 总时间"],["Example: a runner completes one full round of a 400 m track in 50 s: distance = 400 m, displacement = 0 m, average velocity = 0 m/s.","例：跑一圈：路程400 m，位移0，平均速度0"],["Units: distance and displacement in m; time in s; speed and velocity in m/s (1 km/h = 1/3.6 m/s).","单位：m、s、m/s"]],"华文：位移为零不代表没有运动。","Tip: always state the unit; if the question asks for velocity, give the direction as well."],["Formulas for Linear Motion","直线运动公式",[["Speed: \\(v = \\dfrac{s}{t}\\) where s = distance (m), t = time (s), v in m/s.","速率 v = s/t"],["Velocity: \\(v = \\dfrac{\\text{displacement}}{t}\\) (m/s) with direction.","速度 = 位移/时间"],["Acceleration: \\(a = \\dfrac{v-u}{t}\\) where u = initial velocity, v = final velocity (m/s), t = time (s), a in m/s².","加速度 a = (v − u)/t"],["Rearranged: \\(v = u + at\\); \\(t = \\dfrac{v-u}{a}\\). For a deceleration, a is negative.","变形：v = u + at；减速时 a 为负"],["Starts from rest: u = 0. Comes to a stop: v = 0. Constant velocity: a = 0.","从静止出发 u = 0；停下 v = 0；匀速 a = 0"]],"华文：先抄公式，再代入，最后写单位，三步各有分。","Tip: marks are given for formula (1m), substitution (1m) and answer with unit (1m)."],["Worked Example 1: Speed and Velocity","例题1：速率与速度",[["Question: a car travels 180 km in 2 hours 30 minutes. Find its average speed in m/s.","题：汽车2.5小时行驶180 km，求平均速率（m/s）"],["Step 1 convert: distance = 180 000 m; time = 2.5 × 3600 = 9000 s. (1m)","步骤1：换算单位：180000 m；9000 s"],["Step 2 formula and substitution: \\(v = \\dfrac{s}{t} = \\dfrac{180\\,000}{9000}\\) (1m)","步骤2：公式与代入"],["Step 3 answer: \\(v = 20\\ \\text{m/s}\\) (1m)","步骤3：答案 20 m/s（带单位）"],["Check: 20 m/s × 3.6 = 72 km/h, which equals 180 km ÷ 2.5 h.","验算：20 × 3.6 = 72 km/h"]],"华文：先统一单位再代入。","Tip: convert km to m and hours to seconds before substituting."],["Worked Example 2: Acceleration and Deceleration","例题2：加速度与减速",[["Question A: a motorcycle starts from rest and reaches 24 m/s in 8 s. Find the acceleration.","题A：摩托车从静止加速到24 m/s用8 s，求加速度"],["Scheme A: \\(a = \\dfrac{v-u}{t} = \\dfrac{24-0}{8}\\) (1m) \\(= 3\\ \\text{m/s}^2\\) (1m, with unit).","答案A：a = 3 m/s²"],["Question B: a train moving at 30 m/s brakes and stops in 12 s. Find the deceleration.","题B：列车30 m/s刹车12 s停下，求减速度"],["Scheme B: \\(a = \\dfrac{0-30}{12} = -2.5\\ \\text{m/s}^2\\) (1m); deceleration = 2.5 m/s² (1m).","答案B：a = −2.5 m/s²，即减速度2.5 m/s²"],["Question C: using \\(v = u + at\\), a car with u = 5 m/s and a = 2 m/s² for 6 s: \\(v = 5 + 2 \\times 6 = 17\\ \\text{m/s}\\).","题C：v = u + at = 17 m/s"]],"华文：负号表示速度减小。","Tip: show the minus sign for deceleration, or state 'deceleration = 2.5 m/s²'."],["Displacement-Time Graph","位移-时间图",[["Gradient of the graph = velocity.","斜率 = 速度"],["Straight line sloping upwards: constant (uniform) velocity. Horizontal line: the object is stationary (velocity = 0).","斜直线：匀速；水平线：静止"],["Steeper gradient: higher velocity. Curve getting steeper: velocity increasing (accelerating).","越陡速度越大；曲线越来越陡：加速"],["Line sloping downwards: the object is moving back towards the starting point (negative velocity).","向下倾斜：返回出发点（速度为负）"],["Gradient calculation: \\(\\text{gradient} = \\dfrac{\\Delta s}{\\Delta t}\\) using a large triangle on the straight part of the line.","斜率 = Δs/Δt，用大三角形"]],"华文：看到 s-t 图想到斜率 = 速度。","Tip: state 'the gradient represents velocity' before calculating."],["Velocity-Time Graph","速度-时间图",[["Gradient = acceleration; area under the graph = displacement.","斜率 = 加速度；面积 = 位移"],["Straight line sloping upwards: constant acceleration. Horizontal line: constant velocity (a = 0). Line sloping downwards: deceleration.","上斜：匀加速；水平：匀速；下斜：减速"],["Line along the time axis (v = 0): the object is at rest.","贴着时间轴：静止"],["Area of a rectangle = base × height; triangle = ½ × base × height; trapezium = ½ × (sum of parallel sides) × height.","面积：矩形、三角形、梯形"],["Total displacement = sum of all the areas; average velocity = total displacement ÷ total time.","总位移 = 各面积之和"]],"华文：先分段，再逐段算面积。","Tip: split the graph into stages; write the shape, the formula for its area and the unit (m)."],["Worked Example 3: Reading a Velocity-Time Graph","例题3：解读速度-时间图",[["A car: 0 to 4 s velocity rises from 0 to 8 m/s; 4 to 10 s constant at 8 m/s; 10 to 12 s decreases to 0 m/s.","汽车：0–4 s从0加速到8；4–10 s匀速8；10–12 s减速到0"],["Acceleration (0–4 s): \\(a = \\dfrac{8-0}{4} = 2\\ \\text{m/s}^2\\) (1m). Deceleration (10–12 s): \\(a = \\dfrac{0-8}{2} = -4\\ \\text{m/s}^2\\) (1m).","加速度 2 m/s²；减速 −4 m/s²"],["Displacement: area of triangle \\(\\tfrac{1}{2}\\times4\\times8 = 16\\ \\text{m}\\); rectangle \\(6\\times8 = 48\\ \\text{m}\\); triangle \\(\\tfrac{1}{2}\\times2\\times8 = 8\\ \\text{m}\\). (2m)","位移：16 + 48 + 8"],["Total displacement = 16 + 48 + 8 = 72 m (1m).","总位移 72 m"],["Average velocity = \\(\\dfrac{72}{12} = 6\\ \\text{m/s}\\) (1m).","平均速度 = 72/12 = 6 m/s"]],"华文：三段图形的面积相加。","Tip: the unit of area under a v-t graph is metre (m), and of the gradient is m/s²."],["Free Fall and Gravitational Acceleration (F + H)","自由落体与重力加速度（F + H）",[["F1 In a vacuum, a feather and a stone fall at the same rate. H: there is no air resistance, so only gravity acts and all objects have the same acceleration.","F1 真空中羽毛和石头同时落地。H：无空气阻力，只受重力，加速度相同"],["F2 In air, a feather falls more slowly than a stone. H: air resistance has a bigger effect on the feather because of its large surface area and small mass.","F2 有空气时羽毛较慢。H：空气阻力对表面积大质量小的羽毛影响更大"],["F3 The gravitational acceleration near the Earth is about 9.8 m/s² (taken as 10 m/s² in many calculations). H: the velocity of a falling object increases by about 10 m/s every second.","F3 g ≈ 9.8 m/s²（常取10）。H：每秒速度增加约10 m/s"],["F4 Gravitational acceleration is different on other bodies, e.g. about 1.6 m/s² on the Moon. H: the Moon has a smaller mass than the Earth, so its gravitational pull is weaker.","F4 月球 g 约1.6 m/s²。H：月球质量小，引力弱"],["F5 A parachute slows a skydiver. H: the large surface area increases air resistance, which reduces the acceleration and the landing speed.","F5 降落伞减速。H：表面积大，空气阻力增大"]],"华文：F + H 格式：现象 + 原因。","Tip: mention 'air resistance' and 'surface area' for any question on a falling feather or parachute."],["Investigation: Determining the Gravitational Acceleration","探究：测定重力加速度",[["Aim: to determine the gravitational acceleration, g, by free fall. Problem statement: how can g be determined from the time of fall of a steel ball? (1m)","目的：用自由落体测 g"],["Hypothesis: the greater the height, the longer the time taken for the ball to fall. Variables: manipulated = height of fall; responding = time of fall; fixed = same ball (mass). (3m)","假设：高度越大，时间越长；变量：操纵=高度；响应=下落时间；固定=同一钢球"],["Apparatus: steel ball, electromagnet / release mechanism, electronic timer, trapdoor switch, retort stand, metre rule. (1m)","仪器：钢球、电磁铁、电子计时器、活门开关、铁架台、米尺"],["Procedure: 1 Set the height h = 1.0 m using the metre rule. 2 Release the ball; the timer records the time t. 3 Repeat with h = 0.8, 0.6, 0.4 and 0.2 m. 4 Repeat each height 3 times and take the average time. (2m)","步骤：设定高度，释放钢球，计时，改变高度重复，取平均"],["Calculation: since u = 0, \\(h = \\tfrac{1}{2}gt^2\\), so \\(g = \\dfrac{2h}{t^2}\\). Example: h = 1.2 m, t = 0.5 s: \\(g = \\dfrac{2\\times1.2}{0.5^2} = 9.6\\ \\text{m/s}^2\\) (1m).","计算：g = 2h/t²；例：g = 9.6 m/s²"],["Conclusion: the time of fall increases with height; the value of g is close to 9.8 m/s²; the hypothesis is accepted. (1m)","结论：高度越大，时间越长；g 接近9.8；假设被接受"]],"华文：重复测量取平均，可提高准确性。","Tip: to improve the result, repeat and take the average, and use a heavy compact ball to reduce air resistance."],["Mass and Weight","质量与重量",[["Mass: amount of matter, measured with a beam/electronic balance, unit kg, same everywhere. Weight: force of gravity, measured with a spring balance, unit N, changes with the gravitational field.","质量：kg，处处相同；重量：N，随引力场而变"],["Formula: \\(W = mg\\) where W = weight (N), m = mass (kg), g = gravitational acceleration (m/s²).","公式 W = mg"],["Worked example: a 60 kg astronaut on Earth (g = 10 m/s²): \\(W = 60\\times10 = 600\\ \\text{N}\\) (2m). On the Moon (g = 1.6 m/s²): \\(W = 60\\times1.6 = 96\\ \\text{N}\\) (1m).","例：60 kg宇航员地球600 N；月球96 N"],["The mass of the astronaut is still 60 kg on the Moon. H: mass depends on the amount of matter, not on the location.","在月球质量仍是60 kg，因为质量与地点无关"]],"华文：质量不变，重量会变。","Tip: kg is for mass and N is for weight; do not mix the units."],["Inertia (F + H)","惯性（F + H）",[["F1 A larger mass has a larger inertia. H: more force is needed to change its state of motion (to start it, stop it or change its direction).","F1 质量越大惯性越大。H：改变其运动状态需要更大的力"],["F2 When a bus brakes suddenly, passengers lean forward. H: their bodies tend to remain in motion (inertia) while the bus stops.","F2 急刹车乘客前倾。H：身体因惯性保持原来的运动"],["F3 When a bus starts suddenly, passengers lean backward. H: their bodies tend to remain at rest while the bus moves forward.","F3 突然启动乘客后仰。H：身体因惯性保持静止"],["F4 Shaking a tomato sauce bottle downwards then stopping suddenly makes the sauce come out. H: the sauce keeps moving (inertia) when the bottle stops.","F4 番茄酱瓶急停酱料继续前进"],["F5 A heavy lorry is more difficult to stop than a car moving at the same speed. H: its mass and inertia are larger.","F5 重卡比轿车难停：质量与惯性更大"]],"华文：先说物体原来的状态，再说惯性使它保持。","Tip: write 'the body tends to remain in its state of rest / motion' to earn the H mark."],["Investigation: Relationship between Mass and Inertia","探究：质量与惯性的关系",[["Aim: to study the relationship between mass and inertia. Problem statement: does the mass affect the inertia of an object? (1m)","目的：研究质量与惯性的关系"],["Hypothesis: the larger the mass, the larger the inertia (the longer the time for 10 oscillations). (1m)","假设：质量越大，惯性越大（10次摆动时间越长）"],["Variables: manipulated = mass of plasticine; responding = time for 10 oscillations (inertia); fixed = length of the hacksaw blade, displacement of the blade. (3m)","变量：操纵=橡皮泥质量；响应=10次摆动时间；固定=锯条长度、位移"],["Apparatus: hacksaw blade, G-clamp, plasticine of different masses, stopwatch, beam balance. (1m)","仪器：锯条、G形夹、橡皮泥、秒表、天平"],["Procedure: 1 Clamp the blade to the bench; attach 20 g plasticine at the free end. 2 Pull the end sideways and release; measure the time for 10 oscillations. 3 Repeat with 40, 60, 80 and 100 g. (2m)","步骤：固定锯条，加20 g，拉动释放，测10次摆动时间；换40、60、80、100 g重复"],["Observation: the time for 10 oscillations increases as the mass increases. Conclusion: the larger the mass, the larger the inertia; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察：质量越大时间越长；结论：质量越大惯性越大"]],"华文：摆得越慢说明惯性越大。","Tip: inertia is shown by the time taken: a longer time means a larger inertia."],["Inertia: Safety Features and Applications (F + H)","惯性：安全设计与应用（F + H）",[["F1 Seat belt. H: stops the body from continuing forward (inertia) during a collision, so the passenger is not thrown against the windscreen.","F1 安全带：碰撞时阻止身体因惯性前冲"],["F2 Headrest. H: prevents the head from jerking backwards when a car is hit from behind, protecting the neck.","F2 头枕：后方被撞时防止头后仰，保护颈部"],["F3 Airbag. H: cushions the body and reduces the forward movement and the impact on the driver.","F3 安全气囊：缓冲身体前冲的冲击"],["F4 Strong cargo barrier / tie-down straps on a lorry. H: stops the load from moving forward when the lorry brakes suddenly.","F4 货车货物固定装置：防止急刹车时货物前冲"],["F5 Lorries are limited in loading and speed. H: a heavier load increases the inertia and the stopping distance.","F5 货车限载限速：载重越大惯性越大，刹车距离越长"]],"华文：每个安全设计都对应惯性。","Tip: name the device, state the function, then link it to inertia."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Linear Motion","示例题：试卷2 A部分（直线运动）",[["(a) [1] State the quantity that is represented by the gradient of a velocity-time graph. Scheme: acceleration (1m).","(a)v-t图斜率：加速度"],["(b) [3] A cyclist accelerates from 2 m/s to 12 m/s in 5 s. Calculate the acceleration. Scheme: \\(a = (v-u)/t\\) (1m); \\((12-2)/5\\) (1m); 2 m/s² (1m).","(b)骑车人加速度：2 m/s²"],["(c) [2] A passenger leans backwards when a stationary bus starts suddenly. Explain why. Scheme: the passenger tends to remain at rest (1m); due to inertia (1m).","(c)乘客后仰：因惯性保持静止"],["(d) [2] A 50 kg boy stands on the Moon (g = 1.6 m/s²). State his mass and weight. Scheme: 50 kg (1m); \\(W = 50 \\times 1.6 = 80\\) N (1m).","(d)质量50 kg；重量80 N"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Motion and Safety (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（运动与安全）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] A car moves at a constant velocity of 15 m/s for 6 s, then decelerates uniformly to rest in 5 s. Calculate the total displacement. Scheme: \\(15 \\times 6 = 90\\) m (1m); area of triangle \\(\\tfrac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 15\\) (1m) = 37.5 m (1m); total = 127.5 m (1m).","(a)匀速15 m/s 6 s，再5 s减速到停；总位移127.5 m"],["(b) [2] Explain why the displacement-time graph of a stationary object is a horizontal line. Scheme: displacement does not change with time (1m); velocity = gradient = 0 (1m).","(b)静止物体s-t图水平：位移不变，斜率为0"],["(c) [KBAT, 4] Suggest and justify two safety features that reduce injury to passengers in a car accident. Scheme: seat belt (1m) holds the body so it does not continue moving forward due to inertia (1m); airbag / headrest (1m) cushions or supports the body / head (1m).","(c)提出并说明两项安全设计：安全带；气囊/头枕"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: using the distance instead of the displacement for velocity. Correct: velocity = displacement ÷ time, and give the direction.","错误：速度用路程计算。正确：用位移并写方向"],["Mistake: forgetting to convert km/h or minutes to m/s and s. Correct: convert the units first, or state the unit used.","错误：忘记换算单位。正确：先统一单位"],["Mistake: writing the weight in kg. Correct: weight is in newton (N); mass is in kg.","错误：重量用kg。正确：重量N，质量kg"],["Mistake: saying 'inertia is a force'. Correct: inertia is a property (tendency) of the object to resist a change in motion.","错误：说惯性是力。正确：惯性是物体的性质"],["Mistake: writing the area under a v-t graph as velocity. Correct: the area is displacement; the gradient is acceleration.","错误：v-t图面积写成速度。正确：面积是位移，斜率是加速度"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is the difference between distance and displacement? J: Distance is the total path length (scalar); displacement is the shortest distance with direction (vector).","问：距离与位移的区别？答：距离是总路程（标量）；位移是有方向的最短距离（矢量）"],["S: A car goes from 4 m/s to 16 m/s in 3 s. What is a? J: a = (16 - 4)/3 = 4 m/s².","问：汽车3 s从4到16 m/s，a是多少？答：4 m/s²"],["S: What does the area under a velocity-time graph represent? J: Displacement.","问：v-t图面积代表什么？答：位移"],["S: Why do all objects fall at the same rate in a vacuum? J: There is no air resistance, so only gravity acts.","问：为何真空中物体下落一样快？答：没有空气阻力，只受重力"],["S: Find the weight of a 5 kg object (g = 10 m/s²). J: W = mg = 5 x 10 = 50 N.","问：5 kg物体重量？答：50 N"],["S: Why do passengers lean forward when a bus brakes suddenly? J: Their bodies tend to remain in motion because of inertia.","问：急刹车为何前倾？答：因惯性身体保持原来运动"]],"",""]],"sains|T4-12":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Nuclear energy: the energy released from the nucleus of an atom during a nuclear reaction (fission or fusion).","核能：核反应中从原子核释放的能量"],["Nuclear fission: the splitting of a heavy nucleus (e.g. uranium-235) into two smaller nuclei, releasing energy and neutrons.","核裂变：重核分裂成较小原子核，放出能量和中子"],["Nuclear fusion: the joining of two light nuclei (e.g. hydrogen isotopes) to form a heavier nucleus (helium), releasing a very large amount of energy.","核聚变：轻核结合成较重原子核，放出巨大能量"],["Chain reaction: a self-sustaining series of fissions in which the neutrons released cause more nuclei to split.","链式反应：释放的中子引起更多裂变，持续进行"],["Radioactive decay: the spontaneous breaking up of an unstable nucleus, emitting radiation. Half-life: the time taken for half of the radioactive nuclei in a sample to decay.","放射性衰变；半衰期：一半原子核衰变所需时间"],["Radioisotope: an unstable isotope that emits radiation. Nuclear reactor: a device that controls a fission chain reaction to produce heat.","放射性同位素；核反应堆：控制链式反应产生热"]],"华文：裂变是分，聚变是合；定义要写出「释放能量」。","Tip: for fission write 'heavy nucleus splits into smaller nuclei'; for fusion write 'light nuclei combine to form a heavier nucleus'."],["Atoms, Isotopes and Radioactivity","原子、同位素与放射性",[["The nucleus contains protons and neutrons (nucleons). Nucleon number = protons + neutrons; proton number = number of protons.","原子核含质子和中子；核子数 = 质子 + 中子"],["Isotopes: atoms of the same element with the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons (e.g. hydrogen-1, deuterium, tritium).","同位素：质子数相同、中子数不同"],["Unstable nuclei decay and emit radiation: alpha particles, beta particles and gamma rays.","不稳定原子核衰变，放出 α、β 粒子和 γ 射线"],["Radioactive decay is random and cannot be speeded up or slowed down by heat, pressure or chemical reaction.","衰变是随机的，不受温度、压力、化学反应影响"],["Penetration: alpha is stopped by paper; beta by a thin aluminium sheet; gamma needs thick lead or concrete.","穿透力：α用纸挡；β用薄铝片；γ需厚铅或混凝土"]],"华文：γ 射线穿透力最强。","Tip: when asked for shielding, state the material (thick lead or concrete) for gamma rays."],["Half-Life and Worked Example","半衰期与例题",[["After each half-life, the remaining mass (or activity) of the radioisotope becomes half of the previous value.","每经过一个半衰期，剩余量变为一半"],["Number of half-lives: \\(n = \\dfrac{\\text{total time}}{\\text{half-life}}\\); remaining mass = \\(\\text{initial mass} \\times \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^n\\).","半衰期数 n = 总时间 / 半衰期"],["Question: a radioisotope has a half-life of 6 days. Initial mass = 80 g. Find the mass left after 18 days.","题：半衰期6天，原有80 g，18天后剩多少？"],["Scheme: \\(n = 18 \\div 6 = 3\\) (1m); \\(80 \\to 40 \\to 20 \\to 10\\) (1m); mass left = 10 g (1m, with unit).","答案：n = 3；80→40→20→10；剩10 g"],["Half-life graph: the curve of mass against time falls steeply at first and then flattens; the time for the mass to drop to half is read from the graph.","半衰期图：曲线先陡后平，读出降为一半的时间"]],"华文：先算半衰期数，再逐次减半。","Tip: show each halving step; the final answer needs a unit (g or %)."],["Nuclear Fission","核裂变",[["A slow-moving neutron hits a uranium-235 nucleus, which becomes unstable and splits into two smaller nuclei (e.g. barium and krypton) and releases 2–3 neutrons and a large amount of energy.","慢中子撞击铀-235，分裂成较小原子核，放出2–3个中子和大量能量"],["The energy is released mainly as heat and radiation.","能量主要以热和辐射形式释放"],["Fuel: uranium-235 or plutonium-239 (heavy nuclei).","燃料：铀-235、钚-239"],["Equation (word form): uranium-235 + neutron → two smaller nuclei + 2 or 3 neutrons + energy.","铀-235 + 中子 → 两个较小核 + 2或3个中子 + 能量"],["Fission is used in nuclear power stations and in atomic bombs.","用于核电站和原子弹"]],"华文：裂变要写出「中子撞击」。","Tip: draw a diagram: neutron, large nucleus, two smaller nuclei, extra neutrons, energy."],["Chain Reaction and Control (F + H)","链式反应与控制（F + H）",[["F1 The 2–3 neutrons released hit other uranium nuclei. H: these split and release more neutrons, so the number of fissions increases rapidly (chain reaction).","F1 放出的中子撞击其他铀核。H：继续裂变放出更多中子，形成链式反应"],["F2 In a nuclear bomb the chain reaction is uncontrolled. H: all the energy is released in a very short time, causing an explosion.","F2 核弹链式反应不受控。H：瞬间释放全部能量而爆炸"],["F3 In a reactor the chain reaction is controlled by control rods (boron or cadmium). H: they absorb excess neutrons, so the rate of fission and the heat produced are steady.","F3 反应堆用控制棒（硼/镉）。H：吸收多余中子，使裂变速率稳定"],["F4 A moderator (water or graphite) slows down fast neutrons. H: slow neutrons are more likely to be captured by uranium-235 and cause fission.","F4 减速剂使快中子变慢。H：慢中子更易引起裂变"],["F5 Insert the control rods fully to shut down the reactor. H: all neutrons are absorbed so the fission stops.","F5 全部插入控制棒可停堆。H：吸收所有中子"]],"华文：控制棒 = 吸收中子。","Tip: control rods absorb neutrons; moderator slows neutrons. Do not mix them up."],["Nuclear Fusion","核聚变",[["Two light nuclei (deuterium and tritium, isotopes of hydrogen) join to form a helium nucleus and release a neutron and a very large amount of energy.","氘和氚结合成氦，放出中子和巨大能量"],["Fusion needs extremely high temperature (millions of degrees Celsius) and pressure to overcome the repulsion between the positively charged nuclei.","需要极高温度和压力以克服正电核之间的排斥"],["Fusion is the source of energy of the Sun and other stars.","聚变是太阳和恒星的能量来源"],["Advantages: fuel (hydrogen) is abundant; the products are not highly radioactive. Problem: very difficult to control on Earth, so it is not yet used to generate electricity commercially.","优点：燃料丰富，产物放射性低；困难：难以控制，尚未商业发电"]],"华文：聚变需要极高温度。","Tip: give the condition 'very high temperature' when describing fusion."],["Fission versus Fusion","裂变与聚变比较",[["Nuclei: fission uses a heavy nucleus (uranium-235); fusion uses light nuclei (hydrogen isotopes).","原子核：裂变用重核；聚变用轻核"],["Process: fission splits one nucleus into smaller ones; fusion joins nuclei into a heavier one.","过程：裂变分裂；聚变结合"],["Conditions: fission starts with a neutron at normal temperature; fusion needs extremely high temperature and pressure.","条件：裂变由中子引发；聚变需极高温高压"],["Waste: fission produces radioactive waste that lasts a long time; fusion produces little radioactive waste.","废料：裂变核废料持久；聚变废料少"],["Use: fission in nuclear power stations; fusion in the Sun and hydrogen bombs. Energy per kg of fuel: fusion releases more than fission.","应用：裂变用于核电站；聚变发生在太阳。同质量燃料聚变放能更多"]],"华文：比较题要用「…而…」对比。","Tip: in a comparison, write both sides in one sentence, e.g. 'fission splits a heavy nucleus whereas fusion joins light nuclei'."],["Mass-Energy Relationship and Worked Example","质能关系与例题",[["In fission and fusion, the total mass of the products is slightly less than the mass of the reactants. The 'missing' mass is converted into energy.","反应后总质量略少，减少的质量转化为能量"],["Einstein's equation: \\(E = mc^2\\) where E = energy (J), m = mass converted (kg), c = speed of light = \\(3 \\times 10^8\\ \\text{m/s}\\).","E = mc²；c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s"],["Question: 1 g of matter is converted completely into energy. Calculate the energy released.","题：1 g物质完全转化为能量，求能量"],["Scheme: m = 1 g = 0.001 kg (1m); \\(E = 0.001 \\times (3\\times10^8)^2\\) (1m); \\(E = 9 \\times 10^{13}\\ \\text{J}\\) (1m).","答案：m = 0.001 kg；E = 9 × 10¹³ J"],["A very small mass produces a very large energy, which is why nuclear fuel gives much more energy than fossil fuel.","很小质量产生极大能量"]],"华文：先把克换成千克。","Tip: convert g to kg before substituting into E = mc²."],["Generating Electricity from Nuclear Energy","核能发电",[["Fission in the reactor core produces heat.","反应堆内裂变产生热"],["The heat boils water (or heats the coolant, which boils the water in a heat exchanger) to produce steam at high pressure.","热使水沸腾产生高压蒸汽"],["The steam turns the turbine, which turns the generator to produce electricity.","蒸汽推动涡轮，涡轮带动发电机发电"],["The steam is cooled in a condenser and the water returns to be heated again.","蒸汽在冷凝器冷却后回流再加热"],["Energy changes: nuclear energy → heat energy → kinetic energy (turbine) → electrical energy.","能量转换：核能 → 热能 → 动能 → 电能"]],"华文：流程图要按顺序画出。","Tip: write the flow in order: reactor, heat, steam, turbine, generator, electricity."],["Parts of a Nuclear Reactor (F + H)","核反应堆的组成（F + H）",[["F1 Fuel rods contain uranium (enriched uranium-235). H: they undergo fission and produce heat.","F1 燃料棒含浓缩铀。H：发生裂变产生热"],["F2 Control rods (boron or cadmium) can be raised or lowered. H: they absorb neutrons to control the rate of fission.","F2 控制棒可升降。H：吸收中子控制裂变速率"],["F3 Moderator (water or graphite). H: slows down neutrons so that fission occurs more easily.","F3 减速剂。H：使中子减速"],["F4 Coolant (water, heavy water or gas). H: carries the heat from the core to produce steam and prevents the reactor from overheating.","F4 冷却剂。H：带走热量产生蒸汽，防止过热"],["F5 Thick concrete and steel shielding. H: absorbs radiation, protecting workers and the surroundings.","F5 厚混凝土和钢屏蔽层。H：吸收辐射保护人员和环境"]],"华文：每个部件的作用都要会。","Tip: name the part, then its function using 'to absorb', 'to slow down' or 'to carry away'."],["Advantages and Disadvantages of Nuclear Power","核能发电的利与弊",[["Advantage: a small amount of fuel produces a very large amount of energy.","优点：少量燃料产生大量能量"],["Advantage: no carbon dioxide or smoke is released during operation, so it does not directly cause the greenhouse effect or acid rain; it can supply electricity continuously.","优点：运行时不排放CO₂和烟尘，可持续供电"],["Disadvantage: radioactive waste stays dangerous for thousands of years and needs safe storage.","缺点：核废料危险期长，需安全储存"],["Disadvantage: accident risk (leak of radiation); very high cost of building and decommissioning.","缺点：事故风险；建造和除役成本高"],["Disadvantage: hot cooling water released into the sea may harm aquatic life; nuclear material may be misused for weapons.","缺点：热排水影响水生生物；核材料可能被滥用"]],"华文：评价题要两面都写。","Tip: for 'evaluate', give an advantage, a disadvantage and then a decision."],["Impact of Nuclear Energy on Life and Environment","核能对生活与环境的影响",[["Nuclear weapons: atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki in 1945 killed many people and caused radiation sickness and long-term damage.","核武器：1945年广岛、长崎造成大量死亡与辐射病"],["Nuclear accidents: Chernobyl (1986) and Fukushima (2011) released radioactive substances into the environment; large areas were evacuated.","核事故：切尔诺贝利（1986）、福岛（2011）释放放射性物质"],["Effects of high radiation on humans: burns, hair loss, cancer, genetic mutation and, at very high doses, death.","高剂量辐射影响：灼伤、脱发、癌症、基因突变、死亡"],["Effects on the environment: contaminated soil and water; plants and animals are harmed or mutated.","环境影响：土壤水源受污染，动植物受害或突变"]],"华文：知道事件名称、年份和后果。","Tip: link each event to its consequence, e.g. Chernobyl: radiation leak, evacuation, cancer."],["Radiation Safety (F + H)","辐射安全（F + H）",[["F1 Minimise the time of exposure to radiation. H: the shorter the time, the smaller the dose absorbed.","F1 缩短受辐射时间。H：时间越短，吸收剂量越小"],["F2 Keep a large distance from the source (use tongs or remote handling). H: radiation weakens as distance increases.","F2 远离辐射源（用夹子或遥控）。H：距离越远辐射越弱"],["F3 Use shielding such as thick lead or concrete. H: it absorbs the radiation, especially gamma rays.","F3 用铅或混凝土屏蔽。H：吸收辐射"],["F4 Wear a radiation badge (dosimeter) and protective clothing. H: to monitor the dose received and prevent contamination.","F4 佩戴剂量计和防护服。H：监测剂量，防止污染"],["F5 Store radioactive substances in lead containers with the radioactive hazard symbol. H: to prevent leakage and warn people.","F5 放射物质存放在铅容器并贴标志。H：防泄漏并警示"]],"华文：时间、距离、屏蔽三原则。","Tip: remember 'time, distance, shielding' and give a reason for each."],["Uses of Radioisotopes","放射性同位素的应用",[["Medicine: cobalt-60 (gamma rays) kills cancer cells in radiotherapy; iodine-131 treats and diagnoses thyroid problems; technetium-99m is a tracer used for imaging.","医学：钴-60治疗癌症；碘-131甲状腺；锝-99m示踪成像"],["Sterilisation: gamma rays kill bacteria on medical equipment and some foods without heating them.","灭菌：γ射线杀死细菌而不加热"],["Industry: gamma rays detect cracks in pipes or welds; beta radiation is used to control the thickness of paper and aluminium foil; smoke detectors use americium-241.","工业：检测裂缝；控制纸张厚度；烟雾探测器"],["Agriculture: radioisotopes trace the uptake of fertiliser by plants; radiation produces new crop varieties.","农业：示踪肥料吸收；辐射育种"],["Archaeology: carbon-14 dating estimates the age of ancient wood and bones.","考古：碳-14测定年代"]],"华文：每个用途配一个同位素。","Tip: choose a radioisotope with a suitable half-life: short for medical tracers so that it does not stay in the body."],["Nuclear Energy in Malaysia","马来西亚与核能",[["Malaysia has used nuclear technology in research, medicine, industry and agriculture; the TRIGA PUSPATI research reactor (RTP) at Bangi is operated by Nuclear Malaysia.","马来西亚核技术用于研究、医疗、工业、农业；Bangi的TRIGA研究反应堆由马来西亚核机构运营"],["The Atomic Energy Licensing Board (AELB) regulates the use of radioactive materials for safety.","原子能许可局（AELB）负责监管"],["Reasons to consider a nuclear power station: rising demand for electricity, reduce dependence on fossil fuels, lower carbon emissions.","考虑的理由：电力需求上升、减少化石燃料依赖、低碳排放"],["Concerns: safety and accident risk, radioactive waste storage, high cost, public acceptance, need for trained experts, and the risk of natural disasters.","顾虑：安全、废料、成本、民意、人才、自然灾害"]],"华文：这类题要写理由和顾虑，并给出自己的结论。","Tip: for an opinion question, state your decision first and support it with two reasons."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Nuclear Energy","示例题：试卷2 A部分（核能）",[["(a) [1] Name the process in which a uranium-235 nucleus splits into smaller nuclei. Scheme: nuclear fission (1m).","(a)核裂变"],["(b) [2] State the function of control rods in a reactor. Scheme: absorb neutrons (1m); to control the rate of the chain reaction (1m).","(b)控制棒：吸收中子；控制链式反应速率"],["(c) [3] A radioisotope has a half-life of 4 hours. The initial mass is 192 g. How long does it take for the mass to decrease to 48 g? Scheme: 192 to 96 to 48 = 2 half-lives (1m); 2 x 4 (1m); 8 hours (1m).","(c)192 g降到48 g：2个半衰期，8小时"],["(d) [2] State two differences between fission and fusion. Scheme: fission splits a heavy nucleus whereas fusion joins light nuclei (1m); fusion needs very high temperature whereas fission does not (1m).","(d)两点区别"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Nuclear Power Station (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（核电站）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how electricity is generated in a nuclear power station. Scheme: fission of uranium produces heat (1m); heat changes water to steam (1m); steam turns the turbine (1m); turbine turns the generator to produce electricity (1m).","(a)核电站发电的过程"],["(b) [2] Explain why a thick concrete wall surrounds the reactor. Scheme: absorbs radiation / gamma rays (1m); to protect workers and the environment (1m).","(b)为何有厚混凝土墙：吸收辐射，保护人和环境"],["(c) [KBAT, 4] A country is deciding whether to build a nuclear power station. Evaluate this proposal. Scheme: advantage - large energy from little fuel / no CO2 emission (1m + 1m explanation); disadvantage - radioactive waste / accident risk (1m + 1m explanation); decision with a reason.","(c)评价是否建核电站：利、弊、决定"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying that control rods slow down neutrons. Correct: control rods absorb neutrons; the moderator slows them.","错误：控制棒使中子减速。正确：控制棒吸收中子"],["Mistake: confusing fission and fusion. Correct: fission = splitting of a heavy nucleus; fusion = joining of light nuclei.","错误：混淆裂变和聚变"],["Mistake: writing that nuclear power stations release carbon dioxide during operation. Correct: they do not, but they produce radioactive waste.","错误：认为运行时排放CO₂。正确：不排放，但有核废料"],["Mistake: forgetting the unit or the halving steps in half-life calculations. Correct: show each halving and write the unit.","错误：半衰期计算不写步骤和单位"],["Mistake: giving only the advantages in an evaluation. Correct: give both advantages and disadvantages, then your decision.","错误：评价只写优点。正确：利弊都写再下结论"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is nuclear fission? J: A heavy nucleus splits into smaller nuclei, releasing energy and neutrons.","问：什么是核裂变？答：重核分裂成较小核并释放能量和中子"],["S: What is the function of control rods? J: Absorb neutrons to control the chain reaction.","问：控制棒的作用？答：吸收中子以控制链式反应"],["S: A radioisotope of half-life 5 days has 40 g. How much is left after 10 days? J: 10 g.","问：半衰期5天，40 g，10天后剩多少？答：10 g"],["S: Where does fusion occur naturally? J: In the Sun and other stars.","问：聚变在哪里自然发生？答：太阳和恒星"],["S: Give one disadvantage of nuclear power. J: Radioactive waste (or accident risk, high cost).","问：核能一个缺点？答：核废料（或事故风险、成本高）"],["S: Which radioisotope is used to treat cancer? J: Cobalt-60.","问：哪种同位素用于治疗癌症？答：钴-60"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-1":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Microorganism: a living organism that is too small to be seen with the naked eye and can only be seen with a microscope.","微生物：肉眼看不见、需用显微镜观察的生物"],["Pathogen: a microorganism that causes disease. Infectious disease: a disease that can be spread from one person to another.","病原体：引起疾病的微生物；传染病：可在人与人之间传播的疾病"],["Fermentation: the breakdown of sugar by microorganisms (e.g. yeast) without oxygen, producing carbon dioxide and ethanol (alcohol), or lactic acid by some bacteria.","发酵：微生物无氧分解糖，产生CO₂和乙醇或乳酸"],["Vaccine: a preparation of weakened or dead pathogens (or their parts) that stimulates the body to produce antibodies. Antibody: a protein made by white blood cells to destroy a specific pathogen.","疫苗：减弱/死亡的病原体，刺激身体产生抗体；抗体：白细胞产生的蛋白质"],["Antibiotic: a drug that kills or stops the growth of bacteria. Aseptic technique: a method to prevent unwanted microorganisms from contaminating a culture or the surroundings.","抗生素：杀死或抑制细菌；无菌技术：防止杂菌污染"],["Sterilisation: killing all microorganisms on apparatus or in food. Culture medium: a nutrient substance (e.g. agar) on which microorganisms are grown.","灭菌：杀死所有微生物；培养基：供微生物生长的营养物质（琼脂）"]],"华文：定义要写关键词，如「肉眼看不见」「抗体」「抑制细菌」。","Tip: antibiotics work against bacteria only, not viruses; write this in any antibiotic answer."],["Types of Microorganisms","微生物的种类",[["Bacteria: single-celled, no true nucleus, shapes: round (cocci), rod (bacilli), spiral (spirilla). Examples: Lactobacillus, Escherichia coli, Vibrio cholerae.","细菌：单细胞、无真正细胞核；球形、杆形、螺旋形"],["Virus: not a cell; extremely small; reproduces only inside a living host cell; has genetic material in a protein coat. Examples: influenza, dengue virus, HIV.","病毒：非细胞结构，只能在宿主细胞内繁殖"],["Fungi: yeast (single-celled) and moulds (made of thread-like hyphae); get food from dead or living organisms. Examples: Saccharomyces (yeast), Rhizopus (bread mould), Penicillium.","真菌：酵母菌（单细胞）、霉菌（菌丝）"],["Protozoa: single-celled, with a nucleus, many move using cilia, flagella or false feet. Examples: Amoeba, Paramecium, Plasmodium (malaria).","原生动物：单细胞，有细胞核"],["Algae: simple organisms that contain chlorophyll and make food by photosynthesis. Examples: Chlorella, Spirogyra.","藻类：含叶绿素，光合作用"]],"华文：病毒不是细胞，必须寄生。","Tip: the key point for viruses is 'reproduce only inside a living host cell'."],["Conditions for the Growth of Microorganisms (F + H)","微生物生长的条件（F + H）",[["F1 Warm temperature (about 25 to 40 degrees C). H: enzymes in microorganisms work best at a suitable temperature; very low temperature slows growth and very high temperature kills them.","F1 适宜温度。H：酶在适宜温度下最活跃；低温减缓，高温杀死"],["F2 Moisture (water). H: needed for the chemical reactions in the cells and to absorb nutrients.","F2 水分。H：细胞反应和吸收养分需要水"],["F3 Nutrients (sugar, protein, starch). H: source of food and energy for growth and reproduction.","F3 养分。H：提供食物与能量"],["F4 Suitable pH (most bacteria prefer neutral; fungi prefer slightly acidic). H: extreme pH damages their enzymes.","F4 适宜pH。H：极端pH破坏酶"],["F5 Oxygen (for aerobic ones); some bacteria grow without oxygen. H: aerobic organisms need oxygen for respiration.","F5 氧气（需氧型）。H：需氧呼吸"]],"华文：保存食物就是破坏这些条件。","Tip: link each condition to enzymes or respiration for the H mark."],["Investigation: Conditions Affecting the Growth of Mould on Bread","探究：影响面包霉生长的条件",[["Aim: to study the effect of moisture on the growth of mould on bread. Problem statement: does moisture affect the growth of mould on bread? (1m)","目的：研究水分对面包霉生长的影响"],["Hypothesis: the more moist the bread, the more mould grows on it. (1m)","假设：面包越湿，霉越多"],["Variables: manipulated = moisture of bread (dry / moist); responding = growth of mould (area covered); fixed = type and size of bread, temperature, time, light. (3m)","变量：操纵=湿度；响应=霉生长；固定=面包种类大小、温度、时间"],["Apparatus and materials: 2 slices of bread, 2 transparent plastic bags / Petri dishes, water, dropper, magnifying glass. (1m)","仪器与材料"],["Procedure: 1 Sprinkle water on slice A; keep slice B dry. 2 Place each in a sealed bag and leave in a warm place for 5 days. 3 Observe the mould every day with a magnifying glass and record. (2m)","步骤：A片加水，B片保持干；放暖处5天，每天观察"],["Observation: slice A has more mould. Conclusion: the more moist the bread, the more mould grows; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察：A片霉较多；结论：越湿霉越多，假设被接受"]],"华文：不要打开袋子，避免吸入孢子。","Tip: state a safety measure, e.g. keep the bags sealed and wash hands afterwards."],["Culturing Microorganisms and Aseptic Technique (F + H)","培养微生物与无菌技术（F + H）",[["F1 Sterilise the Petri dish and agar (in an autoclave). H: to kill unwanted microorganisms that will contaminate the culture.","F1 培养皿和琼脂灭菌。H：杀死杂菌防止污染"],["F2 Flame the inoculating loop until red hot and let it cool. H: to kill microorganisms on the loop; hot loop would kill the culture.","F2 接种环灼烧后冷却。H：杀菌；过热会杀死样品"],["F3 Open the lid of the Petri dish only slightly and work near a Bunsen flame. H: to reduce contamination from the air.","F3 培养皿盖只开小缝，靠近火焰。H：减少空气污染"],["F4 Seal the lid with tape and incubate upside down at about 30 degrees C. H: to prevent contamination and keep water drops from falling onto the agar.","F4 胶带封口，倒置培养。H：防污染，水珠不滴到琼脂"],["F5 Do not open the dish after incubation; dispose of it after sterilising. H: to prevent the release of pathogens.","F5 培养后不开盖，灭菌后丢弃。H：防止病原体释放"],["Wash hands and wear gloves and a lab coat. H: to prevent infection.","洗手、戴手套、穿实验服。H：防感染"]],"华文：每个步骤都是为了防止污染。","Tip: the reason is always 'to prevent contamination' or 'to kill unwanted microorganisms'."],["Beneficial Microorganisms: Food","有益微生物：食物",[["Yeast: makes bread rise (carbon dioxide forms bubbles in the dough); used to make tapai and alcoholic drinks by fermentation.","酵母菌：使面包膨胀；制作tapai和酒"],["Lactic acid bacteria (Lactobacillus): make yoghurt and cheese from milk; sour taste and preserve the food.","乳酸菌：制作酸奶和奶酪"],["Fungi: Rhizopus makes tempeh from soya beans; Aspergillus is used to make soy sauce and tauhu fermentation products.","真菌：根霉制作天贝；曲霉制作酱油"],["Acetic acid bacteria change ethanol to vinegar.","醋酸菌把乙醇变为醋"]],"华文：每个例子写：哪种微生物 + 做什么食物。","Tip: give the microorganism and the product, e.g. 'Lactobacillus - yoghurt'."],["Investigation: Fermentation by Yeast","探究：酵母菌发酵",[["Aim: to study the effect of temperature on the fermentation of yeast. Problem statement: does temperature affect the rate of fermentation by yeast? (1m)","目的：研究温度对酵母发酵的影响"],["Hypothesis: the higher the temperature (up to the optimum), the higher the rate of carbon dioxide production. (1m)","假设：温度越高（至最适温度），CO₂产生越快"],["Variables: manipulated = temperature of the mixture; responding = height / diameter of the balloon (or volume of gas); fixed = mass of yeast, volume of sugar solution, time. (3m)","变量：操纵=温度；响应=气球大小；固定=酵母量、糖溶液体积、时间"],["Apparatus and materials: conical flasks, balloons, water bath, thermometer, yeast, sugar solution, measuring cylinder, stopwatch, ruler. (1m)","仪器与材料"],["Procedure: 1 Mix yeast with sugar solution in flasks. 2 Place the flasks in water baths of 20, 30, 40 and 60 degrees C. 3 Cover each flask mouth with a balloon. 4 After 30 minutes measure the diameter of each balloon. (2m)","步骤：酵母加糖液，置于不同温度水浴，套气球，30分钟后测直径"],["Observation: the balloon is largest at around 40 degrees C and does not inflate at 60 degrees C. Conclusion: the activity of yeast increases with temperature up to an optimum; the gas is carbon dioxide (lime water turns cloudy). (2m)","观察：约40度最大，60度不膨胀；结论：至最适温度前活性增加；气体为CO₂（石灰水变浑浊）"]],"华文：60度酶被破坏，酵母死亡。","Tip: explain the result at high temperature: enzymes in yeast are denatured."],["Beneficial Microorganisms: Biotechnology and Environment","有益微生物：生物科技与环境",[["Medicine: Penicillium fungus produces the antibiotic penicillin; genetically modified bacteria produce human insulin and vaccines.","医药：青霉菌产生青霉素；转基因细菌生产胰岛素"],["Energy: bacteria decompose organic waste (animal dung, food waste) without oxygen to produce biogas (mainly methane) for cooking and electricity.","能源：细菌分解有机废物产生沼气（甲烷）"],["Agriculture: nitrogen-fixing bacteria in root nodules and in the soil increase soil fertility; biofertilisers and biopesticides replace chemicals.","农业：固氮菌提高土壤肥力；生物肥料和生物农药"],["Environment: decomposers (bacteria and fungi) break down dead organisms and return nutrients to the soil; bacteria are used in sewage treatment and to break down oil spills (bioremediation).","环境：分解者、污水处理、生物修复"]],"华文：微生物是生态系统的分解者。","Tip: write the microorganism, what it does and the benefit."],["Harmful Microorganisms and Diseases","有害微生物与疾病",[["Bacteria: cholera, typhoid, tuberculosis (TB), tetanus, food poisoning (Salmonella).","细菌：霍乱、伤寒、肺结核、破伤风、食物中毒"],["Viruses: influenza, dengue, COVID-19, HIV/AIDS, measles, hepatitis.","病毒：流感、登革热、新冠、艾滋病、麻疹"],["Fungi: athlete's foot, ringworm; Protozoa: malaria (Plasmodium), amoebic dysentery.","真菌：脚癣、体癣；原生动物：疟疾、阿米巴痢疾"],["Food spoilage: microorganisms digest food, producing bad smell, sour taste and slime; some release toxins that cause food poisoning.","食物变质：产生异味、酸味、黏液；毒素致食物中毒"],["Mould on stored crops can produce toxins (e.g. aflatoxin) that damage the liver.","霉菌毒素损害肝脏"]],"华文：每种病写出病原体类型。","Tip: state the pathogen type, e.g. 'dengue is caused by a virus'."],["How Diseases Spread","疾病如何传播",[["Air (droplets): influenza, TB, COVID-19 spread through coughing and sneezing.","空气（飞沫）：流感、肺结核、新冠"],["Contaminated food and water: cholera, typhoid, food poisoning.","受污染的食物和水：霍乱、伤寒"],["Vectors: Aedes mosquito spreads dengue; Anopheles mosquito spreads malaria. A vector is an animal that carries the pathogen from one host to another.","媒介：伊蚊传登革热；按蚊传疟疾"],["Direct contact and body fluids: ringworm, HIV, hepatitis B.","接触与体液：体癣、艾滋病、乙肝"],["Cuts and wounds exposed to soil: tetanus.","伤口接触泥土：破伤风"]],"华文：媒介 = 传播病原体的动物。","Tip: for each disease, name the method of transmission."],["Body Defence and Immunity (F + H)","身体防御与免疫（F + H）",[["F1 Skin acts as a barrier. H: it prevents pathogens from entering the body; mucus and hair in the nose trap microorganisms.","F1 皮肤屏障。H：阻止病原体进入；鼻黏液和鼻毛捕捉"],["F2 Stomach acid (hydrochloric acid). H: kills microorganisms in food and drink.","F2 胃酸。H：杀死食物中的微生物"],["F3 White blood cells (phagocytes) engulf and digest pathogens. H: this destroys pathogens that have entered the body.","F3 吞噬细胞吞噬病原体。H：消灭进入的病原体"],["F4 White blood cells (lymphocytes) produce antibodies. H: antibodies attach to specific pathogens and destroy them or make them clump together.","F4 淋巴细胞产生抗体。H：抗体特异性结合并破坏病原体"],["F5 Memory cells remain after infection. H: the body responds faster and stronger on the next infection by the same pathogen (immunity).","F5 记忆细胞。H：再次感染时反应更快更强"]],"华文：抗体是特异的，一种抗体对付一种病原体。","Tip: antibodies are specific to one type of pathogen; write this for full marks."],["Vaccination (F + H)","疫苗接种（F + H）",[["F1 A vaccine contains weakened or dead pathogens (or their parts). H: they stimulate white blood cells to produce antibodies without causing the disease.","F1 疫苗含减弱/死亡病原体。H：刺激产生抗体而不致病"],["F2 Memory cells are formed. H: if the real pathogen enters later, antibodies are produced quickly and in large amounts, so the person does not fall sick.","F2 形成记忆细胞。H：真病原体入侵时快速大量产生抗体"],["F3 Some vaccines need booster doses. H: to maintain a high level of antibodies and long-lasting immunity.","F3 部分疫苗需加强针。H：维持抗体水平"],["F4 Herd immunity: when most people are vaccinated. H: the spread of the disease is slowed, protecting those who cannot be vaccinated.","F4 群体免疫。H：减缓传播，保护无法接种者"],["Examples of vaccines: BCG (TB), MMR (measles, mumps, rubella), polio, hepatitis B, COVID-19.","疫苗例子：卡介苗、麻腮风、小儿麻痹、乙肝、新冠"]],"华文：疫苗预防，不是治疗。","Tip: vaccination gives active immunity because the body makes its own antibodies."],["Prevention of Diseases and Spread (F + H)","疾病预防与阻断传播（F + H）",[["F1 Wash hands with soap and keep food covered. H: to remove or prevent pathogens from reaching food and the mouth.","F1 用肥皂洗手、食物加盖。H：去除/阻止病原体"],["F2 Wear a mask and cover the mouth when coughing. H: to prevent droplets containing pathogens from spreading through the air.","F2 戴口罩、咳嗽掩口。H：阻止飞沫传播"],["F3 Drink boiled or treated water. H: heat and chlorine kill pathogens in the water.","F3 喝煮沸或处理过的水。H：高温和氯杀菌"],["F4 Destroy the breeding places of mosquitoes (empty stagnant water) and use repellent or nets. H: to break the life cycle of the vector and prevent bites.","F4 清除积水、使用驱蚊剂蚊帐。H：切断媒介生命周期"],["F5 Quarantine and isolation of infected people. H: to prevent the pathogen from infecting others.","F5 隔离感染者。H：防止传染他人"],["Food preservation (drying, freezing, canning, adding salt or sugar). H: removes the growth conditions of microorganisms.","食物保存。H：破坏微生物生长条件"]],"华文：预防 = 阻断传播途径。","Tip: give an action, then 'to prevent ...' or 'to kill ...'."],["Treating Infections: Antibiotics and Resistance (F + H)","治疗感染：抗生素与抗药性（F + H）",[["F1 Antibiotics (e.g. penicillin) are used for bacterial infections. H: they kill bacteria or stop them from growing, but do not work against viruses.","F1 抗生素治细菌感染。H：杀死或抑制细菌，对病毒无效"],["F2 Viral diseases are treated with antiviral drugs, rest and plenty of fluids. H: antiviral drugs reduce virus reproduction; vaccines prevent them.","F2 病毒病用抗病毒药、休息、多喝水"],["F3 Fungal infections use antifungal cream; malaria uses antimalarial drugs.","F3 真菌用抗真菌药；疟疾用抗疟药"],["F4 The patient must complete the full course of antibiotics. H: to kill all the bacteria, otherwise the surviving bacteria multiply and may become resistant.","F4 必须吃完疗程。H：否则幸存细菌繁殖并产生抗药性"],["F5 Antibiotics must not be overused or taken without prescription. H: overuse allows resistant bacteria to survive and spread (e.g. MRSA), so the drugs no longer work.","F5 不可滥用。H：抗药细菌存活扩散（如MRSA）"]],"华文：抗药性是细菌的问题，不是人的问题。","Tip: bacteria become resistant to antibiotics; the person does not become resistant."],["Investigation: Effect of Antibiotics on the Growth of Bacteria","探究：抗生素对细菌生长的影响",[["Aim: to study the effect of different antibiotics on the growth of bacteria. Problem statement: do different antibiotics affect the growth of bacteria differently? (1m)","目的：研究不同抗生素对细菌生长的影响"],["Hypothesis: the larger the clear zone around an antibiotic disc, the more effective the antibiotic. (1m)","假设：抗生素圆片周围透明圈越大，越有效"],["Variables: manipulated = type of antibiotic; responding = diameter of clear zone; fixed = type of bacteria, agar, volume, incubation time and temperature. (3m)","变量：操纵=抗生素种类；响应=透明圈直径；固定=细菌种类、培养基、时间、温度"],["Apparatus and materials: sterile Petri dishes with nutrient agar, bacterial culture, sterile cotton swab, antibiotic discs A, B, C, forceps, incubator, ruler. (1m)","仪器与材料"],["Procedure: 1 Spread the bacteria evenly on the agar with a sterile swab. 2 Place discs A, B and C on the agar using sterile forceps. 3 Seal the dish with tape and incubate upside down at 30 degrees C for 24 to 48 hours. 4 Measure the diameter of each clear zone. (2m)","步骤：涂布细菌，放圆片，封口倒置培养，测透明圈"],["Observation: clear zones of different sizes appear around the discs. Conclusion: the antibiotic with the largest clear zone is the most effective in inhibiting bacterial growth. (2m)","观察：透明圈大小不同；结论：透明圈最大者最有效"]],"华文：透明圈 = 没有细菌生长的区域。","Tip: state the clear zone is where bacteria did not grow because the antibiotic diffused into the agar."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Microorganisms","示例题：试卷2 A部分（微生物）",[["(a) [1] Name the microorganism that makes dough rise. Scheme: yeast (1m).","(a)酵母菌"],["(b) [2] State two conditions needed for the growth of bacteria. Scheme: warmth / suitable temperature (1m); moisture / nutrients (1m).","(b)细菌生长两个条件"],["(c) [2] Why must the inoculating loop be heated until red hot before use? Scheme: to kill unwanted microorganisms (1m); to prevent contamination of the culture (1m).","(c)接种环灼烧：杀死杂菌；防污染"],["(d) [3] Explain how a vaccine protects a person. Scheme: contains weakened pathogens (1m); stimulates the production of antibodies / memory cells (1m); body responds faster when the pathogen enters (1m).","(d)疫苗如何保护人体"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Controlling Disease (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（疾病控制）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain two ways to prevent the spread of dengue. Scheme: destroy stagnant water (1m) to break the breeding of Aedes mosquitoes (1m); use repellent / mosquito net (1m) to prevent bites from the vector (1m).","(a)预防登革热两种方法"],["(b) [2] A patient with influenza asks for antibiotics. Explain why they are not suitable. Scheme: influenza is caused by a virus (1m); antibiotics only work against bacteria (1m).","(b)流感不适用抗生素：病毒；抗生素只对细菌有效"],["(c) [KBAT, 4] A student stops taking antibiotics after 2 days because she feels better. Justify why this is unwise. Scheme: some bacteria remain alive (1m); they multiply and the infection returns (1m); surviving bacteria may become resistant (1m); the antibiotic will no longer be effective (1m).","(c)为何不应提前停药：残留细菌繁殖，可能产生抗药性"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying antibiotics can cure viral diseases such as flu. Correct: antibiotics work only against bacteria.","错误：抗生素治病毒。正确：只对细菌有效"],["Mistake: writing that viruses are cells or can grow on agar alone. Correct: viruses are not cells and reproduce only inside living host cells.","错误：病毒是细胞。正确：非细胞，需宿主"],["Mistake: saying a vaccine cures the disease. Correct: a vaccine prevents the disease by producing antibodies and memory cells.","错误：疫苗治病。正确：疫苗预防"],["Mistake: saying 'the person becomes resistant to antibiotics'. Correct: the bacteria become resistant.","错误：人产生抗药性。正确：细菌产生抗药性"],["Mistake: in aseptic technique, giving only the action. Correct: add the reason, 'to prevent contamination'.","错误：无菌技术只写做法。正确：加上原因"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Why can viruses not be treated with antibiotics? J: Antibiotics only kill bacteria; viruses are not cells.","问：为何抗生素治不了病毒？答：抗生素只杀细菌，病毒不是细胞"],["S: Name the microorganism used to make yoghurt. J: Lactobacillus (lactic acid bacteria).","问：制作酸奶的微生物？答：乳酸菌"],["S: What does a clear zone around an antibiotic disc show? J: The antibiotic inhibits the growth of bacteria.","问：透明圈代表什么？答：抗生素抑制细菌生长"],["S: How does a vaccine give immunity? J: It stimulates the body to produce antibodies and memory cells.","问：疫苗如何产生免疫？答：刺激产生抗体和记忆细胞"],["S: Why should the Petri dish be incubated upside down? J: To prevent water drops from falling onto the agar and contaminating it.","问：培养皿为何倒置？答：防止水珠滴落到琼脂"],["S: What is a vector? J: An animal that carries pathogens from one host to another, e.g. Aedes mosquito.","问：什么是媒介？答：携带病原体传给其他宿主的动物，如伊蚊"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-2":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Balanced diet: a diet that contains all the nutrients (carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, fibre and water) in the right amounts and proportions.","均衡饮食：各类营养素份量和比例适当"],["Calorific value (energy value) of food: the amount of energy released when 1 g of food is completely burnt (unit kJ/g).","食物热量值：1克食物完全燃烧所释放的能量"],["Body Mass Index (BMI): a value that shows whether a person's body mass is suitable for his or her height.","身体质量指数：显示体重与身高是否相称"],["Nitrogen fixation: the conversion of nitrogen gas into nitrogen compounds (nitrates / ammonium) that plants can absorb.","固氮：把氮气转变为植物可吸收的氮化合物"],["Food processing: the methods used to change raw food into other forms or to make it last longer. Food additive: a substance added to food to preserve it or to improve its taste, colour or texture.","食品加工；食品添加剂"],["Hydroponics: growing plants in a nutrient solution without soil.","水培：不用土壤，用营养液种植"]],"华文：定义要写关键词：1 g、完全燃烧、kJ/g。","Tip: for calorific value always include '1 g of food' and 'completely burnt'."],["Nutrients and Their Functions","营养素及其功能",[["Carbohydrates: main source of energy (rice, bread, noodles). Proteins: growth and repair of cells and tissues (fish, egg, beans).","碳水化合物：主要能量来源；蛋白质：生长与修复细胞"],["Fats: source of concentrated energy, insulate the body, store energy. Vitamins and minerals: needed in small amounts for health.","脂肪：高能量，保温，储能；维生素和矿物质：少量但必需"],["Fibre: prevents constipation by helping the movement of food in the intestine (fruits, vegetables). Water: solvent, transport, regulates body temperature.","纤维：防便秘；水：溶剂、运输、调节体温"],["Vitamin C: healthy gums and skin. Vitamin D and calcium: strong bones and teeth. Iron: forms haemoglobin in red blood cells.","维生素C；维生素D与钙；铁：制造血红蛋白"]],"华文：每种营养素都要配「食物例子 + 功能」。","Tip: name the nutrient, one food source and one function."],["Balanced Diet and Food Pyramid","均衡饮食与食物金字塔",[["Food pyramid: eat the largest amount of foods at the base (rice, bread, cereals), then fruits and vegetables, then fish, meat, eggs, beans and milk.","食物金字塔：底层吃最多（米饭、面包、谷类）"],["Eat fats, oil, sugar and salt in small amounts (top of the pyramid).","油、糖、盐吃最少（塔尖）"],["Calorie needs depend on age, gender, body size, type of activity and health condition (e.g. a pregnant woman needs more).","热量需求取决于年龄、性别、体型、活动量、健康状况"],["A balanced diet gives enough energy and nutrients without excess; excess unhealthy calories lead to obesity, heart disease and diabetes.","过量不健康热量导致肥胖、心脏病、糖尿病"]],"华文：设计菜单题要符合金字塔比例。","Tip: when planning a meal, name food from each group and give the amount (more / less)."],["Calorific Value: Formula","食物热量值：公式",[["Energy released by food = energy absorbed by water: \\(Q = m c \\theta\\), where m = mass of water (g), c = specific heat capacity of water = 4.2 J g\\(^{-1}\\) \\(^\\circ\\)C\\(^{-1}\\), \\(\\theta\\) = rise in temperature (\\(^\\circ\\)C).","食物释放的热 = 水吸收的热：Q = mcθ"],["Calorific value \\(= \\dfrac{Q}{\\text{mass of food burnt (g)}}\\) in J g\\(^{-1}\\); divide by 1000 to get kJ g\\(^{-1}\\).","热量值 = Q ÷ 食物质量（J/g）；除以1000得kJ/g"],["Mass of water is taken as: 1 cm\\(^3\\) of water = 1 g.","1 cm³ 水 = 1 g"],["Mass of food burnt = mass before burning minus mass after burning.","燃烧的食物质量 = 燃烧前 − 燃烧后"],["Total energy intake of a person = sum of (mass of each food \\(\\times\\) its calorific value).","总能量摄入 = Σ（食物质量 × 热量值）"]],"华文：单位要换算：J → kJ 要除以1000。","Tip: write formula, substitution and answer with unit (kJ g\\(^{-1}\\)); each step carries a mark."],["Worked Example: Calorific Value","计算示例：热量值",[["Question: 0.5 g of a nut is burnt completely and heats 100 cm\\(^3\\) of water from 30 \\(^\\circ\\)C to 45 \\(^\\circ\\)C. Calculate the calorific value of the nut. (c = 4.2 J g\\(^{-1}\\) \\(^\\circ\\)C\\(^{-1}\\))","题目：0.5 g坚果加热100 cm³水，30°C升到45°C"],["Step 1: mass of water = 100 g; rise in temperature = 45 - 30 = 15 \\(^\\circ\\)C. (1m)","第1步：水100 g；升温15°C"],["Step 2: \\(Q = mc\\theta = 100 \\times 4.2 \\times 15 = 6300\\) J. (1m)","第2步：Q = 100 × 4.2 × 15 = 6300 J"],["Step 3: calorific value \\(= 6300 \\div 0.5 = 12600\\) J g\\(^{-1}\\). (1m)","第3步：6300 ÷ 0.5 = 12600 J/g"],["Answer: 12.6 kJ g\\(^{-1}\\). (1m, with unit)","答案：12.6 kJ/g（要有单位）"]],"华文：先求Q，再除以食物质量。","Tip: do not forget to divide by the mass of the food, not the mass of water."],["Investigation: Calorific Value of Food","探究：食物的热量值",[["Aim: to determine the calorific value of different foods. Problem statement: do different types of food have different calorific values? Hypothesis: food with more fat has a higher calorific value. (1m each)","目的、问题陈述、假设：脂肪越多，热量值越高"],["Variables: manipulated = type of food; responding = rise in temperature of water (calorific value); fixed = mass of food, volume of water, distance between flame and boiling tube. (3m)","变量：操纵=食物种类；响应=水温升高；固定=食物质量、水体积、火焰距离"],["Apparatus and materials: boiling tube, retort stand, thermometer, wire holder, balance, measuring cylinder, peanut, cashew nut, bread. (1m)","仪器材料：试管、铁架、温度计、天平、量筒、各种食物"],["Procedure: 1 Pour 20 cm\\(^3\\) of water into a boiling tube and record its initial temperature. 2 Weigh the food and light it. 3 Hold the burning food under the tube until it stops burning, stirring the water with the thermometer. 4 Record the highest temperature. 5 Repeat with other foods using fresh water. (2m)","步骤：量水、称食物、点燃加热、记录最高温、换食物重复"],["Observation: the rise in temperature is greatest for the peanut (high fat). Conclusion: food with more fat has a higher calorific value; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察与结论：花生温升最大；假设被接受"],["Source of error: some heat is lost to the surroundings, so the value obtained is lower than the actual value. Improve: shield the flame from wind, place the tube close to the flame, use a lid or insulation. (2m)","误差：热量散失，结果偏低；改进：挡风、靠近火焰、隔热"]],"华文：热量实验的结果总是偏低。","Tip: state that heat is lost to the surroundings, so the experimental value is lower than the actual value."],["Body Mass Index (BMI)","身体质量指数（BMI）",[["Formula: \\(\\text{BMI} = \\dfrac{\\text{mass (kg)}}{\\text{height (m)}^2}\\). Unit: kg m\\(^{-2}\\).","公式：BMI = 体重(kg) ÷ 身高(m)²"],["Classification for adults: below 18.5 underweight; 18.5 to 24.9 normal; 25.0 to 29.9 overweight; 30.0 and above obese.","成人分类：<18.5 过轻；18.5–24.9 正常；25–29.9 过重；≥30 肥胖"],["Worked example: mass = 60 kg, height = 1.60 m. BMI = \\(60 \\div (1.60)^2 = 60 \\div 2.56 = 23.4\\) kg m\\(^{-2}\\). (2m)","示例：60 ÷ 2.56 = 23.4"],["Conclusion: 23.4 lies between 18.5 and 24.9, so the person has a normal body mass. (1m)","结论：在18.5至24.9之间，体重正常"],["Height must be in metres: convert 160 cm to 1.60 m before calculating.","身高必须换算成米"]],"华文：不同来源的分类略有差异，考试按题目提供的表格。","Tip: always compare the BMI value with the given range and state the category."],["Effects of an Unbalanced Diet","饮食不均衡的影响",[["Eating too much: obesity, high blood pressure, heart disease, type 2 diabetes.","吃太多：肥胖、高血压、心脏病、糖尿病"],["Eating too little or lacking nutrients (malnutrition): underweight, weak body, poor growth.","营养不良：过轻、虚弱、生长不良"],["Deficiency diseases: lack of vitamin C causes scurvy; vitamin D causes rickets; iron causes anaemia; iodine causes goitre; protein causes kwashiorkor.","缺乏症：维C坏血病；维D佝偻病；铁贫血；碘甲状腺肿；蛋白质夸希奥科病"],["Prevention: balanced diet, regular exercise, less sugar, salt and fat, and regular health check-ups.","预防：均衡饮食、运动、少糖盐油、定期检查"]],"华文：配对题：营养素 ↔ 缺乏症。","Tip: match each nutrient with its deficiency disease exactly."],["Nutrients in Plants","植物的营养",[["Macronutrients (needed in large amounts): nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium, calcium, magnesium, sulphur.","大量元素：氮、磷、钾、钙、镁、硫"],["Micronutrients (small amounts): iron, manganese, zinc, copper, boron.","微量元素：铁、锰、锌、铜、硼"],["Nitrogen deficiency: yellow leaves and stunted growth. Phosphorus deficiency: poor root growth. Potassium deficiency: yellow leaf edges.","缺氮：叶黄、矮小；缺磷：根差；缺钾：叶缘黄"],["Magnesium deficiency: leaves yellow between the veins (magnesium is needed to make chlorophyll).","缺镁：叶脉间变黄（镁用于制造叶绿素）"],["Fertilisers supply the missing nutrients; too much fertiliser pollutes water.","肥料补充养分；过量会污染水源"]],"华文：症状 ↔ 元素配对必背。","Tip: link symptom to nutrient, e.g. 'nitrogen is needed for protein and growth'."],["Investigation: Plant Nutrient Deficiency","探究：植物缺乏养分",[["Aim: to study the effect of a lack of a mineral on the growth of a plant. Hypothesis: a plant lacking nitrogen has yellow leaves and stunted growth. (2m)","目的与假设：缺氮植物叶黄、矮小"],["Variables: manipulated = type of culture solution (complete / without nitrogen); responding = colour of leaves and growth of the plant; fixed = type and size of seedling, amount of light, volume of solution. (3m)","变量：操纵=营养液种类；响应=叶色与生长；固定=幼苗、光照、溶液体积"],["Apparatus and materials: two beakers (or bottles) wrapped in black paper, cotton wool, two similar seedlings, complete culture solution, culture solution without nitrogen. (1m)","仪器材料：两个杯、棉花、幼苗、完整营养液、缺氮营养液"],["Procedure: 1 Fill one bottle with complete solution and the other with solution without nitrogen. 2 Place a seedling in each, held by cotton wool. 3 Leave both in the same sunlight for two weeks and observe. (2m)","步骤：分别装两种溶液，放幼苗，同条件放置两周观察"],["Observation: the seedling in complete solution grows healthily; the seedling without nitrogen has yellow leaves and is stunted. (1m)","观察：完整营养液幼苗健康；缺氮的叶黄矮小"],["Conclusion: nitrogen is needed for healthy leaves and growth; the hypothesis is accepted. (1m)","结论：氮是健康生长所需；假设被接受"]],"华文：用黑纸包住瓶子，防止藻类生长。","Tip: say the container is wrapped to prevent light from reaching the solution (stops algae growth)."],["Nitrogen Cycle","氮循环",[["Nitrogen fixation: lightning and nitrogen-fixing bacteria (in root nodules of legumes and in soil) change nitrogen gas into nitrates or ammonium.","固氮：闪电和固氮菌（豆科根瘤、土壤）把氮气变成硝酸盐/铵"],["Nitrification: nitrifying bacteria change ammonium into nitrite and then nitrate; plants absorb nitrates.","硝化：硝化细菌把铵变成亚硝酸盐再变硝酸盐；植物吸收"],["Plants make proteins from nitrates; animals get nitrogen by eating plants or other animals.","植物用硝酸盐制造蛋白质；动物靠进食获得氮"],["Decomposition: decomposers change dead organisms and waste into ammonium compounds.","分解：分解者把遗体和废物变成铵化合物"],["Denitrification: denitrifying bacteria change nitrates back into nitrogen gas, which returns to the air.","反硝化：反硝化细菌把硝酸盐变回氮气"]],"华文：画图时标出：固氮、硝化、分解、反硝化。","Tip: name the process, the organisms involved and the substance formed."],["Nitrogen Cycle and Fertilisers (F + H)","氮循环与肥料（F + H）",[["F1 Legumes are planted in rotation with other crops. H: nitrogen-fixing bacteria in their root nodules add nitrates to the soil.","F1 豆科作物轮作。H：根瘤固氮菌增加土壤硝酸盐"],["F2 Farmers add nitrogen fertilisers to the soil. H: to replace the nitrates absorbed by plants so that crops grow well.","F2 施氮肥。H：补充被作物吸收的硝酸盐"],["F3 Waterlogged soil has less nitrate. H: denitrifying bacteria change nitrates into nitrogen gas.","F3 积水土壤硝酸盐少。H：反硝化细菌把硝酸盐变为氮气"],["F4 Too much fertiliser washed into rivers is harmful. H: it causes eutrophication, so oxygen in the water decreases and aquatic organisms die.","F4 过量肥料流入河流有害。H：富营养化，水中缺氧，水生生物死亡"]],"华文：F + H 每点2分。","Tip: give the action (F) and the reason using the bacteria or process involved (H)."],["Food Production Technology","食物生产科技",[["Selective breeding: crossing organisms with good characteristics to produce offspring with high yield or disease resistance.","选择性育种：杂交有优良特性的生物"],["Genetic modification (GM): a gene from one organism is transferred into another to give a useful trait (e.g. pest-resistant crops). Benefit: higher yield; concern: effects on health and environment are still debated.","转基因：转移基因获得有用性状；有利有弊"],["Hydroponics: plants grow in nutrient solution; saves space and water, no soil pests, quality can be controlled.","水培：省空间和水、无土壤害虫、可控品质"],["Fertilisers and modern farming (greenhouse, drip irrigation) increase quality and quantity of food.","肥料和现代耕作（温室、滴灌）提高质量与产量"],["Aquaculture: breeding fish and other water organisms in controlled ponds or cages to ensure a steady food supply.","水产养殖：在受控池塘/网箱养殖"]],"华文：评价题要说优点和缺点。","Tip: for each technology give one advantage and one disadvantage."],["Pest Control: Chemical vs Biological (F + H)","害虫防治：化学 vs 生物（F + H）",[["F1 Chemical pesticides kill pests quickly. H: they act fast and are easy to use over a large area.","F1 杀虫剂见效快。H：快速、大面积易用"],["F2 Chemical pesticides can harm the environment. H: they poison non-target organisms, pollute soil and water, and pests may become resistant.","F2 杀虫剂危害环境。H：毒害非目标生物、污染水土、害虫产生抗药性"],["F3 Biological control uses natural predators (e.g. owls to control rats). H: it is environmentally friendly and does not leave chemical residue.","F3 生物防治用天敌（如猫头鹰控制老鼠）。H：环保、无残留"],["F4 Biological control is slow and may not remove all pests. H: the number of predators must increase first, and the predator may itself become a pest.","F4 生物防治较慢。H：天敌数量要先增加，天敌也可能成为害虫"]],"华文：标准答案：快 vs 环保。","Tip: compare both methods using 'faster than' / 'safer for the environment than'."],["Food Processing and Preservation","食品加工与保存",[["Principle: food spoils because microorganisms grow in it. Preservation slows or stops their growth.","原理：微生物生长导致食物变坏；保存即抑制其生长"],["Cooling and freezing: low temperature slows growth of microorganisms. Drying: removes water, so microorganisms cannot grow (dried fish, raisins).","冷藏冷冻：低温减缓；干燥：去除水分"],["Salting and sugaring: high concentration draws water out of microorganisms by osmosis (salted fish, jam). Pickling: acid (vinegar) kills or prevents growth.","盐渍/糖渍：渗透作用使微生物失水；腌渍：酸抑制"],["Canning: food is heated and sealed in an airtight can. Pasteurisation: heating milk at a moderate temperature for a short time to kill harmful bacteria.","罐装：加热后密封；巴氏杀菌：中温短时杀菌"],["Fermentation: microorganisms change food into new products (yoghurt, tempeh, soy sauce, bread).","发酵：微生物把食物变成新产品（酸奶、豆豉、酱油）"]],"华文：每种方法都要说出「如何抑制微生物」。","Tip: give the method and how it stops microorganisms, e.g. 'removes water'."],["Food Additives and Health Foods","食品添加剂与保健食品",[["Preservatives (e.g. sodium benzoate): slow the growth of microorganisms. Antioxidants: prevent fats from going rancid.","防腐剂：减缓微生物生长；抗氧化剂：防止油脂变坏"],["Colouring and flavouring: improve appearance and taste. Stabilisers and emulsifiers: keep the texture even.","色素、香料：改善外观和味道；稳定剂、乳化剂：保持质地"],["Misuse of additives can cause allergies and health problems; read the label and choose foods with approved additives.","滥用添加剂可致过敏；要看标签"],["Health foods and supplements (e.g. vitamins, fish oil, probiotics): helpful when diet is lacking, but must not be overdosed.","保健食品与补充品：饮食不足时有帮助，不可过量"],["Halal food: ingredients and processing must follow Islamic requirements; check the halal logo.","清真食品：成分与过程符合规定；认清清真标志"]],"华文：了解清真标志与标签阅读即可。","Tip: give the additive, its function and one possible risk."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Nutrition and Food","示例题：试卷2 A部分（营养与食物）",[["(a) [1] State one function of protein in the body. Scheme: growth and repair of cells / tissues (1m).","(a)蛋白质功能：生长与修复"],["(b) [3] A student weighs 72 kg and is 1.60 m tall. Calculate his BMI. Scheme: formula mass / height squared (1m); 72 / 2.56 (1m); 28.1 kg m\\(^{-2}\\) (1m, with unit).","(b)BMI计算：72 ÷ 2.56 = 28.1"],["(c) [1] State the category of his body mass. Scheme: overweight (28.1 lies between 25.0 and 29.9) (1m).","(c)属于过重"],["(d) [2] Why is the calorific value found in a food experiment lower than the actual value? Scheme: heat is lost to the surroundings (1m); not all the heat is absorbed by the water (1m).","(d)实验值偏低：热量散失到周围；水未吸收全部热"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Food Preservation and Farming (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（食品保存与农业）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how salting and canning preserve food. Scheme: salting: high salt concentration (1m) draws water out of microorganisms by osmosis so they cannot grow (1m); canning: heating kills microorganisms (1m) and airtight seal prevents new ones entering (1m).","(a)盐渍与罐装如何保存食物"],["(b) [4] A farmer has a pest problem in his vegetable farm. Compare the use of insecticide and biological control. Scheme: insecticide kills pests faster (1m) but pollutes the environment / kills non-target organisms (1m); biological control is friendly to the environment (1m) but slower (1m).","(b)比较杀虫剂和生物防治"],["(c) [KBAT, 2] Suggest and justify a method to increase the yield of crops on a small piece of land. Scheme: hydroponics / greenhouse (1m); saves space and water and the nutrients can be controlled (1m).","(c)建议并说明：水培/温室，省空间水，可控养分"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: calculating calorific value by dividing by the mass of water. Correct: divide the energy by the mass of the food burnt.","错误：除以水的质量。正确：除以食物质量"],["Mistake: using height in cm for BMI. Correct: convert to metres (160 cm = 1.60 m) and square it.","错误：身高用厘米。正确：换成米并平方"],["Mistake: forgetting units (J g\\(^{-1}\\), kJ g\\(^{-1}\\), kg m\\(^{-2}\\)). Correct: write the unit in the final answer.","错误：漏写单位。正确：答案要有单位"],["Mistake: writing only 'kills bacteria' for every preservation method. Correct: state how, e.g. salting draws out water by osmosis; drying removes water.","错误：每种方法都写杀菌。正确：写具体原理"],["Mistake: saying nitrogen gas is absorbed by plants. Correct: plants absorb nitrates.","错误：植物吸收氮气。正确：植物吸收硝酸盐"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Write the formula of BMI. J: BMI = mass (kg) / height squared (m\\(^2\\)).","问：BMI公式？答：体重(kg) ÷ 身高(m)²"],["S: Calculate the calorific value if 0.4 g food releases 5040 J. J: 5040 / 0.4 = 12600 J per g = 12.6 kJ per g.","问：0.4 g食物释放5040 J，热量值？答：12600 J/g = 12.6 kJ/g"],["S: Symptom of nitrogen deficiency in plants? J: Yellow leaves and stunted growth.","问：缺氮症状？答：叶黄、生长迟缓"],["S: Which bacteria change nitrates into nitrogen gas? J: Denitrifying bacteria.","问：哪种细菌把硝酸盐变回氮气？答：反硝化细菌"],["S: How does drying preserve food? J: It removes water so microorganisms cannot grow.","问：干燥如何保存食物？答：去除水分，微生物无法生长"],["S: Why is the experimental calorific value lower than the actual value? J: Heat is lost to the surroundings.","问：为什么实验值偏低？答：热量散失到周围"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-3":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Pollution: the presence of harmful substances (pollutants) in the environment that damage living things and the environment.","污染：环境中有害物质损害生物与环境"],["Carbon footprint: the total amount of greenhouse gases (mainly carbon dioxide) released by an activity, person or product during its life cycle.","碳足迹：活动/产品整个生命周期排放的温室气体总量"],["Product life cycle: all the stages of a product from raw materials, manufacturing, transport and use to disposal.","产品生命周期：从原料、制造、运输、使用到处置"],["Sustainability: using resources to meet the needs of the present without harming the ability of future generations to meet their needs.","可持续：满足当代需求而不损害后代满足需求的能力"],["Conservation: wise use and management of natural resources so they last. Preservation: protecting an area and keeping it untouched.","保育：明智管理资源；保存：保护并保持原状"],["3R: Reduce, Reuse, Recycle.","3R：减少、再用、回收"]],"华文：定义用关键词：greenhouse gases、life cycle、future generations。","Tip: carbon footprint must mention greenhouse gases released."],["Product Life Cycle","产品生命周期",[["Stage 1 raw materials: extracting or growing materials uses energy and may destroy habitats.","第1阶段原料：开采或种植耗能，可能破坏栖息地"],["Stage 2 manufacturing: factories use energy and release waste, gases and heat.","第2阶段制造：耗能，排放废物和气体"],["Stage 3 transport and packaging: burning fuel releases carbon dioxide; packaging creates waste.","第3阶段运输与包装：燃油排放CO₂；包装产生废物"],["Stage 4 use: some products use electricity or fuel while being used (e.g. car, refrigerator).","第4阶段使用：部分产品使用时耗电或燃油"],["Stage 5 disposal: landfill, burning or recycling; plastics take a very long time to decompose.","第5阶段处置：填埋、焚烧、回收；塑料分解极慢"]],"华文：每阶段都要说出对环境的影响。","Tip: name the stage and state one environmental effect."],["Carbon Footprint (F + H)","碳足迹（F + H）",[["F1 Each stage of the life cycle uses energy from burning fossil fuels. H: this releases carbon dioxide, so the product has a carbon footprint.","F1 各阶段耗用化石燃料能源。H：释放CO₂形成碳足迹"],["F2 Buy local products. H: shorter transport distance, so less fuel is burnt and less carbon dioxide is released.","F2 买本地产品。H：运输距离短，燃油少，CO₂少"],["F3 Use reusable bags and recycled materials. H: less raw material and energy are needed for manufacturing.","F3 用环保袋、回收材料。H：减少原料和能源"],["F4 Repair and reuse products. H: the life of the product is longer, so fewer new products are made and less waste is thrown away.","F4 维修再用。H：延长寿命，减少新产品和废物"]],"华文：F + H 每点2分。","Tip: link the action to 'less fuel burnt' or 'less carbon dioxide released'."],["Water Pollution","水污染",[["Sources: domestic sewage and detergents, industrial waste (heavy metals, chemicals), oil spills, agricultural fertilisers and pesticides, rubbish.","来源：生活污水、洗涤剂、工业废物、漏油、肥料农药、垃圾"],["Effects: aquatic organisms die, water becomes unsafe to drink, food chain is disturbed, diseases such as cholera and typhoid spread.","影响：水生生物死亡、水不安全、食物链受扰、传播霍乱伤寒"],["Oil on the water surface blocks oxygen and sunlight from entering the water.","水面油膜阻挡氧气和阳光进入水中"],["Heavy metals (mercury, lead) accumulate along the food chain and harm humans.","重金属沿食物链累积，伤害人类"],["Indicators of polluted water: bad smell, cloudy, dead fish, low dissolved oxygen.","污染指标：臭味、浑浊、死鱼、溶氧低"]],"华文：来源 + 影响 + 一个解决方法。","Tip: give the source and its effect together, e.g. 'oil spill - blocks oxygen'."],["Eutrophication (F + H)","富营养化（F + H）",[["F1 Fertilisers and detergents wash into rivers and lakes. H: the water becomes rich in nutrients (nitrates and phosphates).","F1 肥料洗涤剂流入河湖。H：水中硝酸盐磷酸盐增多"],["F2 Algae grow very fast (algal bloom). H: the algae cover the surface and block sunlight from the aquatic plants below.","F2 藻类暴增（藻华）。H：遮住阳光，水下植物无法光合"],["F3 Algae and plants die and are decomposed by bacteria. H: bacteria use up dissolved oxygen, so the oxygen level falls.","F3 藻类死亡被细菌分解。H：细菌耗尽溶解氧"],["F4 Fish and other aquatic organisms die. H: they lack oxygen for respiration.","F4 鱼类死亡。H：缺氧无法呼吸"]],"华文：因果链四步，不能跳。","Tip: the chain is nutrients - algal bloom - bacteria use oxygen - organisms die of lack of oxygen."],["Air Pollution","空气污染",[["Carbon monoxide: from incomplete combustion of fuel in vehicles; combines with haemoglobin and reduces oxygen carried by the blood.","一氧化碳：燃料不完全燃烧；与血红蛋白结合，减少携氧"],["Sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides: from burning fossil fuels and factories; cause acid rain and breathing problems.","二氧化硫和氮氧化物：燃烧化石燃料；造成酸雨与呼吸问题"],["Particulates (smoke, dust, ash): cause haze, asthma and lung disease; open burning is a main source of haze.","微粒：造成烟霾、哮喘；露天焚烧是烟霾主因"],["Chlorofluorocarbons (CFC): from old refrigerators and aerosol sprays; damage the ozone layer.","氯氟烃：旧冰箱、喷雾剂；破坏臭氧层"],["Control: use public transport, clean fuel, filters in factory chimneys, enforce laws against open burning.","控制：公共交通、清洁燃料、烟囱过滤、禁止露天焚烧"]],"华文：污染物 ↔ 来源 ↔ 影响 三项配对。","Tip: match pollutant, source and effect in one sentence."],["Acid Rain and Global Warming (F + H)","酸雨与全球暖化（F + H）",[["F1 Sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides dissolve in rainwater. H: they form acidic rain (pH below 5.6) that damages buildings, soil and aquatic life.","F1 SO₂和氮氧化物溶于雨水。H：形成酸雨（pH低于5.6）损害建筑、土壤、水生生物"],["F2 Carbon dioxide and methane are greenhouse gases. H: they trap heat from the Earth in the atmosphere, so the temperature rises (greenhouse effect).","F2 CO₂、甲烷是温室气体。H：把热量困在大气中，温度上升"],["F3 Global warming melts polar ice. H: sea level rises and low-lying areas are flooded.","F3 暖化使极地冰融化。H：海平面上升，低地被淹"],["F4 Climate change causes extreme weather. H: more droughts, floods and storms harm crops and settlements.","F4 气候变化。H：更多干旱、洪水、风暴损害农作物与居住地"]],"华文：酸雨和暖化是两个不同的问题，别混淆。","Tip: acid rain is caused by SO2 and NO2; global warming is caused by CO2 and CH4."],["Ozone Depletion and Soil Pollution","臭氧层破坏与土壤污染",[["The ozone layer absorbs harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation from the Sun.","臭氧层吸收有害紫外线"],["CFC releases chlorine in the upper atmosphere which breaks down ozone; more UV reaches the Earth and causes skin cancer, cataracts and harms crops.","CFC释放氯，破坏臭氧；紫外线增多致皮肤癌、白内障，伤害作物"],["Soil pollution: plastics, pesticides, chemical waste and rubbish; plastics do not decompose and reduce soil fertility.","土壤污染：塑料、农药、化学废物；塑料不分解"],["Harmful chemicals in soil can enter crops and pollute underground water.","有害化学品进入作物，污染地下水"],["Solution: use alternatives to CFC, reduce plastic use, practise 3R.","对策：用CFC替代品、少用塑料、3R"]],"华文：《蒙特利尔议定书》就是为了停止使用CFC。","Tip: state that the ozone layer absorbs UV radiation, and the effect of more UV on health."],["Investigation: Effect of Acid Rain on Seed Germination","探究：酸雨对种子发芽的影响",[["Aim: to study the effect of acidic water on the germination of green bean seeds. Problem statement: does acidic water affect the germination of seeds? Hypothesis: the lower the pH of the water, the fewer the seeds that germinate. (3m)","目的、问题、假设：pH越低，发芽的种子越少"],["Variables: manipulated = pH of water; responding = number of seeds that germinate; fixed = type and number of seeds, volume of water, temperature. (3m)","变量：操纵=水的pH；响应=发芽数；固定=种子种类与数量、水量、温度"],["Apparatus and materials: 4 Petri dishes, cotton wool, green bean seeds, distilled water, dilute acid solutions of different pH, pH meter or pH paper, measuring cylinder. (1m)","仪器材料：培养皿、棉花、绿豆、蒸馏水、不同pH酸液、pH试纸"],["Procedure: 1 Put 10 seeds on wet cotton wool in each dish. 2 Add 10 cm\\(^3\\) of water of pH 7, 5, 4 and 3 to the four dishes. 3 Leave in the same place for 5 days and add the same solution daily. 4 Count the seeds that germinate. (2m)","步骤：每皿10粒种子；加pH 7、5、4、3的水；放置5天；数发芽数"],["Observation: the lower the pH, the fewer the seeds that germinate (tabulate pH and number of germinated seeds). (1m)","观察：pH越低，发芽越少"],["Conclusion: acidic water reduces germination; the hypothesis is accepted. (1m)","结论：酸性水降低发芽率；假设被接受"]],"华文：以蒸馏水（pH 7）作对照。","Tip: say pH 7 water is the control for comparison."],["Conservation and Preservation of the Environment","环境保育与保存",[["Conservation: use natural resources wisely so they last for future generations (e.g. replanting trees after logging, controlled fishing).","保育：明智使用资源（砍伐后再植树、限制捕鱼）"],["Preservation: protect an area from human activity (e.g. national parks, wildlife reserves, marine parks).","保存：保护区域免受人类活动（国家公园、保护区、海洋公园）"],["Importance: protects biodiversity, keeps the balance of ecosystems, provides clean air and water, and supports tourism and research.","重要性：保护生物多样性、生态平衡、清洁空气水源"],["Sustainable development: develop the country without destroying the environment for future generations.","可持续发展：发展而不破坏后代的环境"],["Laws such as the Environmental Quality Act help control pollution in Malaysia.","《环境质量法》帮助控制污染"]],"华文：保育 ≠ 保存，别混淆。","Tip: conservation = wise use; preservation = untouched protection."],["Waste Management and 3R","废物管理与3R",[["Reduce: use less (bring own bag and bottle). Reuse: use again (glass jars, old clothes). Recycle: change waste into new products (paper, glass, metal, plastic).","减少、再用、回收"],["Sort waste at source into paper, plastic, glass, metal and organic waste.","源头分类：纸、塑料、玻璃、金属、有机"],["Composting: organic waste is decomposed by microorganisms into compost for plants.","堆肥：有机废物经微生物变成肥料"],["Landfill needs land and may pollute soil and water. Incineration reduces volume but can release polluting gases if not controlled.","填埋：占地且可能污染；焚烧：减体积，但若不控制会排污气"],["Biodegradable waste decomposes naturally (food, paper); non-biodegradable waste does not (plastic, polystyrene).","可生物降解废物（食物、纸）；不可降解（塑料、泡沫）"]],"华文：给定物品，会判断可否回收或降解。","Tip: classify waste as biodegradable or non-biodegradable and give a way to manage it."],["Renewable Energy and Green Technology","可再生能源与绿色科技",[["Renewable energy sources can be replaced naturally: solar, wind, hydroelectric, biomass and geothermal energy.","可再生能源：太阳能、风能、水力、生物质、地热"],["Fossil fuels (coal, petroleum, natural gas) are non-renewable and release carbon dioxide when burnt.","化石燃料不可再生，燃烧释放CO₂"],["Green technology: technology that reduces damage to the environment, e.g. electric vehicles, solar panels, energy-saving appliances, biodegradable plastics.","绿色科技：减少环境破坏（电动车、太阳能板、节能电器）"],["Advantage of solar energy: clean and no pollutant gas. Limitation: depends on sunlight and the installation cost is high.","太阳能：清洁；局限：依赖阳光，成本高"]],"华文：评价题：说一个优点与一个局限。","Tip: always give one advantage and one limitation for evaluation questions."],["Roles of Individuals and Community","个人与社区的角色",[["Individual: save water and electricity, use public transport, do not litter, practise 3R, plant trees.","个人：节水节电、公共交通、不乱丢垃圾、3R、植树"],["Community: organise recycling campaigns, gotong-royong, river cleaning programmes and awareness talks.","社区：回收活动、集体劳动、清洁河流、宣导"],["Government and industry: make and enforce laws, give incentives for green technology, treat waste before release.","政府与企业：制定执法、奖励绿色科技、排放前处理废物"],["Consumers: choose products with eco-labels and less packaging.","消费者：选环保标签、少包装产品"]],"华文：要写出「具体行动 + 好处」。","Tip: action + reason, e.g. 'use public transport to reduce carbon dioxide released'."],["Global Environmental Issues and the United Nations","全球环境问题与联合国",[["Global issues: global warming, climate change, ozone depletion, deforestation, loss of biodiversity, marine pollution.","全球问题：暖化、气候变化、臭氧层、森林砍伐、生物多样性丧失、海洋污染"],["The United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) coordinates action among countries.","联合国环境规划署协调各国行动"],["Montreal Protocol (1987): reduce the use of CFC to protect the ozone layer. Kyoto Protocol (1997): reduce greenhouse gas emissions. Paris Agreement (2015): limit global warming.","蒙特利尔议定书：减少CFC；京都议定书：减排温室气体；巴黎协定：限制暖化"],["Pollution has no borders (e.g. haze), so countries must cooperate.","污染不分国界（如烟霾），国家须合作"]],"华文：知道协议名称及目的即可。","Tip: match each agreement with its purpose."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Environment","示例题：试卷2 A部分（环境）",[["(a) [1] Name one gas that causes global warming. Scheme: carbon dioxide / methane (1m).","(a)暖化气体：二氧化碳/甲烷"],["(b) [2] State two stages in the life cycle of a plastic bottle that release carbon dioxide. Scheme: manufacturing (1m); transport (1m).","(b)塑料瓶释放CO₂的两个阶段：制造；运输"],["(c) [3] Explain why fish die in a river polluted with fertiliser. Scheme: nutrients cause algal bloom (1m); bacteria decomposing dead algae use up oxygen (1m); fish lack oxygen (1m).","(c)肥料污染河中鱼为何死：藻华；细菌耗氧；鱼缺氧"],["(d) [1] Which gas from air conditioners and old refrigerators damages the ozone layer? Scheme: CFC / chlorofluorocarbon (1m).","(d)破坏臭氧层：CFC"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Sustainability (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（可持续）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how acid rain is formed and one of its effects. Scheme: sulphur dioxide / nitrogen oxides released from burning fossil fuels (1m); dissolve in rainwater (1m); acid rain (pH below 5.6) (1m); damages buildings / kills aquatic life (1m).","(a)酸雨的形成与影响"],["(b) [4] Suggest two ways a school can reduce its carbon footprint and give a reason for each. Scheme: use solar panels / switch off lights (1m) less fossil fuel burnt (1m); recycle paper (1m) less energy to make new paper (1m).","(b)学校减少碳足迹的两种方法与原因"],["(c) [KBAT, 2] A factory wants to build near a mangrove area. Justify whether it should be allowed. Scheme: should not (1m); mangrove protects the coast and is a habitat of many organisms / pollution will harm biodiversity (1m).","(c)工厂建在红树林附近：不应批准；红树林保护海岸与栖息地"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying global warming is caused by sulphur dioxide. Correct: global warming is caused by greenhouse gases (carbon dioxide, methane); sulphur dioxide causes acid rain.","错误：二氧化硫造成暖化。正确：暖化由温室气体造成"],["Mistake: writing 'fish die because of fertiliser' only. Correct: explain the chain: algal bloom, bacteria use up oxygen, fish lack oxygen.","错误：只写肥料使鱼死。正确：写完整因果链"],["Mistake: mixing up conservation and preservation. Correct: conservation = wise use; preservation = protect untouched.","错误：混淆保育与保存"],["Mistake: giving an action without a reason (e.g. 'use public transport'). Correct: add 'to reduce the burning of fuel / carbon dioxide released'.","错误：只写做法不写原因。正确：加上原因"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is a carbon footprint? J: The total greenhouse gases (carbon dioxide) released during the life cycle of a product or activity.","问：碳足迹？答：产品或活动生命周期排放的温室气体总量"],["S: What causes eutrophication? J: Excess nutrients (fertilisers, detergents) in water causing algal bloom and loss of oxygen.","问：富营养化的原因？答：水中营养过多，藻华并缺氧"],["S: Which gases cause acid rain? J: Sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides.","问：酸雨由哪些气体造成？答：二氧化硫和氮氧化物"],["S: What does the ozone layer do? J: It absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation from the Sun.","问：臭氧层的作用？答：吸收有害紫外线"],["S: Give the difference between conservation and preservation. J: Conservation is wise use of resources; preservation is protecting an area untouched.","问：保育与保存的区别？答：保育是明智使用；保存是保持原状"],["S: What does 3R stand for? J: Reduce, Reuse, Recycle.","问：3R代表？答：减少、再用、回收"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-4":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Rate of reaction: the change in the quantity of reactant or product per unit time.","反应速率：单位时间内反应物或生成物量的变化"],["Reactant: substance that is used up in a reaction. Product: substance that is formed.","反应物：被消耗；生成物：被生成"],["Fast reaction: reaction that is completed in a short time (e.g. burning, explosion). Slow reaction: reaction that takes a long time (e.g. rusting, fermentation).","快反应：短时间完成；慢反应：需要很长时间"],["Catalyst: a substance that changes the rate of a reaction but is chemically unchanged at the end of the reaction.","催化剂：改变反应速率但反应结束时化学性质不变的物质"],["Activation energy: the minimum energy that colliding particles must have to react.","活化能：粒子碰撞发生反应所需的最低能量"],["Effective collision: a collision between particles that have enough energy (activation energy) and the correct orientation, which results in a reaction.","有效碰撞：能量足够并且方向正确、导致反应的碰撞"]],"","Tip: define rate with 'quantity ... per unit time' and always mention 'time'."],["Rate of Reaction: Formula","反应速率：公式",[["Average rate of reaction = \\(\\dfrac{\\text{quantity of reactant used or product formed}}{\\text{time taken}}\\).","平均速率＝反应物消耗量或生成物生成量÷所需时间"],["Units: \\(\\text{cm}^3\\ \\text{s}^{-1}\\) (volume of gas), \\(\\text{g s}^{-1}\\) (mass), \\(\\text{mol s}^{-1}\\) (moles).","单位：气体体积 cm³/s；质量 g/s；摩尔 mol/s"],["A faster reaction takes a shorter time to finish, so the rate is inversely proportional to the time taken.","反应越快，所需时间越短（速率与时间成反比）"],["Quantities that can be measured: volume of gas collected, decrease in mass of reactant, time for a colour or mark to disappear.","可测量：收集气体体积、质量减少、颜色或记号消失的时间"]],"","Tip: write formula, substitution and answer WITH unit, each step gets a mark."],["Worked Example: Average Rate (Gas Volume)","例题：平均速率（气体体积）",[["Question: 60 \\(\\text{cm}^3\\) of carbon dioxide gas is collected in 120 s. Calculate the average rate of reaction. [3]","题：120秒收集60 cm³ 二氧化碳，求平均速率"],["Formula: average rate = \\(\\dfrac{\\text{volume of gas}}{\\text{time}}\\) (1m).","公式（1分）"],["Substitution: \\(\\dfrac{60\\ \\text{cm}^3}{120\\ \\text{s}}\\) (1m).","代入（1分）"],["Answer: \\(0.5\\ \\text{cm}^3\\ \\text{s}^{-1}\\) (1m, with unit).","答案：0.5 cm³/s（含单位1分）"],["Check: if the question asks for the rate in the first 30 s only, use the volume at 30 s divided by 30 s, not the total volume.","若问前30秒速率，要用30秒时的体积÷30"]],"","Tip: no unit, no mark; write cm³ s⁻¹ or cm³/s."],["Worked Example: Average Rate (Mass) and Time Intervals","例题：平均速率（质量）与时间段",[["Question: 2.4 g of magnesium ribbon is used up completely in 60 s when reacting with hydrochloric acid. Calculate the average rate. [3]","题：2.4 g镁带60秒完全反应，求平均速率"],["Formula: rate = \\(\\dfrac{\\text{mass of magnesium used}}{\\text{time}}\\) (1m).","公式（1分）"],["Substitution: \\(\\dfrac{2.4\\ \\text{g}}{60\\ \\text{s}}\\) (1m). Answer: \\(0.04\\ \\text{g s}^{-1}\\) (1m).","代入并得答案0.04 g/s"],["Table: volume at 0 s = 0, 20 s = 30, 40 s = 50 \\(\\text{cm}^3\\). Rate in 0–20 s = \\(30\\div 20=1.5\\ \\text{cm}^3\\ \\text{s}^{-1}\\); rate in 20–40 s = \\((50-30)\\div 20=1.0\\ \\text{cm}^3\\ \\text{s}^{-1}\\).","表格例：0–20秒1.5，20–40秒1.0 cm³/s"],["The rate decreases with time because the reactants are being used up (concentration decreases).","速率随时间下降：反应物被消耗，浓度下降"]],"","Tip: for a time interval use (change in volume) ÷ (change in time)."],["Fast and Slow Reactions","快反应与慢反应",[["Fast reactions: burning of fuel, explosion of fireworks, neutralisation of acid and alkali, reaction of sodium with water.","快反应：燃烧、爆炸、中和、钠与水"],["Slow reactions: rusting of iron, fermentation, ripening of fruit, weathering of rocks, decay of food.","慢反应：生锈、发酵、水果成熟、岩石风化、食物腐烂"],["Reactions that are useful should be speeded up (e.g. making ammonia, cooking). Reactions that are harmful should be slowed down (e.g. food spoilage, rusting).","有益的反应要加快；有害的反应要减慢"],["Fast reactions show a short time taken; slow reactions show a long time taken.","快反应用时短；慢反应用时长"]],"","Tip: give two examples for each type, using scientific names."],["Measuring the Rate of Reaction","测量反应速率的方法",[["Method 1: measure the volume of gas released at regular time intervals using a gas syringe or by downward displacement of water.","方法1：用注射器或排水法定时测气体体积"],["Method 2: measure the decrease in mass of the reaction mixture on an electronic balance when gas escapes.","方法2：用电子秤测气体逸出造成的质量减少"],["Method 3: measure the time for a mark (cross) under the flask to disappear when a precipitate forms.","方法3：测沉淀形成使底部记号消失的时间"],["Use a stopwatch to measure time; repeat to get a reliable (more accurate) average.","用秒表计时；重复实验取平均"],["Start the stopwatch the moment the reactants are mixed.","反应物混合的同时开始计时"]],"","Tip: name the apparatus: gas syringe / burette, stopwatch, electronic balance."],["Reading the Graph of Volume against Time","读图：体积—时间曲线",[["The gradient (slope) of the graph at any point shows the rate of reaction at that time.","曲线斜率代表该时刻的速率"],["A steeper curve = a higher (faster) rate. The curve is steepest at the start because the concentration of reactant is highest.","越陡速率越快；开始时最陡（浓度最高）"],["The curve becomes less steep (gradient decreases) as the reactant is used up.","曲线渐平：反应物被消耗"],["When the curve becomes horizontal (gradient = 0), the reaction has stopped and one reactant has been used up completely.","曲线水平：反应停止，某反应物已用完"],["If only the rate is changed (and the amount of reactant is the same), the final volume of gas is the same, but the time to reach it is different.","反应物量不变：最终体积相同，仅所需时间不同"]],"","Tip: compare curves with 'steeper' / 'less steep' and say the final volume is the same."],["Factors Affecting the Rate of Reaction","影响反应速率的因素",[["Size of reactant: the smaller the size of the particles (the larger the total surface area exposed), the higher the rate.","反应物大小：颗粒越小（总表面积越大），速率越高"],["Concentration of reactant: the higher the concentration, the higher the rate.","浓度：越高，速率越高"],["Temperature of reactants: the higher the temperature, the higher the rate.","温度：越高，速率越高"],["Catalyst: the presence of a positive catalyst increases the rate.","催化剂：有催化剂速率增大"],["For gases, a higher pressure also increases the rate.","气体：压强越高速率越高"]],"","Tip: write the relationship in full: 'the higher the ..., the higher the rate of reaction'."],["Size of Reactant and Concentration (F + H)","反应物大小与浓度（F + H）",[["F1 Smaller size of reactant (powder) reacts faster than a big lump. H: the total surface area exposed to collision is larger.","F1 粉末比块状快。H：总表面积更大"],["F2 More particles of reactant on the surface can collide with the other reactant. H: the frequency of collisions increases, so the frequency of effective collisions increases.","F2 表面更多粒子可碰撞。H：碰撞和有效碰撞频率增加"],["F3 Higher concentration of acid gives a higher rate. H: there are more particles per unit volume.","F3 浓度高速率高。H：单位体积粒子数更多"],["F4 The particles are closer together. H: the frequency of effective collisions increases, so the rate increases.","F4 粒子更靠近。H：有效碰撞频率增加，速率提高"]],"","Tip: link the factor to 'frequency of effective collisions' to get the H mark."],["Temperature and Catalyst (F + H)","温度与催化剂（F + H）",[["F1 Higher temperature gives a higher rate. H: the particles gain more kinetic energy and move faster.","F1 温度高速率高。H：粒子动能增加，运动更快"],["F2 More particles have energy equal to or higher than the activation energy. H: the frequency of collisions and of effective collisions increases.","F2 更多粒子达到活化能。H：碰撞与有效碰撞频率增加"],["F3 A catalyst increases the rate of reaction. H: it provides an alternative pathway with a lower activation energy.","F3 催化剂提高速率。H：提供活化能较低的另一途径"],["F4 A catalyst is not used up and its mass is the same at the end; only a small amount is needed; it is specific to certain reactions.","F4 催化剂不被消耗，质量不变；少量即可；具有专一性"],["Examples: iron in the Haber process (ammonia), manganese(IV) oxide for decomposition of hydrogen peroxide, enzymes in the body.","例：哈伯法的铁；二氧化锰分解过氧化氢；体内酶"]],"","Tip: for catalyst, write 'lower activation energy', not 'increases energy'."],["Collision Theory (F + H)","碰撞理论（F + H）",[["F1 Reaction occurs when reactant particles collide. H: only effective collisions result in a reaction.","F1 粒子碰撞才反应。H：只有有效碰撞才产生反应"],["F2 The colliding particles must have energy equal to or higher than the activation energy. H: otherwise they just bounce off each other.","F2 须达到活化能。H：否则只会弹开"],["F3 The collision must have the correct orientation. H: so that bonds can break and new substances form.","F3 碰撞方向要正确。H：以便断键并形成新物质"],["F4 A higher frequency of effective collisions means a higher rate of reaction.","F4 有效碰撞频率越高，速率越高"],["Not every collision is effective.","并非每次碰撞都有效"]],"","Tip: write 'frequency of effective collisions', not just 'more collisions'."],["Experiment: Effect of Size of Marble Chips on the Rate","实验：大理石大小对反应速率的影响",[["Aim: to study the effect of the size of marble chips on the rate of reaction. Problem statement: does the size of marble chips affect the rate of reaction? (1m)","目的与问题陈述"],["Hypothesis: the smaller the size of marble chips, the higher the rate of reaction (1m). Variables: manipulated = size of marble chips; responding = rate of reaction (volume of gas per time); fixed = mass of marble, volume and concentration of acid, temperature (3m).","假设与变量"],["Apparatus and materials: conical flask, delivery tube, burette or gas syringe, basin, stopwatch, electronic balance, marble chips (large and small), 0.1 mol \\(\\text{dm}^{-3}\\) hydrochloric acid (1m).","仪器与材料"],["Procedure: (1) Put 50 \\(\\text{cm}^3\\) of acid in the flask. (2) Add 5 g of large marble chips and quickly close the stopper. (3) Start the stopwatch and record the volume of gas every 30 s until constant. (4) Repeat with 5 g of small chips (powder). (5) Plot a graph of volume against time. (2m)","步骤"],["Observation: the small chips give a steeper graph and gas bubbles are released faster. Equation: \\(\\ce{CaCO3 + 2HCl -> CaCl2 + H2O + CO2}\\). Conclusion: the hypothesis is accepted (1m).","观察：小颗粒曲线更陡，气泡更快；结论：假设成立"]],"","Tip: the mass of the marble must be the same, only the size changes."],["Experiment: Effect of Concentration on the Rate","实验：浓度对反应速率的影响",[["Aim: to study the effect of concentration of acid on the rate of reaction. Problem statement: does the concentration of acid affect the rate of reaction? (1m)","目的与问题陈述"],["Hypothesis: the higher the concentration of acid, the higher the rate of reaction (1m).","假设：酸浓度越高，速率越高"],["Variables: manipulated = concentration of acid; responding = time taken to collect a fixed volume of gas (or volume per time); fixed = mass and size of magnesium ribbon (or marble), volume of acid, temperature (3m).","变量"],["Apparatus and materials: conical flask, gas syringe, stopwatch, magnesium ribbon (same length), 0.1, 0.5 and 1.0 mol \\(\\text{dm}^{-3}\\) hydrochloric acid (1m). Procedure: react the same magnesium with each acid, start the stopwatch on mixing and record the time to collect 40 \\(\\text{cm}^3\\) of gas (2m).","仪器材料与步骤"],["Observation: the higher the concentration, the shorter the time taken and the more vigorous the bubbling. Conclusion: hypothesis accepted (1m).","观察：浓度越高用时越短；结论：假设成立"]],"","Tip: write the concentration values with unit mol dm⁻³."],["Experiment: Effect of Temperature (Sodium Thiosulphate and Acid)","实验：温度的影响（硫代硫酸钠与酸）",[["Aim: to study the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction. Hypothesis: the higher the temperature of the sodium thiosulphate solution, the higher the rate of reaction (shorter time taken) (2m).","目的与假设"],["Variables: manipulated = temperature of sodium thiosulphate solution; responding = time taken for the cross to disappear; fixed = volume and concentration of both solutions (3m).","变量"],["Apparatus: conical flask, measuring cylinder, thermometer, Bunsen burner or hot water bath, stopwatch, white paper marked with a cross (1m).","仪器：锥形瓶、量筒、温度计、热源、秒表、画叉白纸"],["Procedure: heat 50 \\(\\text{cm}^3\\) of sodium thiosulphate to 30 °C, place the flask on the cross, add 5 \\(\\text{cm}^3\\) of acid, start the stopwatch and record the time for the cross to disappear when viewed from above; repeat at 40, 50 and 60 °C (2m).","步骤：在30至60℃重复，记录叉消失时间"],["Observation: a yellow precipitate of sulphur forms and the cross disappears sooner at a higher temperature. \\(\\ce{Na2S2O3 + 2HCl -> 2NaCl + H2O + SO2 + S}\\). Conclusion: hypothesis accepted (1m).","观察：黄色硫沉淀，温度高叉消失更快；结论：假设成立"]],"","Tip: rate is proportional to 1/time; the shorter the time, the higher the rate."],["Applications in Daily Life and Industry (F + H)","日常与工业应用（F + H）",[["F1 Food is cut into small pieces before cooking. H: larger total surface area, so food cooks faster.","F1 食物切小块。H：总表面积大，煮得更快"],["F2 A pressure cooker cooks food faster. H: the boiling point of water is higher, so the temperature is higher and the rate is higher.","F2 压力锅更快。H：沸点更高，温度更高"],["F3 Food is kept in the refrigerator. H: low temperature slows down the growth of bacteria and the rate of spoilage.","F3 食物放冰箱。H：低温减慢细菌生长与腐败"],["F4 Catalysts are used in industry (e.g. iron in the Haber process). H: to increase the rate of production and reduce cost.","F4 工业用催化剂。H：加快生产、降低成本"],["F5 Powdered medicine dissolves faster than tablets. H: it has a larger surface area.","F5 药粉比药片溶解快。H：表面积更大"]],"","Tip: one fact (what is done) + one explanation (which factor and why)."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Rate of Reaction","示例题：试卷2 A部分（反应速率）",[["(a) [1] State the type of reaction shown by the rusting of iron. Scheme: slow reaction (1m).","(a)生锈属于慢反应"],["(b) [3] 80 \\(\\text{cm}^3\\) of gas is collected in 100 s. Calculate the average rate. Scheme: formula \\(\\dfrac{\\text{volume}}{\\text{time}}\\) (1m); \\(\\dfrac{80}{100}\\) (1m); \\(0.8\\ \\text{cm}^3\\ \\text{s}^{-1}\\) (1m).","(b)80 cm³用100秒，平均速率0.8 cm³/s"],["(c) [2] Marble powder reacts faster than marble chips. Explain. Scheme: total surface area is larger (1m); frequency of effective collisions is higher (1m).","(c)大理石粉更快：表面积更大，有效碰撞更频繁"],["(d) [2] Name the manipulated variable and the responding variable. Scheme: manipulated = size of marble (1m); responding = rate of reaction / volume of gas per time (1m).","(d)操纵变量=大理石大小；响应变量=反应速率"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Rate of Reaction (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（反应速率）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain, using collision theory, why increasing the temperature increases the rate of reaction. Scheme: particles have more kinetic energy (1m); move faster (1m); more particles have energy equal to or higher than the activation energy (1m); frequency of effective collisions increases (1m).","(a)用碰撞理论解释升温加快速率"],["(b) [4] Plan an investigation on the effect of the concentration of hydrochloric acid on the rate of reaction with magnesium ribbon. Scheme: hypothesis (1m); variables (1m); apparatus and materials with stopwatch / gas syringe (1m); procedure and tabulated results (1m).","(b)设计探究：酸浓度对速率的影响"],["(c) [KBAT] [2] A factory wants to produce a medicine more quickly at low cost. Suggest two ways. Scheme: use a suitable catalyst (1m) with the reason that it lowers the activation energy; use a powdered reactant or a higher temperature (1m) with the reason of a higher frequency of effective collisions.","(c)建议：用催化剂；用粉末或升温"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: writing 'more collisions' only. Correct: 'higher frequency of effective collisions'.","错误：只写更多碰撞。正确：有效碰撞频率更高"],["Mistake: saying a catalyst is used up or increases the energy of particles. Correct: it is not used up and lowers the activation energy.","错误：催化剂被消耗/增加能量。正确：不被消耗，降低活化能"],["Mistake: no unit in the rate answer. Correct: write \\(\\text{cm}^3\\ \\text{s}^{-1}\\), \\(\\text{g s}^{-1}\\).","错误：速率答案漏单位"],["Mistake: saying a higher temperature gives more product. Correct: it only gives the same product faster; the total amount is the same.","错误：升温产物更多。正确：只是更快，总量不变"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Define rate of reaction. J: The change in the quantity of reactant or product per unit time.","问：反应速率的定义？答：单位时间内反应物或生成物量的变化"],["S: 60 cm³ of gas is collected in 30 s. What is the average rate? J: 2 cm³ s⁻¹.","问：30秒收集60 cm³气体，平均速率？答：2 cm³/s"],["S: Why does powder react faster than a lump? J: Larger total surface area, so a higher frequency of effective collisions.","问：为何粉末更快？答：表面积更大，有效碰撞频率更高"],["S: How does a catalyst work? J: It provides an alternative pathway with a lower activation energy.","问：催化剂如何作用？答：提供活化能较低的途径"],["S: What does a steeper graph show? J: A higher rate of reaction.","问：曲线更陡表示什么？答：速率更高"],["S: Why does the rate decrease as the reaction proceeds? J: The concentration of the reactants decreases.","问：为何速率逐渐下降？答：反应物浓度下降"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-5":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Carbon compound: a compound that contains carbon. Organic compounds come from living things (e.g. carbohydrates, proteins, fats); inorganic carbon compounds include carbon dioxide, carbonates and carbon monoxide.","碳化合物：含碳的化合物；有机来自生物；无机如二氧化碳、碳酸盐"],["Hydrocarbon: a compound that contains carbon and hydrogen only.","烃：只含碳和氢的化合物"],["Alkane: a saturated hydrocarbon with single bonds only; general formula \\(\\text{C}_n\\text{H}_{2n+2}\\).","烷：只有单键的饱和烃，通式CnH2n+2"],["Alcohol: an organic compound that contains the hydroxyl group (-OH), e.g. ethanol \\(\\ce{C2H5OH}\\).","醇：含羟基（-OH）的有机化合物"],["Fermentation: the breakdown of sugar by yeast (enzymes) without oxygen to produce ethanol and carbon dioxide.","发酵：酵母在无氧下将糖分解成乙醇和二氧化碳"],["Saponification: the reaction between an oil or fat and an alkali (e.g. sodium hydroxide) to produce soap and glycerol.","皂化：油脂与碱反应生成肥皂和甘油"]],"","Tip: hydrocarbon = carbon and hydrogen ONLY; do not add oxygen."],["Carbon Compounds: Organic and Inorganic","碳化合物：有机与无机",[["Organic carbon compounds are made by living things: carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, and also fossil fuels formed from ancient organisms.","有机碳化合物：糖类、蛋白质、脂肪、维生素及化石燃料"],["Most organic compounds contain carbon with hydrogen, and sometimes oxygen and nitrogen; many burn to give carbon dioxide and water.","多数含碳氢，有的含氧、氮；燃烧生成二氧化碳和水"],["Inorganic carbon compounds: carbon dioxide, carbon monoxide, carbonates (e.g. calcium carbonate in limestone and marble).","无机碳化合物：二氧化碳、一氧化碳、碳酸盐"],["Carbon is also found as elements: diamond, graphite and charcoal.","碳单质：钻石、石墨、木炭"],["Carbon compounds are used as food, fuel, medicine, clothing materials and building materials.","用途：食物、燃料、药物、衣料、建材"]],"","Tip: give examples of both types; carbon dioxide is inorganic."],["The Carbon Cycle","碳循环",[["Carbon dioxide is removed from the atmosphere by photosynthesis in green plants and algae, which make carbohydrates.","光合作用从大气中吸收二氧化碳"],["Carbon dioxide is released by respiration of living things, combustion of fuels and wood, decay of dead organisms by decomposers, and volcanic eruptions.","呼吸、燃烧、分解者分解尸体、火山释放二氧化碳"],["Carbon passes along food chains as animals eat plants and other animals.","碳沿食物链传递"],["Dead plants and animals buried for millions of years form fossil fuels (coal, petroleum, natural gas); burning them returns carbon dioxide to the air.","遗体埋藏数百万年形成化石燃料；燃烧返还二氧化碳"],["Carbon dioxide also dissolves in oceans and is used to make shells of marine organisms.","二氧化碳溶于海洋，用于形成海洋生物外壳"]],"","Tip: state the process that REMOVES CO2 (photosynthesis) and those that RELEASE it."],["Carbon Cycle and Human Activities (F + H)","碳循环与人类活动（F + H）",[["F1 The carbon cycle keeps the percentage of carbon dioxide in the air balanced. H: the amount removed by photosynthesis equals the amount released by respiration, decay and combustion.","F1 碳循环维持二氧化碳平衡。H：光合作用吸收量＝释放量"],["F2 Burning fossil fuels and open burning increase carbon dioxide. H: more carbon dioxide is released than is removed.","F2 燃烧化石燃料使二氧化碳增加。H：释放多于吸收"],["F3 Deforestation reduces the carbon dioxide removed. H: fewer trees carry out photosynthesis.","F3 砍伐森林。H：进行光合作用的树减少"],["F4 The extra carbon dioxide traps heat in the atmosphere. H: this strengthens the greenhouse effect and causes global warming and climate change.","F4 多余CO2吸热。H：温室效应增强、全球暖化"],["Ways to reduce: plant trees, use renewable energy, save energy, reduce open burning and recycle.","对策：植树、可再生能源、节能、减少露天焚烧、回收"]],"","Tip: 'carbon dioxide' + 'greenhouse effect' + 'global warming' are the keywords."],["Hydrocarbons and Their Sources","烃及其来源",[["Sources of hydrocarbons: crude oil (petroleum) and natural gas, which are fossil fuels.","烃的来源：原油和天然气（化石燃料）"],["Crude oil is a mixture of many hydrocarbons; it is separated into fractions by fractional distillation based on different boiling points.","原油是混合物，按沸点不同分馏"],["Fractions include petroleum gas (cooking gas), petrol, kerosene, diesel and bitumen; small molecules have low boiling points and are collected at the top.","分馏产物：石油气、汽油、煤油、柴油、沥青；小分子沸点低，在顶部收集"],["Hydrocarbons are used as fuels and as raw materials for plastics, detergents and medicine.","烃用作燃料及塑料、洗涤剂、药物原料"],["Fossil fuels are non-renewable: they take millions of years to form.","化石燃料不可再生：需要数百万年形成"]],"","Tip: fractional distillation separates by difference in boiling point."],["Alkanes: Names and Formulae","烷：名称与分子式",[["Methane \\(\\ce{CH4}\\) (1 C); ethane \\(\\ce{C2H6}\\) (2 C); propane \\(\\ce{C3H8}\\) (3 C).","甲烷CH4；乙烷C2H6；丙烷C3H8"],["Butane \\(\\ce{C4H10}\\) (4 C); pentane \\(\\ce{C5H12}\\) (5 C); hexane \\(\\ce{C6H14}\\) (6 C).","丁烷C4H10；戊烷C5H12；己烷C6H14"],["General formula of alkanes: \\(\\text{C}_n\\text{H}_{2n+2}\\). All C-C bonds are single bonds, so alkanes are saturated.","通式CnH2n+2；全是单键，为饱和烃"],["Worked example: an alkane has 8 carbon atoms. Number of H = \\(2(8)+2=18\\) (1m); formula \\(\\ce{C8H18}\\) (1m).","例：8个碳→H=2×8+2=18，分子式C8H18"],["Names end with -ane; prefixes meth-, eth-, prop-, but-, pent-, hex- show 1 to 6 carbon atoms.","词根meth-、eth-、prop-、but-、pent-、hex-表示1至6个碳"]],"","Tip: check the formula with 2n+2; e.g. butane C4H10 (2×4+2 = 10)."],["Alkenes, Saturated and Unsaturated Hydrocarbons","烯、饱和与不饱和烃",[["Alkenes contain a C=C double bond; general formula \\(\\text{C}_n\\text{H}_{2n}\\); e.g. ethene \\(\\ce{C2H4}\\), propene \\(\\ce{C3H6}\\).","烯含C=C双键；通式CnH2n；如乙烯、丙烯"],["Saturated hydrocarbons (alkanes) have single bonds only; unsaturated hydrocarbons (alkenes) have at least one double bond.","饱和烃只有单键；不饱和烃含双键"],["Test: shake with bromine water. Alkane: brown colour stays (no change). Alkene: brown colour decolourised (turns colourless).","检验：溴水。烷不褪色；烯使溴水褪色"],["Alkenes burn with a sootier (more smoky) flame than alkanes because of a higher percentage of carbon.","烯燃烧烟更多（含碳百分比更高）"],["Alkenes are used to make plastics (e.g. poly(ethene)).","烯用于制造塑料（聚乙烯）"]],"","Tip: unsaturated hydrocarbon decolourises bromine water; write 'brown to colourless'."],["Combustion of Hydrocarbons (F + H)","烃的燃烧（F + H）",[["F1 Complete combustion in sufficient oxygen produces carbon dioxide and water. H: a blue flame with little soot and a lot of heat. Word equation: hydrocarbon + oxygen → carbon dioxide + water.","F1 氧气充足完全燃烧生成CO2和水。H：蓝色火焰、少烟、热量多"],["F2 Methane: \\(\\ce{CH4 + 2O2 -> CO2 + 2H2O}\\).","F2 甲烷燃烧方程式"],["F3 Incomplete combustion in insufficient oxygen produces carbon monoxide and / or carbon (soot) and water. H: a yellow, sooty flame with less heat.","F3 氧气不足生成CO或炭黑和水。H：黄色多烟火焰、热量少"],["F4 Carbon monoxide is a toxic gas. H: it combines with haemoglobin in the blood and reduces the oxygen carried to the body.","F4 CO有毒。H：与血红蛋白结合，减少携氧"],["Test for the products: carbon dioxide turns limewater cloudy; water turns anhydrous copper(II) sulphate from white to blue or cobalt chloride paper from blue to pink.","检验：CO2使石灰水浑浊；水使无水硫酸铜白变蓝"]],"","Tip: for incomplete combustion write carbon monoxide AND soot."],["Fossil Fuels and Alternative Energy","化石燃料与替代能源",[["Problems of fossil fuels: non-renewable, will run out; burning produces carbon dioxide (global warming), sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides (acid rain) and carbon monoxide.","化石燃料问题：不可再生；燃烧产生CO2、SO2、氮氧化物、CO"],["Renewable energy sources: solar, wind, hydroelectric, geothermal, biomass and biofuel (e.g. biodiesel from palm oil, bioethanol).","可再生能源：太阳能、风能、水力、地热、生物质、生物燃料"],["Renewable energy reduces dependence on fossil fuels and produces less pollution.","可再生能源减少依赖化石燃料、污染少"],["Save fossil fuels by using public transport, using energy-saving appliances and avoiding wastage.","节约：搭乘公共交通、节能电器、避免浪费"]],"","Tip: link the pollutant to its effect: CO2 → global warming; SO2 → acid rain."],["Alcohols and Ethanol","醇与乙醇",[["Alcohols form a homologous series with the functional group -OH: methanol \\(\\ce{CH3OH}\\), ethanol \\(\\ce{C2H5OH}\\), propanol \\(\\ce{C3H7OH}\\) (general formula \\(\\text{C}_n\\text{H}_{2n+1}\\text{OH}\\)).","醇：官能团-OH；甲醇、乙醇、丙醇"],["Physical properties of ethanol: colourless liquid, characteristic smell, volatile, dissolves in water, low boiling point (about 78 °C).","乙醇：无色液体、特殊气味、易挥发、溶于水"],["Chemical property: ethanol is flammable and burns with a blue flame to give carbon dioxide and water.","化学性质：易燃，蓝色火焰燃烧生成CO2和水"],["Uses of ethanol: fuel (biofuel), solvent in perfumes, paints and medicine, antiseptic and disinfectant, alcoholic drinks.","用途：燃料、溶剂、消毒剂、酒精饮料"],["Methanol is highly toxic and must never be drunk.","甲醇剧毒，不可饮用"]],"","Tip: write the formula C₂H₅OH and name the -OH group."],["Experiment: Preparing Ethanol by Fermentation","实验：发酵制乙醇",[["Aim: to prepare ethanol by fermentation of glucose. Hypothesis: yeast ferments glucose solution to produce ethanol and carbon dioxide (1m).","目的与假设"],["Variables: manipulated = presence of yeast; responding = formation of ethanol (smell) and carbon dioxide (limewater turns cloudy); fixed = volume and concentration of glucose, temperature (3m).","变量"],["Apparatus and materials: conical flask, delivery tube, boiling tube, glucose solution, yeast, limewater, water bath (1m).","仪器材料"],["Procedure: (1) Mix glucose solution with yeast in the flask and close with a stopper fitted with a delivery tube into limewater. (2) Keep in a warm place (about 30–35 °C) for several days. (3) Observe the limewater and smell the mixture. (4) Filter and distil the mixture to obtain ethanol (2m).","步骤：混合、保温数天、观察石灰水、过滤蒸馏"],["Observation: bubbles form, limewater turns cloudy, the mixture smells of alcohol. \\(\\ce{C6H12O6 -> 2C2H5OH + 2CO2}\\) (yeast). Conclusion: yeast changes glucose to ethanol and carbon dioxide (1m).","观察：气泡、石灰水浑浊、有酒味；结论：酵母把葡萄糖变成乙醇和CO2"]],"","Tip: yeast gives enzymes (zymase); too hot kills the yeast, so keep it warm, not boiling."],["Effects of Alcohol Misuse (F + H)","酗酒的影响（F + H）",[["F1 Alcohol slows down the nervous system. H: slow reaction time and poor judgement, so the risk of road accidents increases.","F1 酒精减慢神经系统。H：反应迟钝，交通事故风险增加"],["F2 Long-term heavy drinking damages the liver. H: the liver breaks down the alcohol, causing cirrhosis and liver failure.","F2 长期酗酒伤肝。H：肝脏分解酒精，致肝硬化、肝衰竭"],["F3 Alcohol is addictive. H: the drinker becomes dependent and has social, family and financial problems.","F3 酒精使人上瘾。H：产生依赖，引起社会、家庭和经济问题"],["F4 It also damages the brain and stomach and can cause heart disease.","F4 也损害脑、胃并引发心脏病"],["Drinking and driving is an offence; avoid alcohol and choose healthy activities.","酒后驾驶违法；避免饮酒"]],"","Tip: effect + reason, e.g. 'liver damage because the liver breaks down alcohol'."],["Fats: Sources and Types","脂肪：来源与种类",[["Fats and oils are organic compounds made of fatty acids and glycerol; they are an energy-rich food and give insulation.","油脂由脂肪酸和甘油构成；能量高、保温"],["Saturated fats: from animals (butter, ghee, lard, fatty meat) and some plants (coconut oil, palm oil); usually solid at room temperature.","饱和脂肪：动物脂肪、椰油、棕榈油；常温多为固体"],["Unsaturated fats: from plants and fish (olive oil, corn oil, sunflower oil, fish oil); usually liquid at room temperature.","不饱和脂肪：植物油、鱼油；常温多为液体"],["Unsaturated fats contain C=C double bonds in their fatty acid chains; saturated fats have single bonds only.","不饱和脂肪含C=C双键；饱和脂肪只有单键"],["Unsaturated oil can be hardened by adding hydrogen (hydrogenation) to make margarine.","不饱和油加氢硬化制成人造奶油"]],"","Tip: saturated = single bonds, solid; unsaturated = double bonds, liquid."],["Fats and Health (F + H)","脂肪与健康（F + H）",[["F1 A diet high in saturated fat raises the level of blood cholesterol. H: cholesterol deposits on artery walls and narrows them.","F1 高饱和脂肪升高胆固醇。H：沉积在动脉壁使其变窄"],["F2 This increases the risk of heart disease, high blood pressure and stroke. H: blood flow is blocked.","F2 增加心脏病、高血压、中风风险。H：血流受阻"],["F3 Excess fat intake leads to obesity. H: unused energy is stored as fat in the body.","F3 过量摄入导致肥胖。H：多余能量以脂肪储存"],["F4 Unsaturated fats are healthier. H: they help lower the level of bad cholesterol.","F4 不饱和脂肪更健康。H：有助降低坏胆固醇"],["Healthy practice: choose unsaturated oils, steam or bake instead of deep-fry, limit fatty food and exercise regularly.","健康做法：选不饱和油、蒸烤代替油炸、运动"]],"","Tip: cholesterol → blocks arteries → heart disease (chain of F + H)."],["Palm Oil: Extraction and Uses","棕榈油：提取与用途",[["Oil palm fruit: palm oil comes from the mesocarp (flesh); palm kernel oil comes from the kernel (seed).","油棕果：棕榈油取自中果皮；棕榈仁油取自果仁"],["Extraction steps: sterilise the fruit bunches with steam (to stop enzyme action and soften fruit), thresh (separate fruits from bunches), digest (mash the fruit), press (squeeze out the oil), clarify (remove water and impurities).","提取：蒸煮灭菌、脱粒、搅拌、压榨、澄清"],["Uses of palm oil: cooking oil, margarine, chocolate and snacks, soap, cosmetics, candles and biodiesel.","用途：食用油、人造奶油、巧克力、肥皂、化妆品、蜡烛、生物柴油"],["Palm oil is an important export of Malaysia, which provides income and jobs.","棕榈油是马来西亚重要出口，提供收入与就业"],["By-products from the mill (empty fruit bunches, fibre, shell) can be used as fuel or fertiliser.","副产品（空果串、纤维、壳）可作燃料或肥料"]],"","Tip: list the extraction steps in the correct order."],["Experiment: Preparing Soap by Saponification (F + H)","实验：皂化反应制肥皂（F + H）",[["F1 Heat palm oil with concentrated sodium hydroxide solution in a beaker for 10–15 minutes, stirring. H: heat is needed for the alkali to break down (hydrolyse) the oil.","F1 棕榈油加浓NaOH加热搅拌10–15分钟。H：需加热使碱水解油"],["F2 Add sodium chloride (salt) and stir; soap floats on top as a solid. H: this is salting out, because soap is less soluble in salt solution.","F2 加食盐，肥皂浮在上层（盐析）"],["F3 Filter, wash the soap with distilled water to remove excess alkali, then press and dry.","F3 过滤、蒸馏水洗去多余碱，压成型晾干"],["F4 Word equation: oil + sodium hydroxide → soap + glycerol.","F4 油＋NaOH→肥皂＋甘油"],["Precaution: sodium hydroxide is corrosive; wear goggles and gloves. Using potassium hydroxide gives soft soap.","注意：NaOH腐蚀性，戴护目镜手套；KOH制软皂"]],"","Tip: products = soap AND glycerol (1m each); name the alkali."],["How Soap Cleans (F + H)","肥皂的去污原理（F + H）",[["F1 A soap particle has a hydrophilic head and a hydrophobic tail. H: the head dissolves in water, the tail dissolves in oil or grease.","F1 肥皂亲水头、疏水尾。H：头溶于水，尾溶于油脂"],["F2 Soap lowers the surface tension of water. H: water wets the cloth more easily.","F2 肥皂降低水的表面张力。H：水更易润湿衣物"],["F3 The tails surround the grease and pull it off the cloth when scrubbed. H: the grease breaks into small droplets (emulsification).","F3 疏水尾包围油脂，搓洗时拉离衣物。H：油脂成小油滴（乳化）"],["F4 The heads face the water and the droplets are suspended in the water, so they are washed away.","F4 亲水头朝水，油滴悬浮并被冲走"]],"","Tip: use the words hydrophilic, hydrophobic, emulsification."],["Sustainable Palm Oil Industry (F + H)","可持续棕榈油业（F + H）",[["F1 Clearing forest for plantations causes deforestation. H: habitats of animals such as orang utan are lost, reducing biodiversity and releasing carbon dioxide.","F1 开荒种植导致砍伐。H：动物栖息地丧失，生物多样性下降，释放CO2"],["F2 Mill effluent (POME) discharged into rivers causes water pollution. H: it lowers the dissolved oxygen so aquatic organisms die.","F2 工厂废水排入河流污染水。H：溶解氧减少，水生生物死亡"],["F3 Open burning causes haze. H: it harms health and increases carbon dioxide.","F3 露天焚烧造成雾霾。H：损害健康并增加CO2"],["Solutions: replant old trees instead of clearing forest, treat mill effluent before release, trap methane for biogas, avoid burning, and get certification (MSPO, RSPO).","对策：重新种植、处理废水、沼气、不焚烧、认证MSPO/RSPO"],["Sustainable = meets present needs without harming the needs of future generations.","可持续＝满足当前需求而不损害后代需求"]],"","Tip: give the problem, the effect and a solution for each."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Carbon Compounds","示例题：试卷2 A部分（碳化合物）",[["(a) [1] What is a hydrocarbon? Scheme: a compound containing carbon and hydrogen only (1m).","(a)烃：只含碳和氢"],["(b) [2] Write the molecular formula of pentane and state the general formula of alkanes. Scheme: \\(\\ce{C5H12}\\) (1m); \\(\\text{C}_n\\text{H}_{2n+2}\\) (1m).","(b)戊烷C5H12；通式CnH2n+2"],["(c) [2] Name the gas that turns limewater cloudy in the fermentation of glucose and the process that removes it from the air. Scheme: carbon dioxide (1m); photosynthesis (1m).","(c)二氧化碳；光合作用"],["(d) [2] Name the two products of saponification. Scheme: soap (1m); glycerol (1m).","(d)肥皂与甘油"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Carbon Compounds (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（碳化合物）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain how the carbon cycle is affected by deforestation and burning fossil fuels. Scheme: fewer trees for photosynthesis (1m) so less carbon dioxide removed (1m); burning releases carbon dioxide (1m) so greenhouse effect and global warming (1m).","(a)砍伐与燃烧化石燃料对碳循环的影响"],["(b) [4] Describe how soap is prepared from palm oil. Scheme: heat palm oil with concentrated sodium hydroxide (1m); add salt to precipitate the soap (1m); filter and wash with distilled water (1m); press and dry (1m).","(b)描述棕榈油制皂"],["(c) [KBAT] [2] A company wants to expand its palm oil plantation by clearing a forest. Justify why it should replant old estates instead. Scheme: prevents loss of habitat and biodiversity (1m); fewer trees cut so less carbon dioxide released and sustainable (1m).","(c)论证：重新种植而非砍伐森林"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying hydrocarbons contain carbon, hydrogen and oxygen. Correct: carbon and hydrogen only.","错误：烃含碳氢氧。正确：只含碳和氢"],["Mistake: writing that incomplete combustion gives only carbon dioxide. Correct: carbon monoxide and / or soot, and water.","错误：不完全燃烧只生成CO2。正确：CO或炭黑和水"],["Mistake: forgetting the products of fermentation. Correct: ethanol and carbon dioxide (yeast, no oxygen).","错误：漏发酵产物。正确：乙醇和二氧化碳"],["Mistake: saying all vegetable oils are unsaturated. Correct: palm and coconut oil are rich in saturated fat.","错误：植物油都是不饱和。正确：棕榈油椰油饱和脂肪多"],["Mistake: writing only 'protect environment' for sustainable palm oil. Correct: give a specific action such as replanting or treating effluent.","错误：只写保护环境。正确：写具体做法"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Which process removes carbon dioxide from the atmosphere? J: Photosynthesis.","问：哪个过程移除大气中的CO2？答：光合作用"],["S: Write the formula of propane. J: C3H8.","问：丙烷分子式？答：C3H8"],["S: What colour change shows an alkene with bromine water? J: Brown to colourless.","问：烯使溴水怎样变色？答：由棕色变无色"],["S: What are the products of fermentation of glucose by yeast? J: Ethanol and carbon dioxide.","问：酵母发酵葡萄糖产物？答：乙醇和二氧化碳"],["S: Why is a high-saturated-fat diet harmful? J: It raises cholesterol, which blocks arteries and causes heart disease.","问：高饱和脂肪为何有害？答：升高胆固醇，阻塞动脉致心脏病"],["S: Name the steps of palm oil extraction. J: Sterilise, thresh, digest, press, clarify.","问：棕榈油提取步骤？答：蒸煮灭菌、脱粒、搅拌、压榨、澄清"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-6":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Electrolysis: the process of breaking down an electrolyte into its elements by passing an electric current through it.","电解：通电把电解质分解成元素"],["Electrolyte: a substance that conducts electricity in the molten or aqueous state and is chemically decomposed. Non-electrolyte: a substance that does not conduct electricity in any state.","电解质：熔融或水溶液能导电并被分解；非电解质：任何状态都不导电"],["Electrode: a conductor (carbon or metal) through which current enters or leaves the electrolyte. Anode: positive electrode. Cathode: negative electrode (in an electrolytic cell).","电极；阳极：正极；阴极：负极（电解池）"],["Oxidation: loss of electrons. Reduction: gain of electrons. (OIL RIG)","氧化：失去电子；还原：得到电子"],["Electrolytic cell: a cell that uses electrical energy to bring about a chemical change. Chemical cell: a cell that changes chemical energy to electrical energy.","电解池：电能变化学能；化学电池：化学能变电能"],["Electrochemical series: an arrangement of metals in order of their tendency to form positive ions (to lose electrons).","电化学序：金属按形成阳离子（失去电子）倾向排列"]],"华文：OIL RIG：氧化失电子，还原得电子。","Tip: define electrolysis as 'breaking down an electrolyte by electric current' - include the word electrolyte."],["Electrolytes and Non-electrolytes","电解质与非电解质",[["Ionic compounds in the molten state or aqueous solution conduct electricity because they contain freely moving ions.","离子化合物熔融或溶于水含自由移动离子，故导电"],["Solid ionic compounds do not conduct electricity because the ions are held in fixed positions and cannot move.","固态离子化合物离子固定，不导电"],["Covalent compounds (e.g. sugar, ethanol, naphthalene) do not conduct electricity because they exist as neutral molecules without ions.","共价化合物（糖、乙醇）只含中性分子，不导电"],["Metals and graphite conduct electricity in the solid state because of freely moving electrons.","金属和石墨靠自由电子导电"],["In an electrolyte, ions carry the current; in a metal wire, electrons carry the current.","电解质中离子载流；金属导线中电子载流"]],"华文：关键词：freely moving ions。","Tip: explain conductivity with 'freely moving ions' (electrolyte) or 'freely moving electrons' (metal)."],["Electrolytic Cell: Structure and Reactions","电解池：结构与反应",[["Parts: power supply (battery), two electrodes, electrolyte, container, connecting wires.","组成：电源、两电极、电解质、容器、导线"],["Anode is connected to the positive terminal of the battery; cathode is connected to the negative terminal.","阳极接电池正极；阴极接电池负极"],["Anode: anions (negative ions) move to it, lose electrons: oxidation.","阳极：阴离子趋向，失去电子：氧化"],["Cathode: cations (positive ions) move to it, gain electrons: reduction.","阴极：阳离子趋向，得到电子：还原"],["Electrons flow in the wire from the anode to the battery, then to the cathode.","电子在导线中由阳极经电池流向阴极"],["Energy change: electrical energy to chemical energy.","能量转换：电能变化学能"]],"华文：阳极(+)氧化；阴极(−)还原。","Tip: state the electrode, the ion that moves to it, and whether oxidation or reduction occurs."],["Electrolysis of Molten Lead(II) Bromide","熔融溴化铅(II)的电解",[["Ions present: \\(\\ce{Pb^2+}\\) and \\(\\ce{Br-}\\). The compound must be melted so the ions can move (carbon electrodes).","离子：Pb²⁺和Br⁻；须熔化使离子能移动（碳电极）"],["Cathode: \\(\\ce{Pb^2+ + 2e- -> Pb}\\) (reduction). Observation: grey / silvery molten lead deposited.","阴极：Pb²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Pb；银灰色熔融铅"],["Anode: \\(\\ce{2Br- -> Br2 + 2e-}\\) (oxidation). Observation: brown gas (bromine) released.","阳极：2Br⁻ → Br₂ + 2e⁻；释放棕色气体溴"],["Overall products: lead and bromine. Carried out in a fume chamber because bromine is toxic.","产物：铅和溴；在通风橱内进行，因溴有毒"]],"华文：金属在阴极，非金属在阳极。","Tip: write the ion, the half-equation and the observation for each electrode."],["Electrolysis of Aqueous Copper(II) Sulphate with Carbon Electrodes","用碳电极电解硫酸铜溶液",[["Ions present: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\), \\(\\ce{SO4^2-}\\) (from the salt) and \\(\\ce{H+}\\), \\(\\ce{OH-}\\) (from water).","离子：Cu²⁺、SO₄²⁻、H⁺、OH⁻"],["Cathode: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\) is discharged: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2e- -> Cu}\\). Observation: brown solid deposited.","阴极：Cu²⁺放电；棕色固体析出"],["Anode: \\(\\ce{OH-}\\) is discharged: \\(\\ce{4OH- -> 2H2O + O2 + 4e-}\\). Observation: bubbles of colourless gas; glowing splinter relights.","阳极：OH⁻放电；无色气泡；带火星木条复燃"],["Blue colour of the solution fades because the concentration of \\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\) decreases.","溶液蓝色变浅：Cu²⁺浓度下降"]],"华文：氧气检验：带火星的木条复燃。","Tip: test for oxygen - glowing splinter relights."],["Selective Discharge of Ions (F + H)","离子的选择性放电（F + H）",[["F1 Position of the ion in the electrochemical series. H: the ion lower in the series is discharged first (cations: Cu, Ag, H are discharged easily; K, Na, Ca, Mg, Al are not discharged from solution).","F1 离子在序中的位置。H：位置较低者先放电"],["F2 Concentration of the ion. H: a much more concentrated ion is discharged, even if it is higher in the series (e.g. concentrated \\(\\ce{Cl-}\\) is discharged instead of \\(\\ce{OH-}\\)).","F2 离子浓度。H：浓度高的离子优先放电"],["F3 Type of electrode. H: an active electrode (e.g. copper) itself dissolves, while an inert electrode (carbon, platinum) does not take part in the reaction.","F3 电极种类。H：活泼电极（铜）自身溶解；惰性电极（碳、铂）不参与"],["F4 Anions: \\(\\ce{OH-}\\) is normally discharged instead of \\(\\ce{SO4^2-}\\) and \\(\\ce{NO3-}\\). H: these ions are lower in the series than the others, so oxygen is released.","F4 阴离子：OH⁻优先于SO₄²⁻、NO₃⁻放电，释放氧气"]],"华文：三个因素：位置、浓度、电极。","Tip: list the three factors: position in the electrochemical series, concentration, type of electrode."],["Factor: Concentration of the Electrolyte","因素：电解质浓度",[["Dilute sodium chloride solution (carbon electrodes): cathode - hydrogen gas (\\(\\ce{H+}\\) is discharged); anode - oxygen gas (\\(\\ce{OH-}\\) is discharged).","稀氯化钠溶液：阴极H₂；阳极O₂"],["Concentrated sodium chloride solution: cathode - hydrogen gas; anode - chlorine gas (\\(\\ce{Cl-}\\) is discharged because its concentration is high).","浓氯化钠溶液：阴极H₂；阳极Cl₂（Cl⁻浓度高）"],["Chlorine: pungent greenish-yellow gas that bleaches moist blue litmus paper. Hydrogen: burns with a ‘pop’ sound.","氯气：刺激性黄绿色，漂白湿蓝石蕊；氢气：爆鸣声"],["Na+ is never discharged from aqueous solution because it is higher than \\(\\ce{H+}\\) in the electrochemical series.","Na⁺在水溶液中不放电，因在序中高于H⁺"]],"华文：浓度决定阳极产物：O₂ 或 Cl₂。","Tip: say ‘concentrated’ or ‘dilute’ before naming the product at the anode."],["Factor: Type of Electrode (F + H)","因素：电极种类（F + H）",[["F1 Copper(II) sulphate solution with copper electrodes: anode dissolves. H: \\(\\ce{Cu -> Cu^2+ + 2e-}\\); the copper atoms lose electrons to form ions.","F1 铜电极：阳极溶解。H：Cu → Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻"],["F2 The cathode becomes thicker. H: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2e- -> Cu}\\); copper is deposited.","F2 阴极变厚。H：Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu"],["F3 The blue colour of the solution remains unchanged. H: the rate at which \\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\) is formed at the anode equals the rate at which it is discharged at the cathode.","F3 蓝色不变。H：阳极生成Cu²⁺的速率等于阴极放电速率"],["F4 With carbon electrodes the blue colour fades and oxygen is released at the anode. H: \\(\\ce{OH-}\\) is discharged and \\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\) is not replaced.","F4 碳电极：蓝色变浅，阳极放出O₂。H：OH⁻放电，Cu²⁺得不到补充"]],"华文：同一溶液，换电极，结果不同。","Tip: compare the two experiments - anode thinner (copper) vs oxygen gas (carbon)."],["Electrolysis of Water: Volume Calculation","水的电解：体积计算",[["Electrolyte: dilute sulphuric acid or dilute sodium hydroxide with carbon electrodes (to increase conductivity of water).","电解质：稀硫酸或稀氢氧化钠（增强水的导电性）"],["Cathode: hydrogen gas. Anode: oxygen gas. Equation: \\(\\ce{2H2O -> 2H2 + O2}\\).","阴极氢气；阳极氧气"],["Volume ratio hydrogen : oxygen = 2 : 1 (at the same temperature and pressure).","体积比 氢：氧 = 2：1"],["Worked example: 24 cm\\(^3\\) of hydrogen is collected at the cathode. Volume of oxygen at the anode \\(= 24 \\div 2 = 12\\) cm\\(^3\\). (1m ratio, 1m answer with unit)","示例：24 cm³氢气 → 氧气 24 ÷ 2 = 12 cm³"]],"华文：氢多氧少，2比1。","Tip: the test tube at the cathode collects twice the volume of gas as at the anode."],["Investigation: Electrolysis of Copper(II) Sulphate Solution","探究：硫酸铜溶液的电解",[["Aim: to study the effect of the type of electrode on the products of electrolysis of copper(II) sulphate solution. Problem statement: does the type of electrode affect the products? (2m)","目的与问题：电极种类是否影响产物"],["Hypothesis: with carbon electrodes oxygen is released at the anode; with copper electrodes the anode becomes thinner. (1m)","假设：碳电极阳极放O₂；铜电极阳极变薄"],["Variables: manipulated = type of electrode (carbon / copper); responding = product at the anode; fixed = concentration and volume of copper(II) sulphate solution, voltage. (3m)","变量：操纵=电极种类；响应=阳极产物；固定=溶液浓度和体积、电压"],["Apparatus and materials: beaker, carbon and copper electrodes, battery, connecting wires, switch, 0.5 mol dm\\(^{-3}\\) copper(II) sulphate solution, test tube, wooden splinter. (1m)","仪器材料：烧杯、碳/铜电极、电池、导线、开关、硫酸铜溶液"],["Procedure: 1 Fill the beaker with copper(II) sulphate solution. 2 Dip two carbon electrodes and connect to the battery; switch on for 10 minutes. 3 Test the gas at the anode with a glowing splinter. 4 Repeat with two copper electrodes, weigh the electrodes before and after. (2m)","步骤：碳电极通电10分钟，检验气体；改用铜电极，称电极质量"],["Observation and conclusion: carbon - brown solid at cathode, gas relights splinter, blue fades; copper - anode thinner, cathode thicker, blue unchanged. The type of electrode affects the products; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察与结论：电极种类影响产物；假设被接受"]],"华文：用铜电极称重前后质量变化。","Tip: state the observation at both electrodes and in the solution."],["Electroplating","电镀",[["Electroplating: coating a metal object with a thin layer of another metal using electrolysis.","电镀：用电解在金属物体上镀一层薄金属"],["Cathode: the object to be plated. Anode: the plating metal. Electrolyte: a solution containing ions of the plating metal.","阴极：被镀物；阳极：镀层金属；电解质：含镀层金属离子的溶液"],["Example: plating an iron spoon with silver. Electrolyte: silver nitrate solution. Anode: \\(\\ce{Ag -> Ag+ + e-}\\). Cathode: \\(\\ce{Ag+ + e- -> Ag}\\).","例：铁匙镀银：硝酸银溶液；阳极Ag溶解；阴极Ag析出"],["Purposes: to prevent corrosion (rusting), to make the object more attractive, to make it harder or more durable.","目的：防腐蚀（生锈）、美观、更耐用"],["Concentration of the electrolyte stays constant because \\(\\ce{Ag+}\\) removed at the cathode is replaced from the anode.","电解质浓度不变：阴极消耗的离子由阳极补充"]],"华文：电镀三要点：阴极、阳极、电解质。","Tip: ‘object to be plated is the cathode; plating metal is the anode’."],["Investigation: Electroplating an Iron Key with Copper","探究：铁钥匙镀铜",[["Aim: to electroplate an iron key with copper. Hypothesis: copper is deposited on the iron key when it is made the cathode in copper(II) sulphate solution. (2m)","目的与假设：铁钥匙作阴极，铜析出"],["Variables: manipulated = time of electrolysis (or type of electrode); responding = mass of copper deposited on the key; fixed = current, concentration of electrolyte. (3m)","变量：操纵=电解时间；响应=沉积铜质量；固定=电流、电解质浓度"],["Apparatus and materials: iron key, copper plate, copper(II) sulphate solution, beaker, battery, wires, ammeter, sandpaper. (1m)","仪器材料：铁钥匙、铜板、硫酸铜溶液、电池、电流表、砂纸"],["Procedure: 1 Clean the key with sandpaper. 2 Connect the key to the negative terminal and the copper plate to the positive terminal. 3 Immerse both in copper(II) sulphate solution and switch on for 20 minutes. 4 Remove, rinse and dry the key. (2m)","步骤：砂纸清洁；钥匙接负极、铜板接正极；通电20分钟；洗净晾干"],["Observation: brown layer of copper on the key; the copper plate becomes thinner; blue colour unchanged. (1m) Conclusion: the key is electroplated with copper. (1m)","观察：钥匙镀上棕色铜；铜板变薄；蓝色不变；结论：钥匙镀铜成功"]],"华文：先用砂纸清洁，才能镀得均匀牢固。","Tip: explain why the key is cleaned first - to remove oxide and grease so that the layer sticks well."],["Purification of Copper and Extraction of Aluminium","铜的精炼与铝的提取",[["Purification of copper: anode = impure copper; cathode = pure copper; electrolyte = copper(II) sulphate solution.","精炼铜：阳极=粗铜；阴极=纯铜；电解质=硫酸铜溶液"],["Anode: \\(\\ce{Cu -> Cu^2+ + 2e-}\\) (impure anode becomes thinner). Cathode: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2e- -> Cu}\\) (pure cathode becomes thicker). Impurities fall to the bottom as sludge.","阳极变薄；阴极变厚；杂质沉为泥渣"],["Extraction of aluminium: aluminium oxide is dissolved in molten cryolite to lower its melting point and save energy; carbon electrodes are used.","提取铝：氧化铝溶于熔融冰晶石以降低熔点节能；用碳电极"],["Cathode: \\(\\ce{Al^3+ + 3e- -> Al}\\) (molten aluminium collects at the bottom). Anode: \\(\\ce{2O^2- -> O2 + 4e-}\\); the oxygen reacts with the hot carbon anode to form carbon dioxide, so the anodes must be replaced.","阴极得铝；阳极放氧，与碳反应生成CO₂，阳极须更换"],["Aluminium is extracted by electrolysis because it is too reactive to be reduced by carbon.","铝太活泼，无法用碳还原，故用电解法"]],"华文：冰晶石的作用：降低熔点。","Tip: cryolite lowers the melting point of aluminium oxide."],["Chemical Cells: Daniell Cell","化学电池：丹尼尔电池",[["A chemical cell changes chemical energy to electrical energy. It consists of two different metals (electrodes) dipped in electrolytes and connected by wires.","化学电池：化学能变电能；两种不同金属浸入电解质并连线"],["Daniell cell: zinc in zinc sulphate solution and copper in copper(II) sulphate solution, separated by a porous pot or a salt bridge.","丹尼尔电池：锌/硫酸锌与铜/硫酸铜，以多孔盆或盐桥隔开"],["Negative terminal (zinc): \\(\\ce{Zn -> Zn^2+ + 2e-}\\) (oxidation); zinc plate becomes thinner.","负极（锌）：Zn → Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻；锌板变薄"],["Positive terminal (copper): \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2e- -> Cu}\\) (reduction); copper plate becomes thicker; blue colour fades.","正极（铜）：Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu；铜板变厚；蓝色变浅"],["Electrons flow through the external wire from zinc (negative) to copper (positive). The salt bridge / porous pot allows ions to move to complete the circuit.","电子经外电路由锌流向铜；盐桥/多孔盆让离子移动形成回路"]],"华文：电子：负极 → 正极。","Tip: the more electropositive metal is the negative terminal."],["Voltage of a Chemical Cell (Electrochemical Series)","化学电池的电压（电化学序）",[["Electrochemical series (decreasing reactivity): K, Na, Ca, Mg, Al, Zn, Fe, Sn, Pb, (H), Cu, Ag.","电化学序（活泼性递减）：K Na Ca Mg Al Zn Fe Sn Pb (H) Cu Ag"],["The metal higher in the series is the negative terminal (it loses electrons more easily); the metal lower in the series is the positive terminal.","序中较高金属为负极；较低为正极"],["The further apart the two metals in the series, the higher the voltage of the cell.","两金属在序中相隔越远，电压越高"],["Worked example (data supplied in the question; values here are illustrative): voltages with copper as the positive terminal: Mg 2.7 V, Zn 1.1 V, Fe 0.8 V. Largest voltage = Mg and Cu (2.7 V) because Mg is furthest from Cu. (2m)","示例（题目给数据，数值仅示意）：与铜配对：Mg 2.7 V、Zn 1.1 V、Fe 0.8 V；镁最远，电压最大"],["Voltage of a Mg and Zn cell \\(= 2.7 - 1.1 = 1.6\\) V; Mg is the negative terminal. (2m)","Mg与Zn电池电压 = 2.7 − 1.1 = 1.6 V；Mg为负极"]],"华文：电压 = 两个电压相减（以同一金属为参照）。","Tip: write the voltage with unit V and name the negative terminal."],["Investigation: Voltage of Cells with Different Metals","探究：不同金属电池的电压",[["Aim: to study the effect of different pairs of metals on the voltage of a simple chemical cell. Hypothesis: the further apart the metals in the electrochemical series, the higher the voltage. (2m)","目的与假设：金属在序中相隔越远，电压越高"],["Variables: manipulated = pair of metals; responding = voltage; fixed = electrolyte (type, concentration, volume), distance between electrodes. (3m)","变量：操纵=金属组合；响应=电压；固定=电解质种类浓度体积、电极距离"],["Apparatus and materials: beaker, voltmeter, connecting wires, strips of Mg, Zn, Fe, Cu (cleaned with sandpaper), sodium chloride or dilute sulphuric acid. (1m)","仪器材料：烧杯、伏特计、金属片、电解质"],["Procedure: 1 Clean the metal strips. 2 Dip copper and magnesium in the electrolyte and connect to the voltmeter. 3 Read the voltage and note the negative terminal. 4 Repeat with Zn-Cu and Fe-Cu. (2m)","步骤：清洁金属；Cu-Mg接伏特计；读电压；重复Zn-Cu、Fe-Cu"],["Observation: Mg-Cu gives the highest voltage, then Zn-Cu, then Fe-Cu. Conclusion: the further apart the metals, the higher the voltage; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察：Mg-Cu最高；结论：假设被接受"]],"华文：金属片要用砂纸擦净氧化层。","Tip: say the metal strips are cleaned to remove the oxide layer."],["Electrolytic Cell vs Chemical Cell","电解池与化学电池比较",[["Energy change: electrolytic - electrical to chemical; chemical - chemical to electrical.","能量转换：电解池电→化学；化学电池化学→电"],["Source of electricity: electrolytic - external battery needed; chemical - none needed (the cell itself produces electricity).","电源：电解池需外接电池；化学电池自身产电"],["Electrodes: electrolytic - the same or different conductors; chemical - two different metals.","电极：电解池可相同；化学电池须两种不同金属"],["Positive terminal: electrolytic - anode (oxidation); chemical - positive terminal is where reduction occurs (cathode).","正极：电解池阳极（氧化）；化学电池正极发生还原"],["Both cells involve oxidation at one electrode and reduction at the other, and electrons flow in the external circuit.","两者都是一极氧化、一极还原"]],"华文：易错：电解池阳极是正极，化学电池氧化发生在负极。","Tip: compare using ‘whereas’ for each point."],["Types of Chemical Cells","化学电池的种类",[["Primary cells cannot be recharged: dry cell (zinc-carbon) and alkaline cell, used in torches and remote controls.","一次电池不可充电：干电池、碱性电池"],["Secondary cells can be recharged: lead-acid accumulator (cars) and lithium-ion battery (phones, laptops, electric vehicles).","二次电池可充电：铅酸蓄电池（汽车）、锂离子电池（手机、电动车）"],["Used batteries contain heavy metals (e.g. lead, mercury, cadmium) and must be disposed of properly in collection bins.","废电池含重金属，须放入回收箱"],["Choose rechargeable cells to reduce waste and save cost in the long run.","选用可充电电池可减少废物、长期省钱"]],"华文：评价题：可充电电池的优缺点。","Tip: for evaluation, give the advantage (reusable) and the disposal concern."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Electrochemistry","示例题：试卷2 A部分（电化学）",[["(a) [1] State the electrode connected to the positive terminal of the battery in electrolysis. Scheme: anode (1m).","(a)接电池正极的电极：阳极"],["(b) [2] Molten lead(II) bromide is electrolysed using carbon electrodes. Name the products at the cathode and anode. Scheme: lead (1m); bromine (1m).","(b)熔融溴化铅：阴极铅；阳极溴"],["(c) [2] Write the half-equation at the cathode. Scheme: \\(\\ce{Pb^2+ + 2e- -> Pb}\\) (1m for formula, 1m for balanced).","(c)阴极半反应"],["(d) [2] Solid lead(II) bromide does not conduct electricity. Explain. Scheme: ions are held in fixed positions (1m); cannot move freely (1m).","(d)固态不导电：离子固定、不能自由移动"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Electrolysis and Cells (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（电解与电池）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Describe the electroplating of an iron spoon with silver. Scheme: spoon is the cathode (1m); silver plate is the anode (1m); silver nitrate solution as electrolyte (1m); silver deposited on the spoon (1m).","(a)铁匙镀银：阴极匙；阳极银；硝酸银；银析出"],["(b) [4] A Daniell cell uses zinc and copper. State the negative terminal and two observations after some time. Scheme: zinc (1m); zinc plate becomes thinner (1m); copper plate becomes thicker (1m); blue colour fades (1m).","(b)负极锌；锌板变薄；铜板变厚；蓝色变浅"],["(c) [KBAT, 2] A student wants a cell with a higher voltage than the Zn-Cu cell. Suggest the metal to replace zinc and justify. Scheme: magnesium (1m); further from copper in the electrochemical series (1m).","(c)更高电压：用镁替代锌；离铜更远"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying ions move in the wire. Correct: electrons move in the wire; ions move in the electrolyte.","错误：离子在导线中移动。正确：导线中是电子；电解质中是离子"],["Mistake: forgetting that ions must be free to move (molten or aqueous). Correct: solid ionic compounds do not conduct electricity.","错误：忽略离子须能自由移动"],["Mistake: always writing oxygen at the anode or chloride ions never discharged. Correct: depends on concentration and electrode (concentrated chloride gives chlorine; copper anode dissolves).","错误：阳极一律写氧气。正确：取决于浓度与电极"],["Mistake: mixing up the terminals. Correct: electrolytic cell - anode is positive; chemical cell - the more reactive metal is the negative terminal.","错误：混淆电极。正确：电解池阳极为正；化学电池活泼金属为负极"],["Mistake: electroplating with the object as the anode. Correct: the object to be plated is the cathode.","错误：被镀物作阳极。正确：被镀物作阴极"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: At which electrode does oxidation occur in an electrolytic cell? J: The anode.","问：电解池中氧化发生在哪个电极？答：阳极"],["S: What are the products of electrolysis of molten lead(II) bromide? J: Lead at the cathode and bromine at the anode.","问：熔融溴化铅产物？答：阴极铅，阳极溴"],["S: In electroplating, which electrode is the object to be plated? J: The cathode.","问：电镀中被镀物是哪一极？答：阴极"],["S: Why is cryolite added in the extraction of aluminium? J: To lower the melting point of aluminium oxide.","问：提取铝为何加冰晶石？答：降低氧化铝的熔点"],["S: Which is the negative terminal of a Daniell cell? J: Zinc.","问：丹尼尔电池负极？答：锌"],["S: 24 cm3 of hydrogen is collected in the electrolysis of water. What is the volume of oxygen? J: 12 cm3.","问：电解水得24 cm³氢气，氧气体积？答：12 cm³"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-7":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Lens: a piece of transparent material (glass or plastic) with curved surfaces that refracts light to form an image.","透镜：有弧形表面、使光折射成像的透明材料"],["Optical centre (O): the centre of the lens; a ray through O is not deviated. Principal axis: the line through O and perpendicular to the lens.","光心：透镜中心，经过的光线不偏折；主轴：通过光心且垂直于透镜的直线"],["Focal point (F): the point where parallel rays converge (convex lens) or appear to diverge from (concave lens) after passing through the lens.","焦点：平行光经透镜后会聚（凸）或看似发散（凹）的点"],["Focal length (f): the distance between the optical centre and the focal point.","焦距：光心到焦点的距离"],["Real image: formed by actual meeting of rays; can be shown on a screen. Virtual image: formed by rays that only appear to meet; cannot be shown on a screen.","实像：光线实际会聚，可在屏上呈现；虚像：光线看似会聚，不能在屏上呈现"],["Power of a lens (P): the ability of a lens to converge or diverge light; \\(P = \\dfrac{1}{f}\\), unit dioptre (D).","透镜焦度：会聚或发散光线的能力；单位屈光度 D"]],"华文：先背定义，再背成像特征。","Tip: write definitions with the keywords: refract, converge, diverge, optical centre, focal point."],["Convex Lens and Concave Lens","凸透镜与凹透镜",[["Convex lens (converging lens): thicker at the centre than at the edges; brings parallel rays together at a real focal point.","凸透镜（会聚透镜）：中间厚，使平行光会聚于实焦点"],["Concave lens (diverging lens): thinner at the centre than at the edges; spreads parallel rays apart as if from a virtual focal point.","凹透镜（发散透镜）：中间薄，使平行光发散，看似来自虚焦点"],["A thick, strongly curved lens has a short focal length and a high power.","越厚越弯的透镜焦距越短，焦度越高"],["Each lens has two focal points, one on each side, at the same distance from O.","每个透镜两侧各有一个焦点，与光心距离相等"],["Mark on a diagram: O, F, 2F (on both sides), principal axis, and arrows on the rays.","作图须标出 O、F、2F、主轴和光线箭头"]],"华文：画图时凸透镜用双向外箭头，凹透镜用双向内箭头。","Tip: always label O, F and 2F and draw arrows on every ray, otherwise marks are lost."],["Ray Rules for a Convex Lens","凸透镜的特征光线",[["Ray 1: a ray parallel to the principal axis is refracted through the focal point F on the other side.","光线1：平行于主轴的光线折射后经过另一侧焦点 F"],["Ray 2: a ray passing through the optical centre O goes straight without bending.","光线2：经过光心的光线沿直线传播，不偏折"],["Ray 3: a ray passing through the focal point F on the object side is refracted parallel to the principal axis.","光线3：经过物侧焦点的光线折射后平行于主轴"],["The image is located where two refracted rays meet (real image) or where they appear to meet when traced backwards (virtual image).","像在折射光线交点（实像）或反向延长线交点（虚像）"],["Use a ruler and draw at least two of the three rays.","用直尺，至少画出三条中的两条"]],"华文：虚像的反向延长线要用虚线。","Tip: use solid lines for real rays and dashed lines for rays traced backwards to a virtual image."],["Ray Rules for a Concave Lens","凹透镜的特征光线",[["Ray 1: a ray parallel to the principal axis is refracted away from the axis, as if coming from the focal point F on the object side.","光线1：平行于主轴的光线折射后向外发散，反向延长线过物侧焦点"],["Ray 2: a ray passing through the optical centre O is not deviated.","光线2：经过光心的光线不偏折"],["Ray 3: a ray directed towards the focal point F on the other side is refracted parallel to the principal axis.","光线3：射向另一侧焦点的光线折射后平行于主轴"],["The refracted rays diverge, so they never meet; trace them backwards with dashed lines to find the image.","折射光线发散不相交，用虚线反向延长找像"]],"华文：凹透镜只能成虚像。","Tip: the image of a concave lens is on the same side as the object, drawn with dashed lines."],["Image Characteristics: Convex Lens","凸透镜成像特征",[["Object beyond 2F: image between F and 2F; real, inverted, diminished (camera, eye).","物在 2F 外：像在 F 与 2F 之间；倒立缩小实像（相机、眼睛）"],["Object at 2F: image at 2F; real, inverted, same size as the object.","物在 2F：像在 2F；倒立等大实像"],["Object between F and 2F: image beyond 2F; real, inverted, magnified (projector).","物在 F 与 2F 之间：像在 2F 外；倒立放大实像（投影机）"],["Object at F: refracted rays are parallel, so no image is formed (image at infinity).","物在 F：折射光线平行，不成像"],["Object between O and F: image on the same side as the object; virtual, upright, magnified (magnifying glass).","物在 O 与 F 之间：像与物同侧；正立放大虚像（放大镜）"]],"华文：口诀：物远像小，物近像大；F 内变虚像。","Tip: describe an image using four words: position, real/virtual, upright/inverted, size (magnified/diminished/same size)."],["Image Characteristics: Concave Lens","凹透镜成像特征",[["For any object distance, a concave lens forms an image that is virtual, upright and diminished.","无论物距多少：正立缩小虚像"],["The image is on the same side of the lens as the object and nearer to the lens than the object.","像与物同侧，且比物更靠近透镜"],["As the object moves closer to the lens, the image becomes larger but is still smaller than the object.","物体靠近透镜，像变大但仍小于物"],["Uses: spectacles for short-sightedness (myopia), door viewers (peepholes).","用途：近视眼镜、门镜"]],"华文：凹透镜成像特征不随物距改变。","Tip: concave lens answer = virtual, upright, diminished (the only answer)."],["Real and Virtual Images (F + H)","实像与虚像（F + H）",[["F1 A real image is formed by a convex lens when the object is beyond F. H: the refracted rays actually meet at a point, so the image can be projected on a screen.","F1 物在 F 外凸透镜成实像。H：折射光线实际会聚，可在屏上呈现"],["F2 A virtual image is formed when the object is between O and F of a convex lens. H: the refracted rays diverge and only appear to come from a point behind the object, so it cannot be formed on a screen.","F2 物在 F 内成虚像。H：折射光线发散，只是看似来自一点，不能在屏上呈现"],["F3 A concave lens only forms virtual images. H: it diverges the rays so they never meet.","F3 凹透镜只成虚像。H：光线发散，永不相交"],["F4 The image of a camera is inverted. H: rays from the top of the object cross at the lens and reach the bottom of the screen.","F4 相机所成的像倒立。H：来自物体顶部的光线在透镜处交叉，到达屏的下部"]],"华文：F 写结论，H 写光线是否真正相交。","Tip: for real/virtual, the explanation must mention whether the rays actually meet or only appear to meet."],["Power of a Lens","透镜焦度",[["Formula: \\(P = \\dfrac{1}{f}\\), where f is the focal length in metres (m) and P is in dioptre (D).","公式：P = 1/f，f 单位为米，P 单位为屈光度 D"],["Convex lens: f is positive, so P is positive. Concave lens: f is negative, so P is negative.","凸透镜 f、P 为正；凹透镜为负"],["A shorter focal length means a higher power and a stronger bending of light.","焦距越短，焦度越大，光线偏折越强"],["Convert cm to m first: \\(f = 25\\ \\text{cm} = 0.25\\ \\text{m}\\).","先把厘米换算成米"],["Opticians use lens power to prescribe spectacles: convex for long-sightedness, concave for short-sightedness.","验光师用焦度配镜：远视用凸，近视用凹"]],"华文：计算前先换算单位。","Tip: marks are given for the formula, correct substitution in metres, and the answer with the unit D."],["Worked Example: Power of a Lens","例题：透镜焦度",[["Q1: A convex lens has a focal length of 20 cm. Calculate its power. [3]","题1：凸透镜焦距 20 cm，求焦度"],["Step 1: \\(f = 20\\ \\text{cm} = 0.20\\ \\text{m}\\). (1m)","步骤1：f = 0.20 m"],["Step 2: \\(P = \\dfrac{1}{f} = \\dfrac{1}{0.20}\\). (1m)","步骤2：代入公式"],["Step 3: \\(P = +5\\ \\text{D}\\). (1m)","步骤3：P = +5 D"],["Q2: A concave lens has a power of \\(-2.5\\ \\text{D}\\). Find its focal length. Answer: \\(f = \\dfrac{1}{P} = \\dfrac{1}{-2.5} = -0.40\\ \\text{m}\\), that is 40 cm (diverging).","题2：焦度 -2.5 D 的凹透镜；f = -0.40 m，即 40 cm（发散）"]],"","Tip: write the unit D (dioptre) and keep the negative sign for a concave lens."],["Magnification","放大率",[["Linear magnification: \\(m = \\dfrac{\\text{height of image}}{\\text{height of object}} = \\dfrac{h_i}{h_o}\\); m has no unit.","放大率 m = 像高 ÷ 物高；无单位"],["m greater than 1: image is magnified. m = 1: same size. m less than 1: image is diminished.","m 大于 1 放大；等于 1 等大；小于 1 缩小"],["Example: object 2 cm tall, image 6 cm tall. \\(m = \\dfrac{6}{2} = 3\\). (the image is 3 times larger)","例：物高 2 cm，像高 6 cm，m = 3"],["Use the same unit for image height and object height.","像高和物高须用同一单位"]],"华文：放大率没有单位。","Tip: do not write a unit for magnification; write 'magnified' or 'diminished' to describe it."],["Investigation: Finding the Focal Length of a Convex Lens","探究：测定凸透镜焦距",[["Aim: to determine the focal length of a convex lens. (1m) Problem statement: how can the focal length of a convex lens be found? (1m)","目的：测定凸透镜焦距；问题陈述：如何求焦距"],["Hypothesis: the image of a distant object is formed on the screen at a distance equal to the focal length of the lens. (1m)","假设：远处物体的像成在距离等于焦距之处"],["Variables: manipulated = position of the screen; responding = sharpness of the image / distance from lens to screen; fixed = the lens used, the distant object. (3m)","变量：操纵=屏的位置；响应=像是否清晰及透镜到屏距离；固定=所用透镜、远处物体"],["Apparatus: convex lens, lens holder, white screen, metre rule, distant object (e.g. a window or tree). (1m)","仪器：凸透镜、支架、白屏、米尺、远处物体"],["Procedure: 1 Hold the lens facing the distant object. 2 Move the screen until a sharp, inverted image forms. 3 Measure the distance between the lens and the screen using the metre rule. 4 Repeat and find the average. (2m)","步骤：移动屏至得到清晰倒像；量透镜到屏距离；重复取平均"],["Observation: a sharp, small, inverted, real image forms on the screen. Conclusion: the distance from the lens to the screen is the focal length; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察：屏上得到清晰缩小倒立实像；结论：该距离即焦距，假设被接受"]],"华文：远处物体的光线近似平行。","Tip: explain that rays from a distant object are almost parallel, so they converge at F."],["Investigation: Object Distance and Image Characteristics","探究：物距与成像特征",[["Aim: to study the relationship between object distance and the characteristics of the image formed by a convex lens. (1m)","目的：研究物距与凸透镜成像特征的关系"],["Hypothesis: the nearer the object to the lens (beyond F), the larger the image and the further the image from the lens. (1m)","假设：物（在 F 外）越靠近透镜，像越大，像距越远"],["Variables: manipulated = object distance u; responding = image distance v and size of image; fixed = focal length of lens, height of object. (3m)","变量：操纵=物距；响应=像距和像的大小；固定=焦距、物高"],["Apparatus: convex lens, lens holder, candle (or illuminated object), white screen, metre rule. (1m)","仪器：凸透镜、支架、蜡烛、白屏、米尺"],["Procedure: 1 Place the lens at the centre of the metre rule. 2 Place the candle at u beyond 2F; move the screen to get a sharp image. 3 Record v and the image characteristics. 4 Repeat with u at 2F, between 2F and F and inside F. (2m)","步骤：按不同物距移动屏，记录像距与特征"],["Results: u beyond 2F gives a diminished image; u between F and 2F gives a magnified image; u inside F gives no image on the screen. Conclusion: the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","结果：物在 2F 外缩小；F 与 2F 之间放大；F 内屏上无像。结论：假设被接受"]],"华文：F 内的虚像要用眼睛从透镜另一侧观察。","Tip: a virtual image cannot be caught on a screen; say so when the object is inside F."],["Optical Equipment","光学仪器",[["Magnifying glass: a convex lens used with the object inside F; gives a virtual, upright, magnified image.","放大镜：物在 F 内；正立放大虚像"],["Camera: a convex lens forms a real, inverted, diminished image on the film or sensor; the object is beyond 2F.","相机：在底片/感光元件上成倒立缩小实像；物在 2F 外"],["Projector: object between F and 2F of the lens; forms a real, inverted, magnified image on a screen far away.","投影机：物在 F 与 2F 之间；屏上成倒立放大实像"],["Human eye: the lens focuses a real, inverted, diminished image on the retina; the brain interprets it as upright.","眼睛：视网膜上成倒立缩小实像，大脑转为正立"],["Spectacles: convex lens corrects long-sightedness; concave lens corrects short-sightedness.","眼镜：凸透镜矫正远视；凹透镜矫正近视"]],"华文：每种仪器记：用了哪种透镜 + 成什么像。","Tip: name the lens AND give the image characteristics for each instrument."],["Telescope and Microscope (F + H)","望远镜与显微镜（F + H）",[["F1 An astronomical telescope uses two convex lenses: an objective lens of long focal length and an eyepiece of short focal length. H: the objective collects light from a distant object and forms a real image; the eyepiece magnifies it.","F1 天文望远镜：长焦距物镜与短焦距目镜。H：物镜收集远物光线成实像，目镜放大"],["F2 The objective of a telescope has a large diameter. H: to collect more light so that faint, distant objects can be seen clearly.","F2 物镜口径大。H：收集更多光线，看清暗弱远处物体"],["F3 A compound microscope uses two convex lenses; the objective has a very short focal length. H: the object is placed just beyond F of the objective to form a magnified real image, which the eyepiece magnifies again.","F3 复合显微镜：物镜焦距很短。H：物在物镜 F 外附近，成放大实像，目镜再放大"],["F4 The final image in both instruments is inverted. H: the image is not corrected by any extra lens.","F4 两者最终像都是倒立的。H：没有额外透镜校正"],["Project: a simple telescope can be built using two convex lenses of different focal lengths in a tube.","制作：用两块焦距不同的凸透镜装成简易望远镜"]],"华文：望远镜物镜焦距长；显微镜物镜焦距很短。","Tip: state which lens has the longer focal length and what each lens does."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Lenses","示例题：试卷2 A部分（透镜）",[["(a) [1] Name a lens that is thicker at the centre than at the edges. Scheme: convex lens (1m).","(a)凸透镜"],["(b) [2] An object is placed 30 cm from a convex lens of focal length 10 cm. State two characteristics of the image. Scheme: real (1m); inverted and diminished (1m).","(b)物距 30 cm，f = 10 cm：倒立缩小实像"],["(c) [3] A convex lens has a focal length of 25 cm. Calculate its power. Scheme: \\(f = 0.25\\ \\text{m}\\) (1m); \\(P = 1 \\div 0.25\\) (1m); \\(+4\\ \\text{D}\\) (1m).","(c)f = 25 cm：P = +4 D"],["(d) [2] Why is the image on a screen in a camera inverted? Scheme: rays from the top of the object cross after refraction (1m); reach the lower part of the screen (1m).","(d)相机像倒立：光线交叉，顶部光线到屏下部"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Optical Equipment (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（光学仪器）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Compare the telescope and the microscope. Scheme: both use two convex lenses (1m); telescope objective has long f, microscope objective has very short f (1m); telescope views distant objects (1m); microscope views very small near objects (1m).","(a)比较望远镜与显微镜"],["(b) [6] A student wants to investigate how the object distance affects the image formed by a convex lens. Plan the investigation. Scheme: aim (1m); manipulated: object distance (1m); responding: image distance / characteristics (1m); fixed: focal length (1m); procedure with screen and metre rule (1m); tabulate and conclusion (1m).","(b)设计探究：物距对成像的影响"],["(c) [KBAT] A student sees a blurred board at the back of the class. Suggest and justify a suitable lens for his spectacles. Scheme: concave lens (1m); the student is short-sighted / the lens diverges rays so the image falls exactly on the retina (1m).","(c)看不清后排黑板：建议用凹透镜；因近视，凹透镜使光线发散，像落在视网膜上"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: writing only 'real' for an image. Correct: give all points: real, inverted, magnified/diminished.","错误：只写实像。正确：写全位置、实虚、正倒、大小"],["Mistake: drawing rays without arrows or without a ruler. Correct: use a ruler and arrows; dashed lines for virtual images.","错误：光线没箭头、不用直尺。正确：用直尺加箭头，虚像用虚线"],["Mistake: using f in cm in \\(P = 1/f\\). Correct: convert to metres first.","错误：f 用厘米代入。正确：先换成米"],["Mistake: saying a concave lens can form a real image. Correct: concave lens only forms virtual, upright, diminished images.","错误：凹透镜成实像。正确：只成正立缩小虚像"],["Mistake: mixing up the lenses of a telescope. Correct: objective has the longer focal length.","错误：混淆望远镜两透镜。正确：物镜焦距较长"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What are the characteristics of the image in a magnifying glass? J: Virtual, upright and magnified.","问：放大镜成像特征？答：正立放大虚像"],["S: Which ray passes through a lens without bending? J: The ray passing through the optical centre.","问：哪条光线不偏折？答：经过光心的光线"],["S: Calculate the power of a lens of focal length 50 cm. J: +2 D.","问：焦距 50 cm 透镜的焦度？答：+2 D"],["S: Which lens corrects short-sightedness? J: Concave lens.","问：矫正近视用哪种透镜？答：凹透镜"],["S: Where is the object placed for a projector? J: Between F and 2F of the lens.","问：投影机的物在哪里？答：透镜 F 与 2F 之间"],["S: Which lens of a telescope has the longer focal length? J: The objective lens.","问：望远镜哪块透镜焦距较长？答：物镜"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-8":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Pressure: the force acting normally (perpendicularly) on a unit area of a surface; \\(P = \\dfrac{F}{A}\\).","压强：垂直作用在单位面积上的力"],["Pascal (Pa): the SI unit of pressure; \\(1\\ \\text{Pa} = 1\\ \\text{N m}^{-2}\\).","帕斯卡：压强的国际单位；1 Pa = 1 N m⁻²"],["Atmospheric pressure: the pressure exerted by the weight of the air above a surface.","大气压强：上方空气重量产生的压强"],["Pascal's principle: pressure applied to an enclosed fluid is transmitted equally to every part of the fluid and to the walls of the container.","帕斯卡原理：施加于密闭流体的压强等值传递到流体各处和容器壁"],["Hydraulic system: a system that uses an incompressible liquid in an enclosed space to transmit pressure and multiply a force.","液压系统：用密闭的不可压缩液体传递压强以放大力"],["Density: mass per unit volume, \\(\\rho = \\dfrac{m}{V}\\), unit \\(\\text{kg m}^{-3}\\).","密度：单位体积的质量"]],"华文：压强的定义必须有「垂直」和「单位面积」。","Tip: for pressure write 'force per unit area' and give the unit Pa or N m^-2."],["Pressure of a Solid","固体压强",[["Formula: \\(P = \\dfrac{F}{A}\\), where F is force in newtons (N) and A is area in square metres (\\(\\text{m}^2\\)).","公式：P = F ÷ A；F 为牛顿，A 为平方米"],["Pressure is directly proportional to force when area is constant.","面积不变时，压强与力成正比"],["Pressure is inversely proportional to area when force is constant: smaller area gives higher pressure.","力不变时，压强与面积成反比：面积越小，压强越大"],["The force is usually the weight of the object: \\(F = mg\\), with \\(g = 10\\ \\text{N kg}^{-1}\\) (or \\(\\text{m s}^{-2}\\)).","力通常是重力：F = mg，g = 10"],["Convert cm² to m² first: \\(1\\ \\text{m}^2 = 10\\,000\\ \\text{cm}^2\\).","先换算：1 m² = 10 000 cm²"]],"华文：计算前先把面积换成平方米。","Tip: state 'the smaller the area, the higher the pressure' when explaining sharp tools."],["Worked Example: Pressure of a Solid","例题：固体压强",[["Q: A box of mass 60 kg rests on a floor. The area in contact is 0.30 \\(\\text{m}^2\\). Calculate the pressure on the floor. \\(g = 10\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}\\). [4]","题：质量 60 kg 的箱子，接触面积 0.30 m²，求对地面压强"],["Step 1: \\(F = mg = 60 \\times 10 = 600\\ \\text{N}\\). (1m)","步骤1：F = 600 N"],["Step 2: \\(P = \\dfrac{F}{A}\\). (1m)","步骤2：写公式"],["Step 3: \\(P = \\dfrac{600}{0.30}\\). (1m)","步骤3：代入"],["Step 4: \\(P = 2000\\ \\text{Pa}\\). (1m)","步骤4：P = 2000 Pa"]],"","Tip: each step earns a mark: force, formula, substitution, answer with unit."],["Changing Area to Change Pressure (F + H)","改变面积以改变压强（F + H）",[["F1 A knife, needle and nail have a sharp edge or point. H: small area of contact gives high pressure, so they cut or pierce easily.","F1 刀、针、钉尖锐。H：接触面积小，压强大，易切割刺入"],["F2 A tractor and a bulldozer have wide tracks. H: large area reduces the pressure on soft ground, so they do not sink.","F2 拖拉机、推土机履带宽。H：面积大，对软地压强小，不下陷"],["F3 Schoolbags have wide straps. H: large area reduces the pressure on the shoulders, so they are more comfortable.","F3 书包带宽。H：面积大，肩膀受压小，更舒适"],["F4 Buildings have wide foundations. H: the large area reduces pressure on the ground so the building does not sink.","F4 建筑物地基宽。H：减小对地面压强，防止下沉"]],"华文：回答一定包含「面积 → 压强」。","Tip: always write 'area' first, then 'pressure', then the result."],["Pressure in Liquids","液体压强",[["Liquid pressure is caused by the weight of the liquid above; it acts on the container walls and on any object in the liquid.","液体压强由上方液体重量产生，作用于容器壁和物体"],["Liquid pressure increases with depth: deeper means more liquid above.","压强随深度增加：越深，上方液体越多"],["Liquid pressure increases with density: a denser liquid has greater weight for the same volume.","压强随密度增加：密度大则同体积更重"],["At the same depth in the same liquid, the pressure is the same in all directions.","同种液体同一深度各方向压强相等"],["Liquid pressure does not depend on the shape of the container, the volume or the surface area of the liquid.","与容器形状、液体体积、液面面积无关"]],"华文：只与深度和密度有关。","Tip: the two factors are depth and density (and g); never write volume or shape."],["Formula for Liquid Pressure","液体压强公式",[["Formula: \\(P = h\\rho g\\), where h is depth (m), \\(\\rho\\) is density of the liquid (\\(\\text{kg m}^{-3}\\)), g is gravitational acceleration (\\(10\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}\\)).","公式：P = hρg；h 深度(m)，ρ 密度(kg m⁻³)，g = 10"],["Pressure is directly proportional to depth h when the liquid is the same.","同种液体，压强与深度成正比"],["Density of water = \\(1000\\ \\text{kg m}^{-3}\\).","水的密度 = 1000 kg m⁻³"],["Depth is measured from the surface of the liquid vertically downwards to the point.","深度：从液面垂直向下量到该点"]],"华文：h 是垂直深度，不是长度。","Tip: write the formula first, then substitute with units, then the answer with Pa."],["Worked Example: Liquid Pressure","例题：液体压强",[["Q: A diver is 5 m below the surface of the sea. The density of sea water is 1030 \\(\\text{kg m}^{-3}\\). Calculate the pressure due to the water. \\(g = 10\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}\\). [3]","题：潜水员在海面下 5 m，海水密度 1030，求水压"],["Step 1: \\(P = h\\rho g\\). (1m)","步骤1：写公式"],["Step 2: \\(P = 5 \\times 1030 \\times 10\\). (1m)","步骤2：代入"],["Step 3: \\(P = 51\\,500\\ \\text{Pa}\\). (1m)","步骤3：P = 51 500 Pa"],["Compare: in fresh water (1000 \\(\\text{kg m}^{-3}\\)) at 5 m, \\(P = 50\\,000\\ \\text{Pa}\\); the sea has a higher pressure because it is denser.","对比：淡水 5 m 为 50 000 Pa；海水密度大，压强更高"]],"","Tip: compare using 'higher than' and give the reason (denser)."],["Applications of Liquid Pressure (F + H)","液体压强的应用（F + H）",[["F1 A dam is thicker at the bottom. H: pressure increases with depth, so the wall must be stronger to withstand the high pressure.","F1 水坝底部较厚。H：压强随深度增加，须承受高压"],["F2 Divers wear special suits and submarines have strong hulls. H: water pressure is very high at great depth and can crush them.","F2 潜水服和潜艇外壳坚固。H：深处水压高，会压坏"],["F3 A water tank is placed at a high position. H: a greater height gives a greater pressure, so water flows out of the tap with high pressure.","F3 水塔建在高处。H：高度大，水压大，水从水龙头流出压力大"],["F4 Water spurts further from a hole at the bottom of a container. H: the pressure is higher at greater depth.","F4 容器底部的孔水喷得最远。H：深度越大压强越大"]],"华文：每个应用的 H 都是「深度 → 压强」。","Tip: link depth to pressure in every answer to get the explanation mark."],["Atmospheric Pressure and Gas Pressure","大气压强与气体压强",[["Atmospheric pressure at sea level is about \\(1.0 \\times 10^{5}\\ \\text{Pa}\\) (about 101 kPa, or 76 cm of mercury).","海平面大气压约 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa（约 76 cm 汞柱）"],["Atmospheric pressure decreases as altitude increases because the air above is less and the air is thinner.","海拔越高，大气压越小：上方空气少且稀薄"],["Gas pressure is caused by the gas molecules colliding with the walls of the container.","气体压强由分子碰撞容器壁产生"],["Barometer: an instrument that measures atmospheric pressure. Manometer: measures the pressure of a gas by comparing it with atmospheric pressure.","气压计测大气压；压强计测气体压强"],["Examples: a drinking straw, a suction cup and a syringe work because atmospheric pressure pushes on the surface.","例：吸管、吸盘、注射器靠大气压起作用"]],"华文：大气压随高度减小，所以高山上耳朵会胀。","Tip: explain with 'the higher the altitude, the lower the atmospheric pressure'."],["Pascal's Principle","帕斯卡原理",[["A fluid (liquid or gas) in a closed container exerts pressure in all directions on the walls.","密闭容器中的流体向各方向对容器壁施压"],["Pascal's principle: pressure applied to an enclosed fluid is transmitted equally throughout the fluid.","帕斯卡原理：施加于密闭流体的压强等值传递"],["A liquid is used in hydraulic systems because it is almost incompressible, so the pressure is transmitted fully.","液压系统用液体：几乎不可压缩，压强可完整传递"],["Gas is compressible, so air in a hydraulic system reduces its efficiency.","气体可压缩，混入空气降低效率"]],"华文：关键词：enclosed、transmitted equally。","Tip: write the keywords 'enclosed fluid' and 'transmitted equally'."],["Hydraulic Systems","液压系统",[["A hydraulic system has a small input piston (area \\(A_1\\)) and a large output piston (area \\(A_2\\)) joined by a liquid.","液压系统：小输入活塞与大输出活塞由液体相连"],["Pressure is the same on both pistons: \\(\\dfrac{F_1}{A_1} = \\dfrac{F_2}{A_2}\\).","两活塞压强相等：F₁/A₁ = F₂/A₂"],["Output force: \\(F_2 = F_1 \\times \\dfrac{A_2}{A_1}\\); the larger the output piston area, the larger the force.","输出力：F₂ = F₁ × A₂/A₁；输出活塞越大，力越大"],["The small piston moves a longer distance than the large piston; no energy is created.","小活塞移动距离更长；并不产生能量"],["Applications: hydraulic jack, car brakes, car lifts, hydraulic press, excavator arm.","应用：千斤顶、刹车、升降机、液压机、挖掘机臂"]],"华文：省力但费距离。","Tip: say the force is multiplied because the same pressure acts on a larger area."],["Worked Example: Hydraulic System","例题：液压系统",[["Q: In a hydraulic jack the small piston has an area of 0.002 \\(\\text{m}^2\\) and the large piston 0.08 \\(\\text{m}^2\\). A force of 50 N is applied to the small piston. Calculate the force on the large piston. [4]","题：小活塞 0.002 m²，大活塞 0.08 m²，小活塞受力 50 N，求大活塞受力"],["Step 1: \\(\\dfrac{F_1}{A_1} = \\dfrac{F_2}{A_2}\\). (1m)","步骤1：写公式"],["Step 2: \\(\\dfrac{50}{0.002} = \\dfrac{F_2}{0.08}\\). (1m)","步骤2：代入"],["Step 3: \\(F_2 = \\dfrac{50 \\times 0.08}{0.002}\\). (1m)","步骤3：变形计算"],["Step 4: \\(F_2 = 2000\\ \\text{N}\\). (1m)","步骤4：F₂ = 2000 N"]],"","Tip: keep the area in the same unit (m^2) for both pistons and write N in the answer."],["Hydraulic Brakes and Jacks (F + H)","液压刹车与千斤顶（F + H）",[["F1 Brake fluid is a liquid. H: a liquid is almost incompressible, so the pressure is transmitted fully to the brake pads.","F1 刹车油是液体。H：几乎不可压缩，压强完整传到刹车片"],["F2 The piston at the brake is larger than the piston at the pedal. H: the same pressure acts on a bigger area, so a large force is produced to stop the car.","F2 刹车处活塞比踏板处大。H：同样压强作用于大面积，产生大力使车停下"],["F3 There must be no air bubbles in the brake fluid. H: air is compressible, so the pressure is not fully transmitted and the brakes become less effective.","F3 刹车油不能有气泡。H：空气可压缩，压强传递不完整，刹车失效"],["F4 A hydraulic jack lifts a heavy car with a small force. H: the small force on the small piston gives a large force on the large piston.","F4 千斤顶用小力举重车。H：小活塞小力，大活塞得到大力"]],"华文：答案：液体不可压缩 + 活塞面积不同。","Tip: mention both 'incompressible' and 'larger piston area' in the explanation."],["Investigation: Depth and Liquid Pressure","探究：深度与液体压强",[["Aim: to study the relationship between depth and the pressure of a liquid. (1m) Problem statement: does the depth of water affect the pressure of the water? (1m)","目的：研究深度与液体压强的关系"],["Hypothesis: the greater the depth of water, the higher the pressure. (1m)","假设：水越深，压强越大"],["Variables: manipulated = depth of water; responding = pressure (height difference of the manometer liquid, or distance the water spurts); fixed = density of liquid, type of container. (3m)","变量：操纵=深度；响应=压强（压强计液面高度差或水喷射距离）；固定=液体密度、容器"],["Apparatus: tall plastic bottle with three holes at different heights (or a manometer and a thistle funnel), water, ruler, tray. (1m)","仪器：高塑料瓶（不同高度三个孔）或压强计、水、尺、托盘"],["Procedure: 1 Fill the bottle with water. 2 Open the three holes at the same time. 3 Measure the horizontal distance of each water jet. (2m)","步骤：装满水，同时打开三个孔，量水平喷射距离"],["Observation: the lowest hole spurts water the furthest. Conclusion: the greater the depth, the higher the pressure; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察：最低孔喷最远。结论：越深压强越大，假设被接受"]],"华文：保持水位，补水保证公平。","Tip: to change density instead, keep depth constant and use liquids of different density (e.g. water and salt water)."],["Investigation: Area and Pressure of a Solid","探究：面积与固体压强",[["Aim: to study the effect of area of contact on pressure. (1m) Hypothesis: the smaller the area of contact, the higher the pressure. (1m)","目的：研究接触面积对压强的影响；假设：面积越小，压强越大"],["Variables: manipulated = area of contact; responding = depth of the dent in the sand or plasticine; fixed = force (weight of the block). (3m)","变量：操纵=接触面积；响应=沙/橡皮泥凹陷深度；固定=力（砖块重量）"],["Apparatus: wooden block, sand tray (or plasticine), ruler. (1m)","仪器：木块、沙盘或橡皮泥、尺"],["Procedure: 1 Put the block on its largest face on the sand and measure the depth of the dent. 2 Repeat with the medium face and the smallest face. (2m)","步骤：木块不同面放在沙上，量凹陷深度"],["Observation: the smallest face makes the deepest dent. Conclusion: the smaller the area, the higher the pressure; the hypothesis is accepted. (2m)","观察：最小面凹陷最深。结论：面积越小压强越大"]],"华文：用同一木块，力才不变。","Tip: say 'the same block is used so that the force (weight) is a fixed variable'."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Pressure","示例题：试卷2 A部分（压强）",[["(a) [1] State the SI unit of pressure. Scheme: pascal / Pa / N m^-2 (1m).","(a)帕斯卡"],["(b) [3] A force of 120 N acts on an area of 0.04 \\(\\text{m}^2\\). Calculate the pressure. Scheme: \\(P = F/A\\) (1m); \\(120 \\div 0.04\\) (1m); \\(3000\\ \\text{Pa}\\) (1m).","(b)求压强：3000 Pa"],["(c) [2] Why is a dam built thicker at the bottom? Scheme: pressure increases with depth (1m); the wall must withstand higher pressure (1m).","(c)水坝底部厚：压强随深度增加；须承受高压"],["(d) [3] Calculate the pressure of water at a depth of 3 m. \\(\\rho = 1000\\ \\text{kg m}^{-3}\\), \\(g = 10\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}\\). Scheme: \\(P = h\\rho g\\) (1m); \\(3 \\times 1000 \\times 10\\) (1m); \\(30\\,000\\ \\text{Pa}\\) (1m).","(d)3 m 水深压强：30 000 Pa"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Hydraulic System (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（液压系统）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [3] State Pascal's principle and explain how a hydraulic jack works. Scheme: pressure applied to an enclosed fluid is transmitted equally (1m); same pressure on a larger piston (1m); produces a larger force (1m).","(a)帕斯卡原理及千斤顶原理"],["(b) [4] A hydraulic jack has pistons of area 0.001 \\(\\text{m}^2\\) and 0.05 \\(\\text{m}^2\\). Calculate the force needed on the small piston to lift a car weighing 10 000 N. Scheme: \\(F_1/A_1 = F_2/A_2\\) (1m); \\(F_1/0.001 = 10\\,000/0.05\\) (1m); \\(F_1 = 10\\,000 \\times 0.001 \\div 0.05\\) (1m); 200 N (1m).","(b)举起 10 000 N 的车需 200 N"],["(c) [KBAT] Mechanics find that the brakes of a car are not working well because of air in the brake fluid. Explain and suggest a solution. Scheme: air is compressible (1m); pressure is not fully transmitted (1m); remove the air by bleeding the brake / refill with brake fluid (1m).","(c)刹车油混入空气：空气可压缩，压强传递不完整；排除空气并补油"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: using area in cm^2 in \\(P = F/A\\) and giving Pa. Correct: convert to m^2 first.","错误：面积用 cm² 却答 Pa。正确：先换成 m²"],["Mistake: saying liquid pressure depends on the volume or shape of the container. Correct: only depth, density and g.","错误：说与体积/形状有关。正确：只与深度、密度、g 有关"],["Mistake: writing 'force' instead of 'pressure' in the explanation of sharp tools. Correct: small area gives high pressure.","错误：把压强写成力。正确：面积小，压强大"],["Mistake: forgetting the unit or writing N for pressure. Correct: pressure is in Pa, force is in N.","错误：漏单位或压强写 N。正确：压强用 Pa，力用 N"],["Mistake: saying a hydraulic system saves energy. Correct: it multiplies the force; the small piston moves a longer distance.","错误：说液压省能量。正确：放大力，小活塞移动更远"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: Write the formula for pressure. J: P = F/A.","问：压强公式？答：P = F/A"],["S: What are the factors that affect liquid pressure? J: Depth and density of the liquid.","问：影响液体压强的因素？答：深度和液体密度"],["S: A force of 200 N acts on an area of 0.5 m^2. What is the pressure? J: 400 Pa.","问：200 N 作用在 0.5 m²，压强？答：400 Pa"],["S: State Pascal's principle. J: Pressure applied to an enclosed fluid is transmitted equally throughout the fluid.","问：帕斯卡原理？答：施加于密闭流体的压强等值传递"],["S: Why must brake fluid have no air bubbles? J: Air is compressible, so pressure is not fully transmitted.","问：刹车油为何不能有气泡？答：空气可压缩，压强传递不完整"],["S: Why does atmospheric pressure decrease at high altitude? J: There is less air above.","问：高海拔大气压为何减小？答：上方空气较少"]],"",""]],"sains|T5-9":[["Key Terms / Definitions","关键术语 / 定义",[["Satellite: an object that orbits a planet. Natural satellite: the Moon. Artificial satellite: made by humans and launched into orbit.","卫星：绕行星运行的物体；天然卫星如月球；人造卫星由人类发射"],["Orbit: the path of a satellite around a planet, held by the gravitational pull of the planet.","轨道：卫星绕行星的路径，由行星引力维持"],["Geostationary orbit: an orbit above the equator in which the satellite has a period of 24 hours, so it stays above the same point on Earth.","地球静止轨道：赤道上空、周期 24 小时，相对地面固定"],["Apogee: the point in the orbit of a satellite farthest from Earth. Perigee: the point nearest to Earth.","远地点：轨道上离地球最远的点；近地点：最近的点"],["Global Positioning System (GPS): a satellite navigation system that determines the position of a receiver on Earth.","全球定位系统：确定接收器在地球上位置的卫星导航系统"],["Space debris: man-made objects in orbit that no longer serve a purpose, such as old satellites and rocket parts.","太空垃圾：轨道上不再有用的人造物体"]],"华文：定义要有关键词：gravitational pull、24 hours、farthest/nearest。","Tip: define apogee and perigee with 'farthest' and 'nearest' to Earth."],["How a Satellite Stays in Orbit","卫星如何保持在轨道上",[["A rocket launches the satellite to the required height and gives it a high horizontal speed.","火箭把卫星送到所需高度并提供很大的水平速度"],["The gravitational pull of Earth acts towards the centre of Earth and keeps the satellite moving in a curved path.","地球引力指向地心，使卫星沿弧线运动"],["The satellite keeps falling towards Earth but moves sideways fast enough to keep missing it, so it stays in orbit.","卫星不断向地球下落，但水平速度够大，所以始终在轨道上"],["A satellite nearer to Earth moves faster than a satellite farther away.","离地球越近，速度越快"],["Artificial satellites use solar panels for electrical energy and small thrusters to adjust their position.","人造卫星用太阳能板供电，用小推进器调整位置"]],"华文：关键：引力 + 水平速度。","Tip: mention both 'gravitational pull' and 'high speed' to explain why a satellite stays in orbit."],["Types of Orbit","轨道类型",[["Low Earth orbit (LEO): about 200 km to 2000 km above Earth; short period; used by the International Space Station and imaging satellites.","低轨：约 200 至 2000 km；周期短；国际空间站、成像卫星"],["Medium Earth orbit (MEO): about 20 000 km; used by navigation satellites such as GPS.","中轨：约 20 000 km；GPS 等导航卫星"],["Geostationary orbit (GEO): about 36 000 km above the equator; period 24 hours; used by communication and weather satellites.","地球静止轨道：赤道上空约 36 000 km；周期 24 小时；通讯与气象卫星"],["Polar orbit: passes over or near the North and South Poles; the satellite scans the whole Earth as it rotates; used for mapping and weather observation.","极轨：经过南北极；随地球自转扫描全球；测绘与气象"],["The higher the orbit, the longer the period of the satellite.","轨道越高，周期越长"]],"华文：每种轨道记一个例子与高度。","Tip: link the orbit with its use, e.g. geostationary orbit: communication."],["Geostationary Satellites (F + H)","地球静止卫星（F + H）",[["F1 A geostationary satellite orbits above the equator. H: its orbit lies in the same plane as the equator, so it can stay above one point.","F1 在赤道上空运行。H：轨道平面与赤道相同，能停在一点上方"],["F2 Its period is 24 hours and it moves in the same direction as Earth's rotation. H: it moves at the same rate as Earth, so it seems fixed in the sky.","F2 周期 24 小时，与地球自转同向。H：与地球同步，看似静止"],["F3 It is used for television and telephone communication. H: the ground antenna can point at it without moving.","F3 用于电视与电话通讯。H：地面天线无需转动即可对准"],["F4 It is placed at a very high altitude (about 36 000 km). H: a signal takes longer to travel and it can cover a large part of Earth.","F4 高度约 36 000 km。H：信号传播较久，但覆盖面积大"]],"华文：F 写特征，H 写原因。","Tip: the three keywords are 'above the equator', '24 hours' and 'same direction as Earth rotation'."],["Apogee and Perigee","远地点与近地点",[["Some satellites have an elliptical orbit: the distance between the satellite and Earth is not constant.","有些卫星为椭圆轨道：距离会变化"],["Apogee: the point farthest from Earth. Perigee: the point nearest to Earth.","远地点：最远；近地点：最近"],["The satellite moves fastest at perigee and slowest at apogee.","近地点速度最快，远地点最慢"],["Mark both points on a diagram of an ellipse with Earth at one focus (not at the centre).","作图：椭圆，地球位于一个焦点而非中心"],["A circular orbit has a constant distance and a constant speed.","圆形轨道距离与速度恒定"]],"华文：记 perigee = 近（P 像 proximity），apogee = 远。","Tip: draw an ellipse, label Earth, apogee and perigee."],["Speed at Apogee and Perigee (F + H)","远地点与近地点的速度（F + H）",[["F1 The speed is highest at perigee. H: the gravitational pull of Earth is strongest at the nearest point, so the satellite is pulled and accelerates.","F1 近地点速度最大。H：最近处引力最强，卫星被加速"],["F2 The speed is lowest at apogee. H: the gravitational pull is weakest at the farthest point and the satellite slows down while moving away.","F2 远地点速度最小。H：最远处引力最弱，远离时减速"],["F3 The period of an elliptical orbit is longer when the orbit is larger. H: the satellite has to travel a longer path.","F3 椭圆轨道越大周期越长。H：路径更长"]],"华文：用 faster / slower than 比较。","Tip: use comparison words: faster at perigee than at apogee."],["Uses of Artificial Satellites","人造卫星的用途",[["Communication: television broadcast, telephone and internet (e.g. MEASAT).","通讯：电视广播、电话、网络（如 MEASAT）"],["Weather: observe clouds, storms and typhoons for forecasting.","气象：观测云层、风暴，预报天气"],["Remote sensing: monitor forests, farmland, floods and land use, and map the Earth.","遥感：监测森林、农地、洪水、土地使用，绘制地图"],["Navigation: GPS helps vehicles, ships and aircraft find their position.","导航：GPS 帮助车、船、飞机定位"],["Scientific research: space telescopes study stars and galaxies without disturbance from the atmosphere.","科学研究：太空望远镜不受大气干扰观测天体"]],"华文：每个用途举一个例子。","Tip: give the type of satellite and its use, e.g. 'weather satellite: forecast the weather'."],["Global Positioning System (GPS)","全球定位系统",[["GPS has three parts: satellites in medium Earth orbit, ground control stations and receivers (e.g. mobile phone, car navigation).","GPS 三部分：中轨卫星、地面控制站、接收器"],["Each satellite continuously sends a signal containing its position and the time the signal was sent.","每颗卫星持续发出含位置和发射时间的信号"],["The receiver calculates its distance from each satellite using the time taken by the signal to arrive.","接收器根据信号到达时间计算与各卫星的距离"],["Signals from at least 4 satellites are needed to determine the position and the time accurately.","至少需要 4 颗卫星的信号才能准确定位和校时"],["Applications: navigation, mapping and surveying, tracking vehicles and goods, search and rescue, timing.","应用：导航、测绘、追踪、救援、授时"]],"华文：知道 GPS 如何定位：信号时间 → 距离 → 位置。","Tip: write 'receiver', 'signals from at least 4 satellites' and 'time taken'."],["GPS Coordinates and Navigation","GPS 坐标与导航",[["A position is given by latitude and longitude, in degrees.","位置用纬度和经度表示，单位为度"],["Latitude: angle north or south of the equator (N/S). Longitude: angle east or west of the prime meridian (E/W).","纬度：赤道以北或以南；经度：本初子午线以东或以西"],["Example: Kuala Lumpur is about 3.1° N, 101.7° E.","例：吉隆坡约 3.1°N，101.7°E"],["Use the coordinates to mark a location on a map and to plan a route.","用坐标在地图上标出位置并规划路线"]],"华文：N/S 对应纬度，E/W 对应经度。","Tip: state the direction N/S with latitude and E/W with longitude."],["Space Technology and Spacecraft","太空科技与航天器",[["Launch vehicle (rocket): carries satellites, probes and astronauts into space by thrust from burning fuel.","运载火箭：靠燃料燃烧产生的推力把卫星、探测器和宇航员送入太空"],["Space probe: an unmanned spacecraft sent to study planets, moons and the Sun.","太空探测器：无人航天器，研究行星、卫星和太阳"],["Space station (e.g. International Space Station): a large structure in LEO where astronauts live and do experiments.","空间站（如国际空间站）：位于低轨，宇航员居住并做实验"],["Space telescope: a telescope in orbit that gives clear images because there is no atmosphere to blur the light.","太空望远镜：在轨道上，没有大气干扰，影像清晰"],["Malaysia: Sheikh Muszaphar Shukor became the first Malaysian astronaut (angkasawan) in 2007 and visited the International Space Station.","马来西亚：谢赫·穆萨法于 2007 年成为首位大马宇航员，到访国际空间站"]],"华文：各类航天器记：用途 + 有无人。","Tip: give the name of the spacecraft and its purpose."],["Benefits of Space Technology (F + H)","太空科技的好处（F + H）",[["F1 Communication satellites allow live broadcasts and internet around the world. H: signals are sent through satellites over long distances.","F1 通讯卫星使全球直播和上网成为可能。H：信号经卫星长距离传送"],["F2 Weather satellites improve forecasts. H: people can prepare for storms and floods, and reduce loss of life and property.","F2 气象卫星改善预报。H：可预先防备风暴洪水，减少伤亡损失"],["F3 Remote sensing satellites monitor the environment. H: governments can detect deforestation, plan agriculture and manage disasters.","F3 遥感卫星监测环境。H：可发现砍伐、规划农业、管理灾害"],["F4 Space research leads to new technology used on Earth (spin-offs). H: new materials and devices improve medicine, industry and daily life.","F4 太空研究带来地面新技术。H：新材料和设备改善医疗、工业和生活"],["F5 GPS makes travel safer and faster. H: users know their exact position and the best route.","F5 GPS 使出行更安全快捷。H：知道准确位置和最佳路线"]],"华文：每个好处都要写出结果。","Tip: state the benefit and the result for people."],["Challenges of Space Technology (F + H)","太空科技的挑战（F + H）",[["F1 The cost is very high. H: building, launching and maintaining satellites and rockets needs a large budget that could be used for other needs.","F1 成本极高。H：制造、发射和维护需庞大预算"],["F2 Astronauts face microgravity. H: bones and muscles weaken over a long time in space, so they need exercise and special care.","F2 宇航员面对微重力。H：长期太空生活使骨骼肌肉衰弱，需锻炼和照顾"],["F3 Space has strong radiation and extreme temperatures. H: these can harm astronauts and damage equipment, so special shielding is needed.","F3 太空有强辐射和极端温度。H：伤害宇航员和设备，需要防护"],["F4 Rocket launches can pollute the air. H: burning fuel releases gases and particles into the atmosphere.","F4 火箭发射污染空气。H：燃料燃烧释放气体和微粒"],["F5 Failure of a launch or satellite is a great loss. H: the equipment cannot easily be repaired once in space.","F5 发射或卫星失败损失大。H：进入太空后难以维修"]],"华文：挑战：成本、微重力、辐射、污染、风险。","Tip: give a challenge and a reason (H) for each point."],["Space Debris (F + H)","太空垃圾（F + H）",[["F1 Space debris includes old satellites, rocket stages and fragments. H: they stay in orbit for a long time after they stop working.","F1 包括废弃卫星、火箭残骸和碎片。H：失效后长期留在轨道上"],["F2 Debris is dangerous to working satellites and spacecraft. H: it moves at very high speed, so even a small piece can cause serious damage.","F2 对运行中的卫星和航天器危险。H：速度极高，小碎片也造成严重破坏"],["F3 Debris can collide and produce more debris. H: this increases the risk of further collisions.","F3 碰撞会产生更多碎片。H：增加再碰撞的风险"],["Solutions: design satellites that can return or be moved to a safe orbit after use; track debris; reduce the number of launches.","对策：卫星用后返回或移到安全轨道；追踪碎片；减少发射"]],"华文：写出危害与对策。","Tip: include 'high speed' as the reason why small debris is dangerous."],["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Satellites and GPS","示例题：试卷2 A部分（卫星与 GPS）",[["(a) [1] What is the orbital period of a geostationary satellite? Scheme: 24 hours (1m).","(a)24 小时"],["(b) [2] State two uses of a geostationary satellite. Scheme: communication / television broadcast (1m); weather observation (1m).","(b)通讯、气象"],["(c) [2] Define apogee and perigee. Scheme: apogee is the farthest point from Earth (1m); perigee is the nearest point to Earth (1m).","(c)远地点最远；近地点最近"],["(d) [2] A GPS receiver needs signals from how many satellites to find its position accurately? Why? Scheme: at least 4 (1m); to calculate the distances and correct the time (1m).","(d)至少 4 颗；计算距离并校正时间"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Sample Paper 2 Section B/C: Space Technology (Essay / KBAT)","示例题：试卷2 B/C部分（太空科技）（论述/KBAT）",[["(a) [4] Explain why the speed of a satellite in an elliptical orbit is highest at the perigee. Scheme: perigee is the nearest point to Earth (1m); the gravitational pull is strongest (1m); satellite accelerates (1m); faster than at apogee (1m).","(a)椭圆轨道近地点速度最大的原因"],["(b) [3] State three benefits of artificial satellites. Scheme: communication (1m); weather forecasting (1m); navigation / remote sensing (1m).","(b)人造卫星的三项好处"],["(c) [KBAT] Some people say that the government should reduce the spending on space technology. Evaluate this statement. Scheme: benefit (e.g. satellites help in forecasting floods) (1m); challenge (high cost) (1m); give a justified opinion, for example continue but cooperate with other countries to share the cost (1m).","(c)评价政府应否减少太空科技开支：写好处、挑战、有理由的看法"]],"","Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style; marks are an example."],["Common Mistakes","常见错误",[["Mistake: saying a geostationary satellite does not move. Correct: it moves with the same period as Earth (24 hours) so it stays above the same point.","错误：说静止卫星不动。正确：它与地球同周期，故位置固定"],["Mistake: mixing up apogee and perigee. Correct: apogee = farthest, perigee = nearest.","错误：混淆远近地点。正确：apogee 最远，perigee 最近"],["Mistake: writing that GPS satellites are in geostationary orbit. Correct: GPS satellites are in medium Earth orbit.","错误：GPS 卫星在静止轨道。正确：在中轨"],["Mistake: answering challenges without a reason. Correct: give the challenge and the reason (H), e.g. 'high cost because rockets cannot be reused easily'.","错误：挑战不写原因。正确：写挑战+原因"]],"",""],["Uji Diri","自测：先想答案，再点击对照",[["S: What is the orbital period of a geostationary satellite? J: 24 hours.","问：地球静止卫星的周期？答：24 小时"],["S: What is perigee? J: The point in the orbit nearest to Earth.","问：近地点？答：轨道上离地球最近的点"],["S: Where is the speed of a satellite highest in an elliptical orbit? J: At the perigee.","问：椭圆轨道上何处速度最大？答：近地点"],["S: Give one use of a polar-orbit satellite. J: Mapping (or weather observation).","问：极轨卫星的一项用途？答：测绘（或气象观测）"],["S: What is the minimum number of satellites for GPS to find position and time? J: 4.","问：GPS 定位和校时最少需几颗卫星？答：4 颗"],["S: State one challenge of space exploration. J: High cost (or space debris, radiation, microgravity).","问：太空探索的一项挑战？答：成本高（或太空垃圾、辐射、微重力）"]],"",""]]};
